window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0199", [{"word":"magnetic","ipa_uk":"/mæɡˈnetɪk/","ipa_us":"/mæɡˈnetɪk/","definition_zh":"有磁性的；磁的；靠磁力驱动的；有强烈吸引力的","definition_en":"having the power to attract iron, or relating to magnets, magnetic fields and the force they produce","core_image":"一块黑色矿石隔着白纸把铁屑排成一道道弧线，纸下什么都没有，铁屑却自己排队","scene":"实验室的白纸上，一块黑色矿石压着薄薄一层铁屑，铁屑自己排成弧线，围观的人都屏住了呼吸。A magnetic mineral draws iron filings into curved lines even through a sheet of paper.","sceneCN":"这里 magnetic 指「具有吸引铁、能产生磁场的性质」（第 1 个义项：能够吸引铁并形成磁场）；句意为一块有磁性的矿石隔着白纸也能把铁屑吸成弧线。图中可辨识物件：黑色矿石、白纸、铁屑、放大镜。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"有磁性的；磁的；靠磁力工作的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"有魅力的；有强烈吸引力的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"magnetic field","zh":"磁场"},{"phrase":"magnetic force","zh":"磁力"},{"phrase":"magnetic pole","zh":"磁极"},{"phrase":"magnetic material","zh":"磁性材料"},{"phrase":"magnetic compass","zh":"磁罗盘"},{"phrase":"magnetic personality","zh":"有魅力的个性"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more magnetic"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most magnetic"},{"label":"副词","form":"magnetically"},{"label":"名词（磁性；磁学）","form":"magnetism"},{"label":"名词（磁铁）","form":"magnet"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"magnetism","pos":"n.","zh":"磁性；磁学；吸引力"},{"word":"magnetize","pos":"v.","zh":"使磁化；吸引"},{"word":"magnetization","pos":"n.","zh":"磁化；磁化强度"},{"word":"magnetite","pos":"n.","zh":"磁铁矿"},{"word":"electromagnet","pos":"n.","zh":"电磁铁"},{"word":"magnetically","pos":"adv.","zh":"用磁力地；磁性地"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Attracting iron","titleCN":"能吸铁、能产生磁场","definition":"having the property of attracting iron and producing a magnetic field around itself","definitionCN":"具有吸引铁并在周围产生磁场的性质","example":"A magnetic rod lifted every nail from the bench in one sweep.","exampleCN":"一根有磁性的棒子一扫，就把工作台上的钉子全吸了起来。","why":"The word names the property that first made a certain ore famous: iron moves toward it although nothing visible pulls.","whyCN":"这个词命名的是让某种矿石最早出名的性质：看不见任何东西在拉，铁却朝它移动。"},{"no":"02","title":"Belonging to the study of magnets","titleCN":"与磁学、磁力研究有关的","definition":"relating to magnetism as a subject of scientific study","definitionCN":"与作为科学研究对象的磁学、磁力有关","example":"Her thesis examines the magnetic behaviour of thin films.","exampleCN":"她的论文研究薄膜的磁性行为。","why":"Once the stone became an object of experiment, the adjective shifted from the object to the whole field of inquiry.","whyCN":"当磁石成为实验对象之后，这个形容词就从物件本身转到了整个研究领域。"},{"no":"03","title":"Driven by magnetic force","titleCN":"靠磁力驱动或工作的","definition":"operated or produced by magnetic forces rather than by direct contact","definitionCN":"靠磁力而非直接接触来运转或产生","example":"The magnetic levitation train floats above its guideway.","exampleCN":"磁悬浮列车悬浮在导轨上方。","why":"If a stone can move iron without touching it, that pull can also be harnessed to lift a whole train.","whyCN":"既然磁石不接触就能移动铁，这股拉力自然也就能用来托起整列火车。"},{"no":"04","title":"Of a planet's field","titleCN":"地磁与天体磁场的","definition":"relating to the natural field generated by a planet or a star","definitionCN":"与行星或恒星自然产生的磁场有关","example":"Migrating birds appear to read the magnetic field of the earth.","exampleCN":"迁徙的鸟似乎能读取地球的磁场。","why":"The same invisible influence surrounds the whole planet, so the adjective applies to fields far larger than any stone.","whyCN":"同一种看不见的作用笼罩整个行星，于是这个词也用于比任何磁石都大得多的场。"},{"no":"05","title":"Storing data in magnetized material","titleCN":"用磁性材料记录数据","definition":"using magnetized material to record and keep information","definitionCN":"用被磁化的材料记录并保存信息","example":"The old magnetic tape still holds the studio recordings.","exampleCN":"那卷旧磁带里还存着当年的录音。","why":"A magnet can fix a pattern in iron particles, and a fixed pattern can carry a signal, so magnetism became a way to write memory.","whyCN":"磁体能在铁微粒里固定下一道图案，而固定图案可以承载信号，于是磁性成了写入记忆的手段。"},{"no":"06","title":"Having two opposite poles","titleCN":"分南北极、同极相斥异极相吸","definition":"having north and south poles that attract and repel one another","definitionCN":"具有南北两极，同极相斥、异极相吸","example":"Two magnetic poles of the same kind push each other away.","exampleCN":"两个同类的磁极会把对方推开。","why":"The pull is never single: it always comes in a pair of opposite ends, which is why the adjective also describes polarity.","whyCN":"这种拉力从不单独出现，总是成对的两端，因此这个词也用来描述极性。"},{"no":"07","title":"Charming a room","titleCN":"个性有魅力的","definition":"having a personality that draws people strongly and willingly","definitionCN":"具有让人不由自主被吸引的个性","example":"Her magnetic presence made the whole room quiet.","exampleCN":"她那种有磁性的气场让整个房间安静下来。","why":"The metaphor borrows the stone's invisible pull: nothing is said or forced, yet attention turns toward the person.","whyCN":"这个比喻借用了磁石看不见的拉力：没有言语也没有强迫，注意力却转向那个人。"},{"no":"08","title":"An abstract pull","titleCN":"抽象义：不可抗拒的吸引力","definition":"exerting an attraction so strong that it feels physical","definitionCN":"施加一种强到近乎物理层面的吸引","example":"The magnetic appeal of the old city keeps artists returning.","exampleCN":"老城那种不可抗拒的吸引力让艺术家一再回来。","why":"The abstract sense generalizes the stone: what is attracted is no longer iron but a person, a memory or a whole crowd.","whyCN":"抽象义把磁石一般化：被吸引的不再是铁，而是人、记忆或一整群人。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Magnetic goes back to the Greek name of a stone from Magnesia, through Latin magnes and the later Latin adjective magneticus. Dates are approximate.","cn":"magnetic 经拉丁 magnes 与晚期拉丁形容词 magneticus，上溯希腊语中一种来自马格尼西亚的石头之名。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK MAGNES","en":"Magnētis lithos, 'the stone of Magnesia', named a naturally magnetized iron ore. The place-name explanation is generally accepted, but the origin of the place name itself is not settled.","cn":"magnētis lithos 意为「马格尼西亚的石头」，指一种天然带磁性的铁矿石。以地名解释这一石名一般认为是可行的，但地名本身的来源没有定论。"},{"era":"LATIN MAGNES","en":"Latin borrowed the Greek noun as magnes, genitive magnetis, and later formed the adjective magneticus from the same stem.","cn":"拉丁语借入这个希腊名词，作 magnes，属格 magnetis；后来又用同一词干构成形容词 magneticus。"},{"era":"MIDDLE ENGLISH","en":"English magnet is recorded in the thirteenth century through Old French magnete, and the adjective magnetic follows in the sixteenth.","cn":"英语 magnet 在十三世纪经古法语 magnete 出现，形容词 magnetic 则到十六世纪才跟上。"},{"era":"EARLY SCIENCE","en":"From the sixteenth century magnetic described the invisible influence itself, and magnetic field became standard after Faraday's experiments in the nineteenth century.","cn":"从十六世纪起，magnetic 开始描述那种看不见的作用本身；到十九世纪法拉第的实验之后，magnetic field 成为标准说法。"},{"era":"FIGURATIVE USE","en":"Animal magnetism, the theory Franz Mesmer promoted in the 1770s, supplied the metaphor of a person who draws others like iron to a lodestone.","cn":"梅斯默在十八世纪七十年代推崇的「动物磁力」理论，提供了「人像铁被磁石吸引」这一比喻。"},{"era":"SOURCE UNCERTAIN","en":"Source uncertain (place name and first record): the link to Magnesia is generally accepted, yet the origin of the place name and the exact earliest English citation of magnetic remain unsettled.","cn":"来源不确定（地名与首见记录）：与马格尼西亚的联系一般认为是成立的，但地名的来源以及 magnetic 最早的确切英语书证仍无定论。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words built on the same magnet stem, plus one look-alike from a different root; group two holds words for the pull itself.","cn":"第一组是同出 magnet 词干的词，另加一个形近却异源的词；第二组是表示「吸引力」本身的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"magnet","ipa":"/ˈmæɡnət/","tag":"same stem, noun","definition":"The stone or device itself; magnetic is the adjective made from it.","definitionCN":"磁石或磁体本身；magnetic 是由它构成的形容词。"},{"word":"magnetism","ipa":"/ˈmæɡnətɪzəm/","tag":"same stem, noun","definition":"The property or the science, not the object; the ending -ism marks a state or system.","definitionCN":"指性质或学科，而不是物件；-ism 后缀标记状态或体系。"},{"word":"magnetite","ipa":"/mæɡˈnetʌɪt/","tag":"same stem, mineral","definition":"The black iron ore that can be magnetized; the ending -ite marks a mineral.","definitionCN":"能被磁化的黑色铁矿石；-ite 后缀标记矿物。"},{"word":"magnate","ipa":"/ˈmæɡneɪt/","tag":"look-alike, different root","definition":"A powerful person in business or industry, from Latin magnus 'great'; it shares spelling only, not ancestry.","definitionCN":"商业或工业界的权贵，来自拉丁 magnus「大的」；只同拼写，并不同源。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"attractive","ipa":"/əˈtræktɪv/","tag":"general pull","definition":"Pleasing enough to draw interest, used of looks or offers; it carries no hint of a field.","definitionCN":"足够讨喜而引来兴趣，多用于外貌或条件；不含磁场的意味。"},{"word":"charismatic","ipa":"/ˌkærɪzˈmætɪk/","tag":"leadership pull","definition":"Able to inspire followers through force of personality; narrower than magnetic and mainly about leaders.","definitionCN":"靠人格力量鼓舞追随者；比 magnetic 窄，主要用于领袖。"},{"word":"alluring","ipa":"/əˈljʊərɪŋ/","tag":"tempting","definition":"Attractive in a way that promises pleasure or gain; it suggests enticement rather than natural pull.","definitionCN":"以快乐或利益诱人的；偏「引诱」而非自然吸引。"},{"word":"hypnotic","ipa":"/hɪpˈnɒtɪk/","tag":"spell-like","definition":"So absorbing that attention cannot leave it; stronger and stranger than magnetic.","definitionCN":"吸引人到无法移开注意；比 magnetic 更强也更奇异。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real stem, the real compounds and the real phrases of the magnet family.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的词干、真实的复合词，以及磁石词族里真实存在的搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"The stem is the name of a stone from Magnesia, so magnet came before magnetism and magnetic.","cn":"词干来自马格尼西亚的一种石头之名，因此先有 magnet，才有 magnetism 与 magnetic。"},{"en":"The family runs magnet, magnetism, magnetize, magnetite, electromagnet and magnetometer.","cn":"同族词包括 magnet、magnetism、magnetize、magnetite、electromagnet 与 magnetometer。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the physical sense: magnetic field, magnetic pole, magnetic force, magnetic compass.","cn":"固定搭配标出物理义：磁场、磁极、磁力、磁罗盘。"},{"en":"The same adjective serves the metaphor: a magnetic personality draws people the way a stone draws pins.","cn":"同一个形容词也承担比喻：有魅力的个性吸人，正如磁石吸针。"},{"en":"Electricity and magnetism sit side by side: electromagnet joins electro- to magnet.","cn":"电与磁并肩而立：electromagnet 由 electro- 与 magnet 拼成。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture an invisible hand under the paper: the filings line up though nothing touches them.","cn":"想象纸下有一只无形的手：没有东西碰到铁屑，它们却排好了队。"},{"en":"Picture two ends that cannot be separated: cut the bar in half and each half still has a north and a south.","cn":"想象两个无法分开的端点：把磁条切成两半，每一半仍有南极和北极。"},{"en":"Picture a crowd drifting toward one speaker without being told to move.","cn":"想象一群人没有接到任何指令，却慢慢朝同一个演讲者靠过去。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The magnetic strip on the card was worn, so the machine could not read it.","cn":"卡片上的磁条磨损了，机器读不出来。"},{"en":"Iron is strongly magnetic, while copper barely responds at all.","cn":"铁有很强的磁性，而铜几乎毫无反应。"},{"en":"The campaign gained magnetic force once the young mayor joined it.","cn":"年轻市长加入之后，这场运动有了强大的吸引力。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"magnet（磁石）+ -ic（形容词后缀）——像磁石那样会吸 → 有磁性的；也有吸引力","word":"magnetic"},"root":"希腊语 magnētis lithos（马格尼西亚的石头）→ 拉丁 magnes/magnetis → 拉丁形容词 magneticus → 英语 magnetic；地名来源一般认为是，地名本身来源不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with a stone pulling iron, pass through field, machine and stored data, and end with the pull a person or a place exerts on a crowd.","cn":"八个义项从一块吸铁的石头出发，经过磁场、机器与存储的数据，最后落到一个人或一个地方对人群的吸引力。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a stone moves iron across a sheet of paper without ever touching it.","cn":"核心意象：一块石头隔着纸移动铁，却从不接触它。"},"chain":["ATTRACTS IRON","PAIRS OF POLES","INVISIBLE FIELD","LEVITATED MACHINE","WRITTEN TAPE","PERSONAL PULL"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 06","en":"The stone and its poles: attraction and repulsion are two faces of one property.","cn":"磁石与其两极：吸与斥是同一种性质的两张脸。"},{"senses":"02 · 03","en":"From property to force: what the physicist measures is what the machine harnesses.","cn":"从性质到力：物理学家测量的，正是机器所利用的。"},{"senses":"04","en":"The planet itself as one huge magnet with a field around it.","cn":"行星本身就是一块巨大的磁铁，外面罩着一层场。"},{"senses":"05","en":"The pull fixed into matter as a pattern that can be read back.","cn":"把拉力固定进物质，变成可以读回的图案。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"The same pull felt between people, or toward a place or an idea.","cn":"同样的拉力发生在人与人之间，或指向一个地方、一个念头。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Magnetic is an adjective built on the noun magnet with the Latin suffix -ic, so the whole family reads outward from the stone.","cn":"magnetic 是名词 magnet 加拉丁形容词后缀 -ic 构成，整个词族都可以从磁石向外读。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin magnes, genitive magnetis, came from Greek magnēs; New Latin added magnetismus for the property, and English built the rest on that stem.","cn":"拉丁 magnes（属格 magnetis）来自希腊 magnēs；新拉丁语又加 magnetismus 表示性质，英语其余词都建在这个词干上。"},"items":[{"word":"magnet","structure":"magnet (free noun from Latin magnes)","meaning":"a stone or device that attracts iron","meaningCN":"能吸铁的石头或器件","example":"The magnet held the note to the steel door.","exampleCN":"磁铁把便条吸在钢门上。"},{"word":"magnetic","structure":"magnet + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"of a magnet; able to attract","meaningCN":"磁的；有吸引力的（加形容词后缀，由物件转为性质）","example":"The magnetic field bends the beam.","exampleCN":"磁场使电子束偏转。"},{"word":"magnetism","structure":"magnet + -ism (state or system)","meaning":"the property of magnets; the science of it","meaningCN":"磁性；磁学（加状态后缀，由物件转为性质与学科）","example":"Magnetism puzzled naturalists for centuries.","exampleCN":"磁性感住了博物学家好几个世纪。"},{"word":"magnetize","structure":"magnet + -ize (make, cause)","meaning":"to make something magnetic","meaningCN":"使磁化（加动词后缀，表示使成为）","example":"The current magnetizes the iron core.","exampleCN":"电流使铁芯磁化。"},{"word":"magnetization","structure":"magnetize + -ation (process or result)","meaning":"the process or degree of becoming magnetic","meaningCN":"磁化过程或磁化程度（再加名词后缀，表示过程与结果）","example":"Magnetization reverses as the current alternates.","exampleCN":"电流交变时，磁化方向随之反转。"},{"word":"magnetite","structure":"magnet + -ite (mineral suffix)","meaning":"the black iron ore that magnets occur in","meaningCN":"磁铁矿（加矿物后缀，由性质转到具体矿石）","example":"Magnetite lies in bands along the ridge.","exampleCN":"磁铁矿沿着山脊成带状分布。"},{"word":"electromagnet","structure":"electro- (electric) + magnet","meaning":"a magnet worked by an electric coil","meaningCN":"电磁铁（由「电」与人造磁体复合，动力来源改变）","example":"The electromagnet drops the load when switched off.","exampleCN":"断电时电磁铁把货物放下。"},{"word":"magnetometer","structure":"magnet + -o- + -meter (measuring device)","meaning":"an instrument for measuring magnetic strength","meaningCN":"磁强计（加测量器械后缀，由性质转为量具）","example":"The survey used a magnetometer over the wreck.","exampleCN":"勘测时用磁强计扫过沉船。"},{"word":"nonmagnetic","structure":"non- (not) + magnetic","meaning":"not affected by magnets","meaningCN":"非磁性的（加否定前缀，性质被取消）","example":"The case is made of nonmagnetic steel.","exampleCN":"外壳用的是非磁性钢。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"magnes","structure":"magnes, magnetis (m., third declension)","meaning":"a magnet; the Magnesian stone","meaningCN":"磁石；马格尼西亚石"},{"word":"magneticus","structure":"magneticus, magnetica, magneticum (adjective)","meaning":"of a magnet, magnetic","meaningCN":"磁的；有磁性的"},{"word":"magnetismus","structure":"magnetismus (New Latin noun, seventeenth century)","meaning":"the property of magnets","meaningCN":"磁性"},{"word":"magnesia","structure":"Magnesia (place name, Greek)","meaning":"the region that gave the stone its name","meaningCN":"给这种石头命名的那一地区"}]}},{"word":"magnetism","ipa_uk":"/ˈmæɡnətɪzəm/","ipa_us":"/ˈmæɡnətɪzəm/","definition_zh":"磁性；磁学；磁力作用；吸引力，魅力","definition_en":"the property of attracting iron, the science that studies it, or a strong power to attract people","core_image":"一块磁石周围看不见的场：铁屑一进入范围就自动转向，像被一条条虚线牵着","scene":"讲台上，老师把一块黑石放到铁屑上方，铁屑立刻立起来，像针刺一样指向同一个方向。Magnetism arranges the filings before anyone touches them.","sceneCN":"这里 magnetism 指「物质吸引铁的性质」（第 1 个义项：能吸铁并形成磁场）；句意为磁性在没人碰的情况下就把铁屑排好了方向。图中可辨识物件：黑石、铁屑、讲台、投影幕。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"磁性；磁力；磁学"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"吸引力；魅力（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"animal magnetism","zh":"动物磁力；个人魅力"},{"phrase":"earth's magnetism","zh":"地磁"},{"phrase":"the study of magnetism","zh":"磁学研究"},{"phrase":"residual magnetism","zh":"剩磁"},{"phrase":"magnetism of a place","zh":"一个地方的吸引力"}],"forms":[{"label":"名词（不可数，物理义）","form":"magnetism"},{"label":"名词（复数，罕用，指多种磁现象）","form":"magnetisms"},{"label":"形容词","form":"magnetic"},{"label":"动词","form":"magnetize"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"magnet","pos":"n.","zh":"磁铁；磁石"},{"word":"magnetic","pos":"adj.","zh":"磁的；有吸引力的"},{"word":"magnetize","pos":"v.","zh":"使磁化"},{"word":"magnetite","pos":"n.","zh":"磁铁矿"},{"word":"electromagnetism","pos":"n.","zh":"电磁学；电磁现象"},{"word":"magnetometer","pos":"n.","zh":"磁强计"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The property of attracting iron","titleCN":"磁性：物质吸铁的性质","definition":"the property of a material that attracts iron and produces a field around it","definitionCN":"物质吸引铁并在周围产生磁场的性质","example":"Magnetism makes the compass needle swing toward the north.","exampleCN":"磁性让罗盘指针转向北方。","why":"The word names what the stone does, separated from the stone itself: a property rather than an object.","whyCN":"这个词命名的是磁石所做的事，并与石头本身分开：它是一种性质，而不是一件东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"The branch of physics","titleCN":"磁学：研究磁现象的学科","definition":"the branch of physics that studies magnets, fields and their effects","definitionCN":"研究磁体、磁场及其效应的物理分支","example":"She taught magnetism to first-year physics students.","exampleCN":"她给物理系一年级学生讲授磁学。","why":"Once the property could be measured, it became a subject with laws, instruments and textbooks.","whyCN":"当这种性质可以被测量，它就成了一门有定律、有仪器、有教科书的学科。"},{"no":"03","title":"Force around a magnet or coil","titleCN":"磁力作用：磁体或线圈施加的力","definition":"the force that a magnet or a current-carrying coil exerts on nearby objects","definitionCN":"磁体或通电线圈对附近物体施加的力","example":"The magnetism of the coil pulled the iron core inward.","exampleCN":"线圈的磁力把铁芯往里吸。","why":"Property seen from the receiving side is force: the same thing that makes iron line up also pushes and pulls it.","whyCN":"从受力的一方看，性质就是力：让铁排队的东西，同时也在推拉它。"},{"no":"04","title":"The link between current and magnet","titleCN":"电磁：电流与磁的相互作用","definition":"the magnetic effect of an electric current and the electric effect of a changing magnet","definitionCN":"电流产生的磁效应，以及变化磁场产生的电效应","example":"The discovery of magnetism around a live wire changed telegraph design.","exampleCN":"带电导线周围存在磁效应这一发现，改变了电报的设计。","why":"A current behaves like a magnet, so the single word covers both sides of the link that later became electromagnetism.","whyCN":"电流的行为就像一块磁铁，因此这同一个词覆盖了后来被称为电磁学那条联系的两端。"},{"no":"05","title":"The earth's pull","titleCN":"地磁：地球与动物的导航依据","definition":"the natural magnetic influence of the earth that compasses and some animals use","definitionCN":"地球天然产生的磁作用，罗盘与部分动物据此导航","example":"Pigeons appear to sense the earth's magnetism on long flights.","exampleCN":"鸽子在长途飞行中似乎能感知地磁。","why":"The planet behaves like one enormous magnet, so the same word names the field that compasses and animals follow.","whyCN":"行星的行为就像一块巨大的磁铁，因此同一个词也指罗盘与动物所依循的那个场。"},{"no":"06","title":"A magnetized state kept in metal","titleCN":"剩磁：留在金属里的磁化状态","definition":"the degree to which a material has been magnetized and still holds a field","definitionCN":"材料被磁化后仍保有磁场的程度","example":"Heating the hammer destroyed the magnetism stored in its head.","exampleCN":"加热锤子毁掉了它头部存着的那点磁性。","why":"A property can be left behind in an object, so magnetism also names a stored condition rather than an active stone.","whyCN":"性质可以残留在物体里，因此 magnetism 也指一种被储存下来的状态，而不是正在起作用的磁石。"},{"no":"07","title":"Personal charm","titleCN":"个人魅力：吸引人的气质","definition":"a strong personal quality that draws other people","definitionCN":"吸引他人的强烈个人气质","example":"Her magnetism filled the small lecture hall.","exampleCN":"她的魅力让那间小讲堂坐得满满当当。","why":"The old theory of animal magnetism treated personal influence as a fluid, and the figurative sense kept the idea of an invisible pull.","whyCN":"旧的「动物磁力」理论把人的影响力当作一种流体，比喻义保留了「看不见的拉力」这一想法。"},{"no":"08","title":"The pull of a place or idea","titleCN":"抽象义：地方或观念的吸引力","definition":"the power of a place, an idea or an activity to draw people toward it","definitionCN":"地方、观念或活动把人吸引过去的力量","example":"The magnetism of the mountain towns keeps climbers coming back.","exampleCN":"这些山间小镇的吸引力让登山者一再回来。","why":"The metaphor extends once more: now the field belongs to a landscape or a calling, not to a person.","whyCN":"比喻再扩大一步：这一次场属于一片风景或一种召唤，而不属于某个人。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Magnetism is a New Latin coinage built on the Greek and Latin name of the Magnesian stone. Dates are approximate.","cn":"magnetism 是建立在该希腊、拉丁石名之上的新拉丁语造词。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK MAGNES","en":"Magnētis lithos named the stone of Magnesia. The place-name origin is generally accepted, though the origin of the place name is not settled.","cn":"magnētis lithos 指「马格尼西亚的石头」。以地名解释这一石名一般认为是可行的，但地名本身的来源没有定论。"},{"era":"LATIN MAGNES","en":"Latin borrowed the noun as magnes, genitive magnetis, and used it for both the ore and the force it showed.","cn":"拉丁语借入该名词作 magnes，属格 magnetis，既指矿石，也指它显现出的那种作用。"},{"era":"NEW LATIN","en":"Seventeenth-century scholars formed magnetismus to name the property itself rather than the stone that carries it.","cn":"十七世纪的学者造出 magnetismus，用来命名这种性质本身，而不是承载它的石头。"},{"era":"ENGLISH","en":"English adopted magnetism in the seventeenth century, first for the physical property and soon for the study of it.","cn":"英语在十七世纪吸收 magnetism，先用指物理性质，很快也指对它的研究。"},{"era":"ANIMAL MAGNETISM","en":"Franz Mesmer's animal magnetism, promoted in the 1770s, treated personal influence as a fluid and gave English the sense of a charming, drawing power.","cn":"梅斯默在十八世纪七十年代推崇的「动物磁力」把人影响力当作流体，为英语留下了「迷人吸引力」这一义。"},{"era":"FIRST RECORD UNCERTAIN","en":"Nineteenth-century physics made magnetism a measurable branch of study. The earliest English citation is dated only approximately, so the first record remains uncertain.","cn":"十九世纪物理学使 magnetism 成为可测量的学科。其最早的英语书证只能给出约略年代，因此首见记录属首见年代不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds relatives of the same magnet stem; group two holds nouns for the pull people feel.","cn":"第一组是同出 magnet 词干的亲属词；第二组是表示人所感受到的吸引力的名词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"magnet","ipa":"/ˈmæɡnət/","tag":"the object","definition":"The thing itself; magnetism is what it has or what it does.","definitionCN":"物件本身；magnetism 是它所拥有或所施行的东西。"},{"word":"magnetic","ipa":"/mæɡˈnetɪk/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"Describes something as magnet-like; magnetism is the noun behind it.","definitionCN":"形容某物像磁石；magnetism 是它背后的名词。"},{"word":"magnetite","ipa":"/mæɡˈnetʌɪt/","tag":"the ore","definition":"A specific black mineral; it is one carrier of magnetism, not the property.","definitionCN":"一种具体的黑色矿物；它是磁性的载体之一，而不是性质本身。"},{"word":"magnate","ipa":"/ˈmæɡneɪt/","tag":"look-alike, different root","definition":"An industrial or business magnate, from Latin magnus 'great'; the resemblance is spelling only.","definitionCN":"工业或商业巨头，来自拉丁 magnus「大的」；相似只在拼写。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"attraction","ipa":"/əˈtrækʃn/","tag":"general pull","definition":"Any force or quality that draws things or people together; wider and plainer than magnetism.","definitionCN":"任何把事物或人拉近的力或性质；比 magnetism 更宽也更平实。"},{"word":"charisma","ipa":"/kəˈrɪzmə/","tag":"personal gift","definition":"A personal gift for inspiring devotion; it names the effect on people, not a physical field.","definitionCN":"鼓舞他人忠诚的个人天赋；指对人的效果，而非物理场。"},{"word":"allure","ipa":"/əˈljʊə/","tag":"tempting draw","definition":"The quality of tempting someone toward something; it carries desire, which magnetism need not.","definitionCN":"诱使人靠近的品质；带欲望色彩，而 magnetism 不一定有。"},{"word":"pull","ipa":"/pʊl/","tag":"plain word","definition":"Everyday word for any drawing force, physical or social; magnetism is its technical and vivid version.","definitionCN":"任何拉力的日常说法，物理或社会皆可；magnetism 是它技术化、形象化的版本。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real stem, the real Latin coinage and the real compounds of the family.","cn":"正常联想使用真实词干、真实的新拉丁造词，以及词族中真实的复合词。"},"normal":[{"en":"The ending -ism turns a thing into a property or a system, so magnet plus -ism is magnetism.","cn":"-ism 把物件变成性质或体系，因此 magnet 加 -ism 就是 magnetism。"},{"en":"The family runs magnet, magnetic, magnetize, magnetization, magnetite and electromagnetism.","cn":"同族词包括 magnet、magnetic、magnetize、magnetization、magnetite 与 electromagnetism。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the physical sense: animal magnetism, earth's magnetism, residual magnetism.","cn":"固定搭配标出物理义：动物磁力、地磁、剩磁。"},{"en":"The same noun serves the metaphor: the magnetism of a city or a singer.","cn":"同一个名词也用于比喻：一座城市或一位歌手的吸引力。"},{"en":"A current makes magnetism and a changing magnet makes current, which is why the pair is called electromagnetism.","cn":"电流产生磁，变化的磁又产生电，因此这一对被称作电磁学。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture iron filings standing up like grass blades when the field arrives.","cn":"想象磁场到来时，铁屑像草叶一样立起来。"},{"en":"Picture a hidden current under a table making every compass on it turn.","cn":"想象桌子底下有股隐藏的电流，让桌上所有罗盘一起偏转。"},{"en":"Picture a room that people enter for ten minutes and then cannot leave.","cn":"想象一间屋子，人进去十分钟后就舍不得离开。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Magnetism was studied long before anyone knew what an electron was.","cn":"人们研究磁性时，还不知道电子是什么。"},{"en":"The magnetism of the old harbour town draws painters every summer.","cn":"这座老港镇的吸引力每年夏天都招来画家。"},{"en":"Iron loses its magnetism when it is heated past a certain point.","cn":"铁被加热到一定程度之后就会失去磁性。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"magnet（磁石）+ -ism（性质、体系）——磁石身上那种性质 → 磁性；研究它的学问 → 磁学","word":"magnetism"},"root":"希腊 magnētis lithos（马格尼西亚石）→ 拉丁 magnes/magnetis → 新拉丁 magnetismus → 英语 magnetism。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move from the property of a stone to the science of it, then to the force, the electric link, the earth's field, a stored state, and finally to the pull of a person or a place.","cn":"八个义项从石头的性质走到研究它的学科，再到力、与电的联系、地磁、残留状态，最后落到人或地方的吸引力。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: an invisible field around a stone that turns iron before anything touches it.","cn":"核心意象：磁石周围有一层看不见的场，在没有任何接触之前就转动了铁。"},"chain":["ATTRACTS IRON","BECOMES A SCIENCE","FORCE IN A COIL","EARTH AS MAGNET","STORED IN METAL","PERSONAL CHARM"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 06","en":"The property and its residue: what a material has, and what it keeps after the source is gone.","cn":"性质与残留：材料拥有的，以及源头消失后仍留住的。"},{"senses":"02","en":"The property made measurable, with laws and instruments of its own.","cn":"性质变得可测量，有了自己的定律与仪器。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"Force around a coil, and the two-way link between current and magnet.","cn":"线圈周围的力，以及电流与磁之间的双向联系。"},{"senses":"05","en":"The whole planet as one field that birds and compasses read.","cn":"整个行星成为一个场，鸟与罗盘都在读它。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"The field detached from metal and felt as charm or as the pull of a place.","cn":"场脱离金属，被感受为魅力，或一个地方的吸引力。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Magnetism is a noun formed from magnet with -ism, and the ending is the key to reading the family.","cn":"magnetism 是 magnet 加 -ism 构成的名词，这个后缀是读懂整个词族的钥匙。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin magnes and Greek magnēs supply the stem; magnetismus is a New Latin noun, and English added the rest with native suffixes.","cn":"拉丁 magnes 与希腊 magnēs 提供词干；magnetismus 是新拉丁名词，英语其余词则用本族后缀继续构造。"},"items":[{"word":"magnet","structure":"magnet (free noun from Latin magnes)","meaning":"the stone or device that attracts iron","meaningCN":"能吸铁的石头或器件","example":"A magnet sat on the bench.","exampleCN":"工作台上放着一块磁铁。"},{"word":"magnetism","structure":"magnet + -ism (state, system, doctrine)","meaning":"the property of magnets; the science of it","meaningCN":"磁性；磁学（加状态后缀，由物件转为性质与学科）","example":"Magnetism has its own units and laws.","exampleCN":"磁学有自己的单位与定律。"},{"word":"magnetic","structure":"magnet + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"of magnets or of the force","meaningCN":"磁的；磁性的（加形容词后缀，由物件转为属性）","example":"A magnetic field surrounds the coil.","exampleCN":"线圈周围有磁场。"},{"word":"magnetize","structure":"magnet + -ize (make, cause to be)","meaning":"to give magnetic properties to something","meaningCN":"使磁化（加使动后缀，性质被授予另一物体）","example":"The pulse magnetizes the alloy.","exampleCN":"这一脉冲使合金磁化。"},{"word":"magnetization","structure":"magnetize + -ation (process, result)","meaning":"the act or degree of being magnetized","meaningCN":"磁化过程或磁化程度（再加过程后缀）","example":"Magnetization falls as the metal heats.","exampleCN":"金属升温时磁化程度下降。"},{"word":"electromagnetism","structure":"electro- (electric) + magnetism","meaning":"the linked science of electricity and magnetism","meaningCN":"电磁学（由「电」与磁性复合，两个领域合为一门）","example":"Electromagnetism explains both motors and radios.","exampleCN":"电磁学同时解释电动机与无线电。"},{"word":"magnetometer","structure":"magnet + -o- + -meter (measuring device)","meaning":"a device that measures magnetic strength","meaningCN":"磁强计（磁性加测量器械后缀，性质变成可读数）","example":"The magnetometer read a sharp anomaly.","exampleCN":"磁强计读到一个明显的异常。"},{"word":"magnetosphere","structure":"magnet + -o- + -sphere (region)","meaning":"the field region around a planet","meaningCN":"磁层（磁性加球层后缀，场被扩展到行星尺度）","example":"Charged particles gather in the magnetosphere.","exampleCN":"带电粒子聚集在磁层里。"},{"word":"diamagnetism","structure":"dia- (through, apart) + magnetism","meaning":"a weak repulsion shown by some materials","meaningCN":"抗磁性（加「相对、反」前缀，吸引变成微弱排斥）","example":"Water shows a faint diamagnetism.","exampleCN":"水表现出微弱的抗磁性。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"magnes","structure":"magnes, magnetis (m., third declension)","meaning":"a magnet; the Magnesian stone","meaningCN":"磁石；马格尼西亚石"},{"word":"magneticus","structure":"magneticus, magnetica, magneticum (adjective)","meaning":"magnetic, of a magnet","meaningCN":"磁的；有磁性的"},{"word":"magnetismus","structure":"magnetismus (New Latin noun)","meaning":"the property of magnets","meaningCN":"磁性"},{"word":"Magnesia","structure":"Magnesia (Greek place name)","meaning":"the region linked to the stone's name","meaningCN":"与这种石头之名相关的那一地区"}]}},{"word":"magnet","ipa_uk":"/ˈmæɡnət/","ipa_us":"/ˈmæɡnət/","definition_zh":"磁铁；磁石；有吸引力的人或地方","definition_en":"an object that attracts iron and produces a magnetic field, or a person or place that draws others","core_image":"一块黑亮的石头压在铁钉堆上，钉子像树枝一样从它身上长出来","scene":"厨房里，孩子把一张画纸吸在冰箱门上，纸没有掉下来，门上还挂着一串回形针。A small magnet holds the drawing while the fridge door swings open.","sceneCN":"这里 magnet 指「能吸铁的磁体」（第 2 个义项：人造的小块磁铁）；句意为一块小磁铁吸住画纸，冰箱门打开时纸也没掉。图中可辨识物件：冰箱门、画纸、彩色磁贴、回形针。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"磁铁；磁体；磁石"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"有吸引力的人；吸引人群的地方"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a bar magnet","zh":"条形磁铁"},{"phrase":"a horseshoe magnet","zh":"马蹄形磁铁"},{"phrase":"electromagnet","zh":"电磁铁"},{"phrase":"magnet for tourists","zh":"吸引游客的地方"},{"phrase":"magnet for talent","zh":"吸引人才的中心"},{"phrase":"magnet school","zh":"特色择优学校"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"magnet"},{"label":"复数","form":"magnets"},{"label":"形容词","form":"magnetic"},{"label":"名词（磁性）","form":"magnetism"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"magnetic","pos":"adj.","zh":"磁的；有磁性的；有吸引力的"},{"word":"magnetism","pos":"n.","zh":"磁性；磁学"},{"word":"magnetize","pos":"v.","zh":"使磁化"},{"word":"magnetization","pos":"n.","zh":"磁化；磁化强度"},{"word":"magnetite","pos":"n.","zh":"磁铁矿"},{"word":"electromagnet","pos":"n.","zh":"电磁铁"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The natural stone","titleCN":"天然磁石","definition":"a piece of naturally magnetized iron ore that attracts iron","definitionCN":"天然带磁性的铁矿石，能吸铁","example":"The old compass held a sliver of magnet cut from native ore.","exampleCN":"那只旧罗盘里装着一小片从天然矿石上切下来的磁石。","why":"Before manufacture, the word meant the ore itself: a stone found already able to move iron.","whyCN":"在人工制造出现之前，这个词指的就是矿石本身：一块被发现时就已经能移动铁的石头。"},{"no":"02","title":"A shaped piece of magnetized metal","titleCN":"人造磁铁：加工成形的磁体","definition":"a piece of metal or ceramic made so that it attracts iron","definitionCN":"经过加工、能吸铁的金属或陶瓷块","example":"He stuck the note to the fridge with a small magnet.","exampleCN":"他用一块小磁铁把便条贴在冰箱上。","why":"The same power found in ore can be shaped into bars and discs, so the noun widened from a found stone to a made tool.","whyCN":"矿石里的那种力量可以被加工成条块与圆片，于是这个名词从捡到的石头扩大到做出来的工具。"},{"no":"03","title":"A coil with an iron core","titleCN":"电磁铁：靠电流工作的磁体","definition":"a coil of wire with an iron core that acts as a magnet while current flows","definitionCN":"通电时起磁体作用的带铁芯线圈","example":"The crane's magnet releases the scrap metal when the current stops.","exampleCN":"电流一断，吊车的电磁铁就把废金属放开。","why":"Once electricity could make magnetism, a magnet no longer had to be a permanent stone; it could be switched on and off.","whyCN":"当电能够制造磁性，磁体就不必再是永久的石头，而可以被开与关。"},{"no":"04","title":"The two poles of a magnet","titleCN":"磁体的两极","definition":"one of the two ends of a magnet, where the pull is strongest and opposite poles attract","definitionCN":"磁体两端吸力最强之处，异极相吸、同极相斥","example":"Every magnet has a north pole and a south pole, however often it is cut.","exampleCN":"无论把磁铁切多少次，每一块都仍有南极和北极。","why":"The object is not uniform: the pull concentrates at the ends, and that pair of ends is part of what the word names.","whyCN":"物体并不均匀：吸力集中在两端，而这一对端点也是这个词所指内容的一部分。"},{"no":"05","title":"A charming person","titleCN":"有魅力的人","definition":"a person who attracts others strongly, as if by magnetism","definitionCN":"像被磁力吸引那样强烈吸引他人的人","example":"As a speaker she was a magnet, and the hall filled within minutes.","exampleCN":"作为演讲者，她像一块磁石，几分钟就把礼堂填满了。","why":"A stone that draws iron is an easy picture for a person who draws a crowd, so the noun moved from metal to people.","whyCN":"吸铁的石头很容易拿来比喻吸住人群的人，于是这个名词从金属转到了人。"},{"no":"06","title":"A place that draws visitors","titleCN":"吸引游客的地方","definition":"a place that attracts many visitors or residents","definitionCN":"吸引大量游客或居民的地方","example":"The rebuilt pier became a magnet for day trippers.","exampleCN":"重建后的码头成了当日游客的聚集地。","why":"A place pulls people the way the stone pulls iron: no one orders the crowd to come, yet the current of visitors bends toward it.","whyCN":"地方吸人就像磁石吸铁：没有人下令，游客的人流却朝它弯过去。"},{"no":"07","title":"A centre that draws resources","titleCN":"吸引人才与资金的中心","definition":"an institution or district that draws talent, money or investment","definitionCN":"吸引人才、资金或投资的机构或地区","example":"The research park is a magnet for young engineers.","exampleCN":"这座研究园区是年轻工程师的聚集地。","why":"The metaphor turns practical: a place that offers work and equipment draws skilled people and their money as reliably as a field draws iron.","whyCN":"这个比喻转为实用：一个提供工作与设备的地方，吸来技术人才与资金，其可靠程度如同磁场吸铁。"},{"no":"08","title":"Anything that captures attention","titleCN":"抽象义：吸引注意力的事物","definition":"anything that holds attention so firmly that people turn to it","definitionCN":"牢牢抓住注意力、让人转向它的事物","example":"That question acted as a magnet for the whole debate.","exampleCN":"那个问题像磁石一样吸住了整场辩论。","why":"The pull can attach to nothing physical at all: an idea holds attention the way a stone holds filings, and the noun needs no metal.","whyCN":"这种拉力完全可以不附着在任何实物上：一个念头抓住注意，就像石头抓住铁屑，这个名词不再需要金属。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Magnet comes from the Greek name of the stone of Magnesia through Latin and Old French. Dates are approximate.","cn":"magnet 经拉丁语与古法语，上溯希腊语中「马格尼西亚的石头」之名。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK MAGNES","en":"Magnētis lithos, the stone of Magnesia, named a natural iron ore that already attracted iron. The place-name account is generally accepted; the origin of the place name is not settled.","cn":"magnētis lithos 即「马格尼西亚的石头」，指一种本身就能吸铁的天然矿石。以地名解释这一石名一般认为是可行的；地名本身的来源没有定论。"},{"era":"LATIN MAGNES","en":"Latin took the Greek noun as magnes, genitive magnetis, and used it for the ore and for anything that behaved like it.","cn":"拉丁语借入该希腊名词作 magnes，属格 magnetis，既指矿石，也指任何行为像它的东西。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"Old French magnete carried the word into English in the thirteenth century, at first as the name of the mineral.","cn":"古法语 magnete 在十三世纪把这个词带进英语，最初是矿物的名字。"},{"era":"SIXTEENTH-CENTURY SCIENCE","en":"Experimenters began shaping iron into artificial magnets, and the word widened from a found stone to any made object with the same power.","cn":"实验者开始把铁加工成人造磁体，这个词也从「捡到的石头」扩大到任何具有同样力量的制成品。"},{"era":"ELECTROMAGNET","en":"In 1825 William Sturgeon wrapped a coil around an iron core and called it an electromagnet, tying the noun to a switchable device.","cn":"1825 年斯特金把线圈绕在铁芯上，称之为电磁铁，把这个名词与可开关的装置绑在一起。"},{"era":"FIGURATIVE USE","en":"By the nineteenth and twentieth centuries a magnet was also a person or place that draws others, especially visitors, talent or money.","cn":"到十九、二十世纪，magnet 也指吸引他人的人或地方，尤其吸引游客、人才或资金。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words built on the same stem and one look-alike from another root; group two holds things that attract in the same practical way.","cn":"第一组是同出该词干的词，以及一个异源形近词；第二组是在实际用途上同样能吸引东西的事物。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"magnetic","ipa":"/mæɡˈnetɪk/","tag":"same stem, adjective","definition":"Describes what a magnet is or does; the noun names the object.","definitionCN":"形容磁体是什么、能做什么；名词则指物件。"},{"word":"magnetism","ipa":"/ˈmæɡnətɪzəm/","tag":"same stem, property","definition":"The property or the science; a magnet is the thing that has it.","definitionCN":"性质或学科；magnet 是拥有这一性质的东西。"},{"word":"magnetite","ipa":"/mæɡˈnetʌɪt/","tag":"same stem, ore","definition":"The black mineral that magnets are made from and that occurs naturally magnetized.","definitionCN":"可用来制作磁体、也会天然带磁的黑色矿物。"},{"word":"magnate","ipa":"/ˈmæɡneɪt/","tag":"look-alike, different root","definition":"A business magnate, from Latin magnus 'great'; it is not related to the stone at all.","definitionCN":"商业巨头，来自拉丁 magnus「大的」；与磁石毫无同源关系。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"lodestone","ipa":"/ˈləʊdstəʊn/","tag":"the natural ore","definition":"The old name for naturally magnetized magnetite, the original magnet.","definitionCN":"天然带磁的磁铁矿的旧称，也就是最早的磁石。"},{"word":"electromagnet","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrəʊmæɡnət/","tag":"switchable magnet","definition":"A magnet that works only while current flows, so it can be turned off.","definitionCN":"只在通电时起作用的磁体，因此可以关掉。"},{"word":"attraction","ipa":"/əˈtrækʃn/","tag":"general pull","definition":"Any drawing force; a magnet is one physical source of it.","definitionCN":"任何拉力；磁体是它在物理上的一种来源。"},{"word":"draw","ipa":"/drɔː/","tag":"verb-facing word","definition":"The act of pulling a crowd or interest; a magnet is the object that produces the draw.","definitionCN":"吸引人群或兴趣的动作；magnet 是产生这种吸引的物件。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real stone name, the real compounds and the real modern metaphors.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的石名、真实的复合词，以及真实存在的现代比喻。"},"normal":[{"en":"The word is the stone, not the property: magnet names the thing, magnetism names what it has.","cn":"这个词指的是石头而非性质：magnet 指物件，magnetism 指它拥有的东西。"},{"en":"Everyday magnets carry prefixes: electromagnet, nanomagnet, fridge magnet.","cn":"日常磁体常带前缀：电磁铁、纳米磁体、冰箱贴。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases show the figurative sense: a magnet for tourists, a magnet for talent, a magnet school.","cn":"固定搭配显示比喻义：吸引游客的地方、吸引人才的中心、特色择优学校。"},{"en":"The same stone name gives magnetite, the ore, and magnetometer, the measuring device.","cn":"同一个石名还给出 magnetite（矿石）与 magnetometer（测量器械）。"},{"en":"Cut a magnet in half and you do not get one pole; you get two smaller magnets, each with both poles.","cn":"把磁铁切成两半，你不会得到一个单极，而是得到两块更小的磁铁，各有两极。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a stone that grows iron branches when it is laid on a pile of nails.","cn":"想象一块石头放在钉堆上，就长出铁的枝条。"},{"en":"Picture a switch that turns attraction on and off without moving the metal.","cn":"想象一个开关，不动金属就能让吸引力出现或消失。"},{"en":"Picture a town where every road seems to slope gently toward the same square.","cn":"想象一座小镇，每条路都像微微向下倾向同一个广场。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A magnet is useless once it is heated far above its working temperature.","cn":"磁铁被加热到远超工作温度之后就没用了。"},{"en":"The festival has become a magnet for young filmmakers.","cn":"这个影展已经成了年轻电影人的聚集地。"},{"en":"She kept the spare key under a magnet on the steel door.","cn":"她把备用钥匙放在钢门上的磁贴下面。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"马格内特——来自马格尼西亚的石头，能吸铁 → 磁石、磁铁","word":"magnet"},"root":"希腊 magnētis lithos（马格尼西亚石）→ 拉丁 magnes/magnetis → 古法语 magnete → 英语 magnet。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with the native ore and the shaped object, then its poles and its electric version, and end with the person, place and idea that draw others.","cn":"八个义项从天然矿石与成形磁体出发，经过两极与电磁版本，最后落到吸人的人、地方与念头。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a black stone with iron nails growing out of it like branches.","cn":"核心意象：一块黑石头上长出铁钉，像树枝一样。"},"chain":["NATIVE ORE","SHAPED BAR","COIL CORE","TWO POLES","A CHARMING PERSON","A PLACE THAT DRAWS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"Found stone and made object: the same power, first in ore and then in a shaped piece.","cn":"捡来的石头与制成的物件：同一种力量，先在矿石里，后在成形块里。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"A magnet can be switched by current, and every version still has two poles.","cn":"磁体可由电流开关，而无论哪种版本都仍有两极。"},{"senses":"05","en":"The stone's pull applied to a person who holds a room.","cn":"磁石的拉力用在一个人身上，他能稳住一屋子人。"},{"senses":"06 · 07","en":"A place or an institution that pulls visitors, talent and money.","cn":"一个地方或机构，吸来游客、人才与资金。"},{"senses":"08","en":"The pull detached from place and metal, working on attention itself.","cn":"拉力脱离地方与金属，直接作用于注意力。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Magnet is a free noun from Greek through Latin, and all its relatives attach ordinary suffixes to that stem.","cn":"magnet 是经拉丁语来自希腊语的自由名词，所有亲属词都在这同一词干上加普通后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin magnes, genitive magnetis, is the direct source; magnetismus is a New Latin extension, and Greek magnēs stands at the head of the chain.","cn":"拉丁 magnes（属格 magnetis）是直接来源；magnetismus 是新拉丁语的延伸，链条最前端是希腊 magnēs。"},"items":[{"word":"magnet","structure":"magnet (free noun)","meaning":"a body that attracts iron","meaningCN":"能吸铁的物体","example":"The magnet clung to the steel frame.","exampleCN":"磁铁吸在钢架上。"},{"word":"magnetic","structure":"magnet + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"having the power of a magnet","meaningCN":"有磁性的（加形容词后缀，物件转为性质）","example":"The magnetic clamp held the plate.","exampleCN":"磁性夹具固定住板块。"},{"word":"magnetism","structure":"magnet + -ism (state or system)","meaning":"the property of magnets","meaningCN":"磁性（加状态后缀，物件转为性质）","example":"Magnetism faded as the metal cooled.","exampleCN":"金属冷却后磁性减弱。"},{"word":"magnetize","structure":"magnet + -ize (make)","meaning":"to make an object act like a magnet","meaningCN":"使磁化（加使动后缀，性质被赋予别的物件）","example":"A brief pulse magnetizes the needle.","exampleCN":"一次短脉冲就能使指针磁化。"},{"word":"magnetization","structure":"magnetize + -ation (process or result)","meaning":"the process or strength of being magnetized","meaningCN":"磁化过程或磁化强度（再加过程后缀）","example":"The magnetization survived the drop.","exampleCN":"跌落之后磁化状态仍在。"},{"word":"magnetite","structure":"magnet + -ite (mineral name)","meaning":"the black ore that magnets occur in","meaningCN":"磁铁矿（加矿物后缀，由物件转为矿种）","example":"Magnetite grains darken the sand.","exampleCN":"磁铁矿颗粒把沙子染黑。"},{"word":"electromagnet","structure":"electro- (electric) + magnet","meaning":"a magnet driven by a coil","meaningCN":"电磁铁（电加磁体，动力来源变成电流）","example":"The electromagnet lifts the car bodies.","exampleCN":"电磁铁把车身吊起。"},{"word":"fridge magnet","structure":"fridge + magnet (compound)","meaning":"a small decorative magnet for a refrigerator","meaningCN":"冰箱贴（由冰箱与磁体复合，用途收窄到装饰）","example":"She bought a fridge magnet at the museum.","exampleCN":"她在博物馆买了一个冰箱贴。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"magnes","structure":"magnes, magnetis (m., third declension)","meaning":"a magnet; the Magnesian stone","meaningCN":"磁石；马格尼西亚石"},{"word":"magnetismus","structure":"magnetismus (New Latin noun)","meaning":"the property of magnets","meaningCN":"磁性"},{"word":"magneticus","structure":"magneticus, magnetica, magneticum (adjective)","meaning":"magnetic","meaningCN":"磁的"},{"word":"Magnesia","structure":"Magnesia (Greek place name)","meaning":"the region behind the stone's name","meaningCN":"石名背后的那一地区"}]}},{"word":"electricity","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪlekˈtrɪsəti/","ipa_us":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɪsəti/","definition_zh":"电；电力；电荷；电学；强烈的兴奋感","definition_en":"the physical effect of electric charge, the power supplied through wires, or a tense feeling of excitement","core_image":"看不见的电流在铜线里奔跑，一按开关，整间屋子的灯同时亮起","scene":"雷雨夜里，整条街的灯忽然同时熄灭，只有远处的闪电把屋顶照白。When the storm cut the electricity, the whole street went dark at once.","sceneCN":"这里 electricity 指「送入住户与街道的电力供应」（第 4 个义项：供电、用电）；句意为暴风雨切断供电时，整条街同时黑了。图中可辨识物件：闪电、熄灭的路灯、窗户里的烛光、雨幕。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"电；电力；电能（不可数）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"兴奋的情绪张力；强烈的活力（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"generate electricity","zh":"发电"},{"phrase":"electricity supply","zh":"电力供应"},{"phrase":"static electricity","zh":"静电"},{"phrase":"electricity bill","zh":"电费账单"},{"phrase":"cut off the electricity","zh":"切断供电"}],"forms":[{"label":"名词（不可数）","form":"electricity"},{"label":"形容词（电的）","form":"electric"},{"label":"形容词（电气的）","form":"electrical"},{"label":"动词（使带电； electrify）","form":"electrify"},{"label":"名词（电工）","form":"electrician"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"electric","pos":"adj.","zh":"电的；电动的；令人激动的"},{"word":"electrical","pos":"adj.","zh":"电气的；与电有关的"},{"word":"electrician","pos":"n.","zh":"电工"},{"word":"electrify","pos":"v.","zh":"使带电；使震惊"},{"word":"electrification","pos":"n.","zh":"电气化"},{"word":"electronics","pos":"n.","zh":"电子学；电子器件"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The physical phenomenon","titleCN":"电：电荷及其效应这一物理现象","definition":"the physical phenomenon of electric charge, its movement and its effects","definitionCN":"电荷及其运动与效应构成的物理现象","example":"Electricity is easiest to see when it jumps across a gap as a spark.","exampleCN":"电最容易看见的时候，是它作为火花跳过一道缝隙。","why":"The word names an invisible event that becomes visible only at its edge, which is why early students spoke of a fluid.","whyCN":"这个词命名的是看不见的事件，只在边缘才现形，因此早期研究者把它说成一种流体。"},{"no":"02","title":"Power sold as energy","titleCN":"电能、电力：作为能源使用的电","definition":"electric power treated as a form of energy that can be generated and sold","definitionCN":"把电当作可以生产、出售的一种能源","example":"The plant sells electricity to three neighbouring towns.","exampleCN":"这座电厂向邻近的三个镇供电。","why":"Once electricity could be metered and billed, the phenomenon turned into a commodity measured in units.","whyCN":"当电能被计量、收费，这个现象就变成了以单位计价的商品。"},{"no":"03","title":"Charge carried by particles","titleCN":"电荷：粒子所带的电","definition":"the electric charge that particles carry and transfer","definitionCN":"粒子携带与转移的电荷","example":"Rubbing the rod transfers electricity to the cloth.","exampleCN":"摩擦棒子把电荷转移到布上。","why":"The word can point at the quantity itself rather than at the effect, especially when it moves from one body to another.","whyCN":"这个词也可以指向那个量本身，而不是效应，尤其当它从一个物体转到另一个物体时。"},{"no":"04","title":"The supply to a building","titleCN":"供电、用电：送到房屋或街道的电","definition":"the supply of electric power to a building, a street or a region","definitionCN":"向房屋、街道或地区输送的电力","example":"When the storm cut the electricity, the whole street went dark at once.","exampleCN":"暴风雨切断供电时，整条街同时黑了。","why":"In daily speech people say the electricity for the service they buy, not for the physics behind it.","whyCN":"日常口语里，人们用这个词指自己买到的服务，而不是背后的物理原理。"},{"no":"05","title":"Charge that stays put","titleCN":"静电：停留在物体上的电荷","definition":"charge that gathers on an object and stays there until it is discharged","definitionCN":"聚集在物体上、直到被释放才消失的电荷","example":"Walking across the carpet built up enough electricity to make a spark.","exampleCN":"走过地毯积起的静电足以打出一个火花。","why":"A stored charge has no circuit to flow through, so it sits still and surprises the hand that touches it.","whyCN":"被储存的电荷没有回路可走，于是停在原处，吓到伸手去碰的人。"},{"no":"06","title":"The branch of physics","titleCN":"电学：研究电荷的物理分支","definition":"the branch of physics that studies electric charge, current and related effects","definitionCN":"研究电荷、电流及相关效应的物理分支","example":"He studied electricity before switching to acoustics.","exampleCN":"他先学电学，后来转去研究声学。","why":"A phenomenon with laws and instruments turns into a subject taught under its own name.","whyCN":"一个有定律、有仪器的现象，会变成以自己名字授课的学科。"},{"no":"07","title":"Tension in a room","titleCN":"情绪张力：现场紧张而兴奋的气氛","definition":"a tense, exciting feeling that seems to fill a room or a performance","definitionCN":"似乎充满房间或表演现场的紧张兴奋感","example":"The electricity in the hall rose as the band took the stage.","exampleCN":"乐队登台时，礼堂里的紧张感一下子升高了。","why":"The metaphor borrows the spark: something invisible passes between people and makes the air feel charged.","whyCN":"这个比喻借用了火花：某种看不见的东西在人与人之间传递，让空气像带了电。"},{"no":"08","title":"Energy in a place","titleCN":"抽象活力：让地方振作起来的劲头","definition":"a feeling of energy and excitement that spreads through a place or a group","definitionCN":"在一个地方或群体中扩散开来的活力与兴奋","example":"The new plan brought electricity to a tired neighbourhood.","exampleCN":"新方案给一个疲惫的社区带来了生气。","why":"The abstract sense widens the charge from a room to a whole district, where the current is social rather than electrical.","whyCN":"抽象义把电荷从一间屋子扩展到整个街区，那里的电流是社会的，而不是电学的。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Electricity was coined in the seventeenth century on the Greek word for amber, the substance that first showed the effect. Dates are approximate.","cn":"electricity 于十七世纪用希腊语中「琥珀」一词造出，琥珀正是最早显现这一效应的物质。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK ELEKTRON","en":"Greek ēlektron meant amber, and rubbed amber was known to attract light objects such as straw and feathers. The deeper origin of the Greek word is source uncertain.","cn":"希腊语 ēlektron 意为琥珀，人们早已知道摩擦过的琥珀能吸引草屑、羽毛等轻物。这个希腊词更深层的来源属于来源不确定。"},{"era":"LATIN ELECTRUM","en":"Latin borrowed the Greek noun as electrum, which named both amber and a pale gold alloy; English took the same stem through learned Latin.","cn":"拉丁语借入该希腊名词作 electrum，既指琥珀，也指一种淡金色的合金；英语经学术拉丁语继承了同一词干。"},{"era":"NEW LATIN ELECTRICUS","en":"William Gilbert coined electricus around 1600 for substances that behave like rubbed amber, using the Latin stem rather than the Greek one.","cn":"吉尔伯特约在 1600 年造出 electricus，指行为像摩擦琥珀的物质，用的是拉丁词干而非希腊词干。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ELECTRIC","en":"English electric appears in the seventeenth century as the adjective for that attracting power, and electricity follows as its noun.","cn":"英语 electric 在十七世纪出现，用作这种吸引力的形容词，随后 electricity 作为名词跟上。"},{"era":"EARLY RECORDS","en":"Sir Thomas Browne is often credited with the first English use of electricity in the 1640s; the exact date is approximate and the spelling varied.","cn":"人们常把 electricity 最早的英语使用归给托马斯·布朗，时在十七世纪四十年代；确切年代只是约数，拼写也多有变化。"},{"era":"MODERN POWER","en":"Nineteenth-century generators turned electricity into a public supply, and twentieth-century writing extended the word to the excitement felt in a crowd.","cn":"十九世纪的发电机把电变成公共供应，二十世纪的写作又把这个词扩展到人群中的兴奋感。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds relatives and look-alikes of the electric stem; group two holds the physical quantities people mix it up with.","cn":"第一组是同出 electric 词干的亲属词与形近词；第二组是常被与它混淆的物理量。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"electric","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɪk/","tag":"same stem, adjective","definition":"Describes a device or effect that works by electricity; electricity is the noun.","definitionCN":"形容靠电工作的装置或效应；electricity 是对应名词。"},{"word":"electrical","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɪkl/","tag":"same stem, adjective","definition":"The broader adjective for systems and engineering, not for a single working device.","definitionCN":"更广的形容词，用于系统与工程，而非单台工作装置。"},{"word":"electron","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɒn/","tag":"same stem, particle","definition":"The negatively charged particle; electricity is the flow or effect of such particles.","definitionCN":"带负电的粒子；electricity 是这些粒子的流动或效应。"},{"word":"electrician","ipa":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɪʃn/","tag":"same stem, person","definition":"A person who installs and repairs wiring; the ending -ian marks a trade.","definitionCN":"安装与维修线路的人；-ian 后缀标记职业。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"power","ipa":"/ˈpaʊə/","tag":"supply word","definition":"The general word for energy delivered to homes, measured in watts; electricity is one form of it.","definitionCN":"泛指送到住户的能量，以瓦计量；electricity 是其中一种形式。"},{"word":"current","ipa":"/ˈkʌrənt/","tag":"flow word","definition":"The rate at which charge moves through a wire; it is the flow, not the supply.","definitionCN":"电荷在导线中移动的速率；指流动，而非供应。"},{"word":"charge","ipa":"/tʃɑːdʒ/","tag":"quantity word","definition":"The amount of electricity a body carries, measured in coulombs.","definitionCN":"物体所带电的量，以库仑计量。"},{"word":"energy","ipa":"/ˈenədʒi/","tag":"wider quantity","definition":"The capacity to do work in any form; electricity is only one carrier of it.","definitionCN":"任何形式的做功能力；电只是它的一种载体。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real Greek source, the real derivatives and the real phrases of the electricity family.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的希腊语来源、真实的派生词，以及电这个词族里真实的搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"The word began with amber: rubbed amber pulled straw, and the effect was named after the stuff.","cn":"这个词从琥珀开始：摩擦过的琥珀能吸草屑，效应就以这种材料命名。"},{"en":"The family runs electric, electrical, electrician, electrify, electrification and electronics.","cn":"同族词包括 electric、electrical、electrician、electrify、electrification 与 electronics。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the supply sense: generate electricity, electricity supply, electricity bill.","cn":"固定搭配标出供应义：发电、电力供应、电费账单。"},{"en":"The adjective and the noun split the work: electric device, electrical system, electricity supply.","cn":"形容词与名词分工：电动的装置、电气的系统、电力的供应。"},{"en":"Static electricity is charge with nowhere to go, which is why it waits and then shocks.","cn":"静电是无处可去的电荷，因此它先等在那里，然后电你一下。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture water in a pipe: the pressure is voltage, the flow is current, and the water itself is charge.","cn":"想象水管里的水：水压是电压，水流是电流，水本身是电荷。"},{"en":"Picture a spark as the moment the invisible becomes visible.","cn":"想象火花就是看不见的东西现形的那一瞬。"},{"en":"Picture a room where everyone speaks at once and the air itself seems to hum.","cn":"想象一屋子人同时开口，连空气都像在嗡嗡作响。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The village lived without electricity for a week after the line came down.","cn":"线路倒下之后，村子过了一周没有电的日子。"},{"en":"Copper wire carries electricity better than iron does.","cn":"铜线导电比铁好。"},{"en":"There was electricity in the room when the two rivals finally met.","cn":"两个对手终于见面时，屋里充满了紧张的气氛。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"electr-（琥珀）+ -icity（性质、状态）——摩擦琥珀吸起草屑的那种性质 → 电；供电","word":"electricity"},"root":"希腊 ēlektron（琥珀）→ 拉丁 electrum → 新拉丁 electricus（吉尔伯特，约 1600）→ 英语 electric → electricity。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move from an invisible physical event to a commodity, a quantity, a household service, a stored charge, a science, and finally to the excitement in a room and in a district.","cn":"八个义项从看不见的物理事件走到商品、数量、住户服务、储存的电荷、一门学科，最后落到房间与街区里的兴奋感。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: an invisible current running through copper, switching a whole building into light.","cn":"核心意象：一股看不见的电流在铜线里奔跑，把整栋楼点亮。"},"chain":["AMBER SPARK","FLOWING CHARGE","STORED CHARGE","MAINS SUPPLY","BRANCH OF PHYSICS","A ROOM'S EXCITEMENT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 03","en":"The phenomenon and the quantity: what happens, and how much of it a body carries.","cn":"现象与数量：发生了什么，以及物体带了多少。"},{"senses":"02 · 04","en":"The commodity and the household service it becomes once it is metered.","cn":"商品与住户服务：一旦被计量，它就变成这两样东西。"},{"senses":"05","en":"Charge that cannot move, waiting on a surface to surprise the next hand.","cn":"不能移动的电荷，停在表面等着吓到下一只手。"},{"senses":"06","en":"The effects made into a subject with laws, instruments and textbooks.","cn":"把种种效应变成一门有定律、仪器与教科书的学科。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"The spark detached from wires and felt as tension in a room or energy in a district.","cn":"火花脱离导线，被感受为屋里的紧张或街区的生气。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Electricity is a noun on the electric stem with -ity, and the whole family reads from the Greek word for amber.","cn":"electricity 是 electric 词干加 -ity 构成的名词，整个词族都可以从希腊语「琥珀」读起。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Greek ēlektron gave Latin electrum, and New Latin electricus supplied the stem on which English built every derivative.","cn":"希腊 ēlektron 给出拉丁 electrum，新拉丁 electricus 提供词干，英语在其上构造了全部派生词。"},"items":[{"word":"electric","structure":"electr- + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"working by electricity","meaningCN":"电的；电动的（加形容词后缀，材料名转为性质）","example":"An electric pump drained the cellar.","exampleCN":"一台电动泵把地窖的水抽干。"},{"word":"electricity","structure":"electric + -ity (state or quality)","meaning":"the state or effect of electric charge","meaningCN":"电；电力（加性质后缀，形容词转为抽象名词）","example":"Electricity lit the whole valley.","exampleCN":"电力照亮了整个山谷。"},{"word":"electrical","structure":"electric + -al (adjective suffix)","meaning":"relating to electric systems","meaningCN":"电气的；与电有关的（再加形容词后缀，范围由单台设备扩到系统）","example":"The electrical wiring was replaced.","exampleCN":"电气线路已更换。"},{"word":"electrician","structure":"electric + -ian (person of a trade)","meaning":"a person who installs and repairs electric systems","meaningCN":"电工（加人名词后缀，性质转为职业）","example":"An electrician tested the panel.","exampleCN":"一名电工检测了配电盘。"},{"word":"electrify","structure":"electric + -fy (make)","meaning":"to charge with electricity; to shock","meaningCN":"使带电；使震惊（加使动后缀，名词变动词并引申为震惊）","example":"The fence is electrified at night.","exampleCN":"围栏在夜里通电。"},{"word":"electrification","structure":"electrify + -ation (process)","meaning":"the process of bringing electricity to a place","meaningCN":"电气化（再加过程后缀，动作转为大规模工程）","example":"Electrification reached the farms late.","exampleCN":"电气化很晚才到农场。"},{"word":"electronics","structure":"electron + -ics (field of study)","meaning":"the study and use of electronic devices","meaningCN":"电子学；电子器件（由电子加学科后缀，粒子转成技术领域）","example":"Electronics filled the second floor.","exampleCN":"二楼全是电子设备。"},{"word":"electrostatic","structure":"electro- + static (standing)","meaning":"relating to charge at rest","meaningCN":"静电的（由「电」与「静止」复合，流动义被取消）","example":"Electrostatic filters trap fine dust.","exampleCN":"静电滤器捕捉细尘。"},{"word":"hydroelectric","structure":"hydro- (water) + electric","meaning":"generating power from falling water","meaningCN":"水电的（由「水」与「电」复合，动力来源变成水流）","example":"The hydroelectric dam feeds the grid.","exampleCN":"水电站向电网送电。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"electrum","structure":"electrum (n., from Greek ēlektron)","meaning":"amber; a pale gold alloy","meaningCN":"琥珀；一种淡金色合金"},{"word":"electricus","structure":"electricus, electrica, electricum (New Latin adjective, c. 1600)","meaning":"like amber; producing attraction when rubbed","meaningCN":"像琥珀的；摩擦后产生吸引的"},{"word":"ēlektron","structure":"ēlektron (Greek noun)","meaning":"amber","meaningCN":"琥珀"},{"word":"electricitas","structure":"electricitas (New Latin noun)","meaning":"the quality of being electric","meaningCN":"带电的性质"}]}},{"word":"electrical","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈlektrɪkl/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈlektrɪkl/","definition_zh":"电的；电气的；用电的；与电气工程有关的","definition_en":"relating to electricity, to electric systems, or to the engineering that installs and maintains them","core_image":"一面墙后面藏着一整束彩色电线，标签写明每条线通向哪个房间","scene":"装修队打开墙板，里面是一束编号的电线，工程师逐条核对后才允许合闸。The electrical system was mapped before anyone touched the switch.","sceneCN":"这里 electrical 指「与电气系统有关的」（第 3 个义项：电气工程与安装）；句意为合闸之前先把整套电气系统查清。图中可辨识物件：配电箱、彩色电线、标签、绝缘手套。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"电的；电气的；用电的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"与电气工程或电力系统有关的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"electrical engineering","zh":"电气工程"},{"phrase":"electrical system","zh":"电气系统"},{"phrase":"electrical appliance","zh":"电器"},{"phrase":"electrical wiring","zh":"电气布线"},{"phrase":"electrical fault","zh":"电气故障"},{"phrase":"electrical grid","zh":"电网"}],"forms":[{"label":"副词","form":"electrically"},{"label":"名词（电；电力）","form":"electricity"},{"label":"形容词（电动的）","form":"electric"},{"label":"名词（电工）","form":"electrician"},{"label":"名词（电气化）","form":"electrification"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"electricity","pos":"n.","zh":"电；电力"},{"word":"electric","pos":"adj.","zh":"电动的；电的"},{"word":"electrician","pos":"n.","zh":"电工"},{"word":"electrify","pos":"v.","zh":"使带电；电气化"},{"word":"electrification","pos":"n.","zh":"电气化"},{"word":"electrically","pos":"adv.","zh":"用电地；电气上"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Relating to electricity in general","titleCN":"与电有关的（总称）","definition":"relating to electricity as a physical phenomenon","definitionCN":"与作为物理现象的电有关","example":"The report covers the electrical properties of the new film.","exampleCN":"报告论述了这种新薄膜的电学性质。","why":"The suffix -al turns the noun into a broad adjective of relation, so it can describe any property connected with charge.","whyCN":"后缀 -al 把名词变成宽泛的关系形容词，因此凡与电荷相关的性质都能用它描述。"},{"no":"02","title":"Working by electricity","titleCN":"用电工作的、电动的","definition":"using electricity to operate","definitionCN":"靠电来运转","example":"All electrical appliances must be tested before shipping.","exampleCN":"所有电器在出货前都必须检测。","why":"A device that runs on current is described by the adjective because the power source is what matters, not the brand or shape.","whyCN":"靠电流运转的装置用这个形容词描述，因为关键在于动力来源，而不是品牌或外形。"},{"no":"03","title":"Of electrical engineering","titleCN":"与电气工程有关的","definition":"relating to the design, installation and maintenance of electric systems","definitionCN":"与电气系统的设计、安装与维护有关","example":"She took a degree in electrical engineering.","exampleCN":"她拿的是电气工程学位。","why":"This is the professional sense: the adjective names a branch of engineering rather than a single appliance.","whyCN":"这是职业义：形容词命名的是一门工程学科，而不是单台电器。"},{"no":"04","title":"Of the power grid","titleCN":"与发电、输电的电力系统有关的","definition":"relating to the generation, transmission and distribution of electric power","definitionCN":"与电力的生产、输送与分配有关","example":"The storm damaged the electrical grid across the region.","exampleCN":"暴风雨破坏了整个地区的电网。","why":"At grid scale the adjective stops describing one machine and describes the whole wired network that moves power from plant to socket.","whyCN":"到了电网尺度，这个形容词不再描述单台机器，而描述把电力从电厂送到插座的整套线路网络。"},{"no":"05","title":"Of the physics of charge","titleCN":"与电学理论有关的","definition":"relating to the physical theory of charge, current and fields","definitionCN":"与电荷、电流与电场的物理理论有关","example":"The paper offers an electrical model of the nerve fibre.","exampleCN":"这篇论文提出了神经纤维的电学模型。","why":"In scientific writing the adjective marks a model or explanation framed in terms of charge and current.","whyCN":"在科学写作中，这个形容词标记以电荷与电流为框架的模型或解释。"},{"no":"06","title":"Of faults and shock","titleCN":"与电气故障、电击危险有关的","definition":"relating to faults, shocks, overloads and fire risk in electric equipment","definitionCN":"与电气设备的故障、电击、过载与火灾风险有关","example":"A loose wire caused an electrical fire in the basement.","exampleCN":"一根松动的电线在地窖里引发了电气火灾。","why":"Risk belongs to the installation rather than to any single appliance, so the system adjective is the natural label for faults and fires.","whyCN":"风险属于整套安装，而不属于任何单台电器，因此用系统形容词来标记故障与火灾最自然。"},{"no":"07","title":"Carrying signals","titleCN":"承载电信号的","definition":"carrying information as electric pulses or currents","definitionCN":"以电脉冲或电流承载信息","example":"The sensor sends an electrical pulse to the controller.","exampleCN":"传感器向控制器发送一个电脉冲。","why":"A signal is a patterned current, so the same adjective covers wires that carry messages rather than power.","whyCN":"信号是有图案的电流，因此同一个形容词也用于传输信息而非电力的线路。"},{"no":"08","title":"Charged with excitement","titleCN":"比喻：气氛紧张兴奋、像带了电","definition":"so tense or exciting that the atmosphere seems charged","definitionCN":"紧张或兴奋到空气仿佛带了电","example":"The air in the stadium felt electrical before the final whistle.","exampleCN":"终场哨响之前，体育场里的空气像通了电。","why":"The metaphor keeps the spark and drops the wiring: what passes through the crowd is feeling, not current.","whyCN":"这个比喻保留火花，去掉线路：穿过人群的是情绪，而不是电流。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Electrical is the relational adjective of electric, whose stem goes back through Latin to the Greek word for amber. Dates are approximate.","cn":"electrical 是 electric 的关系形容词，其词干经拉丁语上溯希腊语「琥珀」。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK ELEKTRON","en":"Greek ēlektron named amber, the rubbed substance that first showed attraction. The deeper origin of the Greek word is source uncertain.","cn":"希腊 ēlektron 指琥珀，也就是最早显现吸引现象的摩擦材料。这个希腊词更深层的来源属于来源不确定。"},{"era":"NEW LATIN ELECTRICUS","en":"William Gilbert formed electricus around 1600 from the Latin stem for amber, and English borrowed it as electric.","cn":"吉尔伯特约在 1600 年用琥珀的拉丁词干造出 electricus，英语借入作 electric。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ELECTRIC","en":"Electric entered English in the seventeenth century, first describing bodies that attract after rubbing.","cn":"electric 在十七世纪进入英语，最初描述摩擦后产生吸引的物体。"},{"era":"DERIVED ADJECTIVE","en":"Electric plus the relational suffix -al produced electrical, which spread as the adjective for systems rather than single bodies.","cn":"electric 加关系后缀 -al 构成 electrical，逐渐成为描述系统而非单个物体的形容词。"},{"era":"NINETEENTH-CENTURY ENGINEERING","en":"As telegraphs, motors and power stations grew, electrical engineering became a named profession and the adjective its standard label.","cn":"随着电报、电动机与发电站的发展，电气工程成为有名字的职业，这个形容词也就成了它的标准标签。"},{"era":"MODERN APPLIANCE SENSE","en":"Twentieth-century homes filled with electrical appliances, and the adjective extended to faults, wiring and grids.","cn":"二十世纪的家庭充满电器，这个形容词又扩展到故障、布线与电网。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds adjectives and nouns from the same stem; group two holds the near synonyms that divide the same territory.","cn":"第一组是同出该词干的形容词与名词；第二组是划分同一片语义领域的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"electric","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɪk/","tag":"same stem, narrower","definition":"Usually marks the device or the exciting effect: an electric motor, an electric atmosphere.","definitionCN":"多标记装置或激动效果：电动机、带电般的气氛。"},{"word":"electricity","ipa":"/ˌɪlekˈtrɪsəti/","tag":"same stem, noun","definition":"The phenomenon or the supply; the adjective only describes.","definitionCN":"现象或供应本身；形容词只作描述。"},{"word":"electrician","ipa":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɪʃn/","tag":"same stem, person","definition":"A tradesperson who works on wiring; the ending marks a person, not a property.","definitionCN":"从事线路工作的技工；后缀标记人，而非性质。"},{"word":"electronic","ipa":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɒnɪk/","tag":"look-alike, different base","definition":"Built on electron, so it refers to circuits that process signals, not to power supply.","definitionCN":"由 electron 构成，指处理信号的电路，而不是供电。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"electric","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɪk/","tag":"closest partner","definition":"The everyday adjective for a working device; electrical is broader and more technical.","definitionCN":"日常形容正在工作的装置；electrical 更宽、更技术化。"},{"word":"electronic","ipa":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɒnɪk/","tag":"signal, not power","definition":"Describes devices that handle information through transistors and chips, often at low voltage.","definitionCN":"描述用晶体管与芯片处理信息的装置，通常电压很低。"},{"word":"powered","ipa":"/ˈpaʊəd/","tag":"source-neutral","definition":"Says only that a device has a source of power, which may be electric, battery or solar.","definitionCN":"只说明装置有动力来源，可能是电、电池或太阳能。"},{"word":"live","ipa":"/laɪv/","tag":"dangerous state","definition":"Describes a wire or circuit that is currently carrying voltage and can shock.","definitionCN":"描述当前带电、可能电人的导线或电路。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real suffix -al, the real compounds and the real professional phrases.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的后缀 -al、真实的复合词，以及真实的职业说法。"},"normal":[{"en":"The suffix -al makes a relation adjective: electric is the thing, electrical is what belongs to the system.","cn":"后缀 -al 构成关系形容词：electric 指那个东西，electrical 指属于那个系统的。"},{"en":"The family runs electric, electricity, electrician, electrify and electrification.","cn":"同族词包括 electric、electricity、electrician、electrify 与 electrification。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the technical sense: electrical engineering, electrical system, electrical wiring.","cn":"固定搭配标出技术义：电气工程、电气系统、电气布线。"},{"en":"The split is worth remembering: an electric kettle, but the electrical wiring of the kitchen.","cn":"这个区分值得记住：电水壶是 electric，厨房的布线是 electrical。"},{"en":"A fault, a shock and a fire are all described as electrical because they belong to the system, not to one device.","cn":"故障、电击与火灾都用 electrical 描述，因为它们属于整个系统，而不是某一台装置。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture the nervous system of a building: wires as nerves, the panel as the brain.","cn":"想象一栋建筑的神经系统：电线是神经，配电盘是大脑。"},{"en":"Picture a diagram where every line is labelled by the room it feeds.","cn":"想象一张图纸，每条线都标明它供向哪个房间。"},{"en":"Picture a stadium a minute before the whistle, when the crowd itself seems to hum.","cn":"想象终场哨响前一分钟的体育场，人群本身像在嗡嗡作响。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The electrical load doubled after the new wing opened.","cn":"新侧翼启用后，用电负荷翻了一倍。"},{"en":"Keep water away from electrical outlets and bare wires.","cn":"让水和插座、裸线保持距离。"},{"en":"The atmosphere in the studio was almost electrical as the announcement came.","cn":"消息传来时，演播室里的气氛几乎像通了电。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"electric（电的）+ -al（关系形容词后缀）——属于电这一整套系统的 → 电气的","word":"electrical"},"root":"希腊 ēlektron（琥珀）→ 拉丁 electrum → 新拉丁 electricus → 英语 electric → 加 -al 得 electrical。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses run from a broad relation to charge, through devices and engineering, to the grid, theory, faults, signals, and finally to a charged atmosphere.","cn":"八个义项从与电的宽泛关系出发，经装置与工程，到电网、理论、故障、信号，最后落到带电般的气氛。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a bundle of labelled wires hidden behind a wall, each feeding a different room.","cn":"核心意象：墙后藏着一束带标签的电线，每条供向不同的房间。"},"chain":["WIRED DEVICE","ENGINEERED SYSTEM","POWER GRID","THEORY OF CHARGE","FAULT AND SHOCK","SIGNAL AND ATMOSPHERE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"The general relation and the working device: what belongs to electricity, and what runs on it.","cn":"宽泛关系与工作装置：什么属于电，什么靠电运转。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"The engineered system and the public grid it connects to.","cn":"工程系统与它所连接的公共电网。"},{"senses":"05","en":"The theory that explains all of it in terms of charge and current.","cn":"用电荷与电流解释这一切的理论。"},{"senses":"06","en":"The same system seen as risk: faults, shocks, overloads and fire.","cn":"同一个系统被看作风险：故障、电击、过载与火灾。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"Current as a carrier of messages, and as a metaphor for a charged crowd.","cn":"电流作为信息载体，以及作为带电人群的比喻。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Electrical is electric plus the relational suffix -al, and the family keeps that same stem throughout.","cn":"electrical 是 electric 加关系后缀 -al 构成，整个词族都沿用同一词干。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The stem is New Latin electricus, built on Latin electrum from Greek ēlektron 'amber'; -al is a Latin relational suffix.","cn":"词干是新拉丁 electricus，建立在来自希腊 ēlektron「琥珀」的拉丁 electrum 上；-al 是拉丁关系后缀。"},"items":[{"word":"electric","structure":"electr- + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"of or worked by electricity","meaningCN":"电的；电动的（加形容词后缀，材料名转为性质）","example":"An electric drill bored the hole.","exampleCN":"一把电钻打好了孔。"},{"word":"electrical","structure":"electric + -al (relational adjective)","meaning":"belonging to electric systems","meaningCN":"电气的；与电系统有关（加关系后缀，由装置扩到系统）","example":"The electrical plan needs approval.","exampleCN":"电气方案需要审批。"},{"word":"electricity","structure":"electric + -ity (state, quality)","meaning":"the phenomenon and its supply","meaningCN":"电；电力（加性质后缀，形容词转抽象名词）","example":"Electricity reached the village in winter.","exampleCN":"这个村子在冬天通了电。"},{"word":"electrician","structure":"electric + -ian (person of a trade)","meaning":"one who installs and repairs wiring","meaningCN":"电工（加职业人后缀，性质转为从业者）","example":"The electrician rewired the kitchen.","exampleCN":"电工重排了厨房线路。"},{"word":"electrify","structure":"electric + -fy (make, cause)","meaning":"to supply with power; to shock","meaningCN":"使电气化；使震惊（加使动后缀，名词变动词并引申）","example":"The line electrified the branch railway.","exampleCN":"这条线使支线铁路电气化。"},{"word":"electrification","structure":"electrify + -ation (process)","meaning":"the process of powering a place or system","meaningCN":"电气化（再加过程后缀，动作转为工程进程）","example":"Electrification cut coal use in the mills.","exampleCN":"电气化减少了工厂的用煤。"},{"word":"electrically","structure":"electrical + -ly (adverb suffix)","meaning":"by means of electricity","meaningCN":"用电地；在电气上（加副词后缀，性质转方式）","example":"The valve is electrically operated.","exampleCN":"这个阀门是电动操作的。"},{"word":"electrode","structure":"electro- + -ode (path)","meaning":"a conductor through which current enters","meaningCN":"电极（由「电」与「通路」复合，系统转成具体部件）","example":"The electrode corroded after a month.","exampleCN":"电极一个月后就腐蚀了。"},{"word":"electronics","structure":"electron + -ics (field of study)","meaning":"the technology of signal-handling circuits","meaningCN":"电子学；电子器件（由电子加学科后缀，供电义转向信号义）","example":"Electronics replaced the mechanical relays.","exampleCN":"电子器件取代了机械继电器。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"electrum","structure":"electrum (n., from Greek ēlektron)","meaning":"amber; pale gold alloy","meaningCN":"琥珀；淡金色合金"},{"word":"electricus","structure":"electricus, electrica, electricum (New Latin adjective)","meaning":"electric, amber-like","meaningCN":"电的；像琥珀的"},{"word":"ēlektron","structure":"ēlektron (Greek noun)","meaning":"amber","meaningCN":"琥珀"},{"word":"electricitas","structure":"electricitas (New Latin noun)","meaning":"the quality of being electric","meaningCN":"带电的性质"}]}},{"word":"electric","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈlektrɪk/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈlektrɪk/","definition_zh":"电的；电动的；带电的；令人激动的；（乐器）电声的","definition_en":"worked by electricity, carrying electric charge, or so exciting that it feels charged","core_image":"一辆没有排气管的汽车从身边滑过，只听见轮胎压过路面的声音","scene":"清晨的车库里，一辆没有排气管的车静静滑出，仪表盘上的指针轻轻抬起。The electric car left the garage without a sound.","sceneCN":"这里 electric 指「靠电驱动的」（第 1 个义项：电动的、用电运转的）；句意为那辆电动车无声地驶出车库。图中可辨识物件：充电插头、仪表盘、没有排气管的车尾、安静的车库。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"电的；电动的；带电的；电声的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"令人激动的；像触电般的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（口语）电动车；电力供应系统"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"electric car","zh":"电动汽车"},{"phrase":"electric motor","zh":"电动机"},{"phrase":"electric current","zh":"电流"},{"phrase":"electric guitar","zh":"电吉他"},{"phrase":"electric shock","zh":"电击"},{"phrase":"electric atmosphere","zh":"令人激动的气氛"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more electric"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most electric"},{"label":"副词","form":"electrically"},{"label":"名词（电；电力）","form":"electricity"},{"label":"形容词（电气的）","form":"electrical"},{"label":"名词（电工）","form":"electrician"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"electricity","pos":"n.","zh":"电；电力"},{"word":"electrical","pos":"adj.","zh":"电气的；与电有关的"},{"word":"electrician","pos":"n.","zh":"电工"},{"word":"electrify","pos":"v.","zh":"使带电；使震惊"},{"word":"electrification","pos":"n.","zh":"电气化"},{"word":"electronics","pos":"n.","zh":"电子学"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Driven by a motor","titleCN":"电动的、用电驱动的","definition":"driven by an electric motor rather than by fuel","definitionCN":"靠电动机而不是燃料驱动","example":"The city replaced its diesel buses with electric ones.","exampleCN":"这座城市用电动车替换了柴油公交车。","why":"The oldest scientific sense narrows to transport: the adjective marks the power source of a moving machine.","whyCN":"最古老的科学义在交通上收窄：形容词标记一台运动机器的动力来源。"},{"no":"02","title":"Of electric power","titleCN":"电的、与电力有关的","definition":"relating to electric power, current or supply","definitionCN":"与电力、电流或供电有关","example":"The electric current in the wire is measured in amperes.","exampleCN":"导线中的电流以安培计量。","why":"As a general adjective it names the force itself, which is why current, power and motor all take it.","whyCN":"作为一般形容词，它命名的是那股力本身，因此电流、电力与电动机都用它。"},{"no":"03","title":"Carrying charge","titleCN":"带电的","definition":"carrying or producing electric charge","definitionCN":"带有或产生电荷的","example":"An electric charge builds up on the surface of the drum.","exampleCN":"鼓面会积累电荷。","why":"Charge is the quantity behind every electric effect, so the adjective also describes a body that holds it.","whyCN":"电荷是一切电效应背后的量，因此这个形容词也描述带着它的物体。"},{"no":"04","title":"Amplified sound","titleCN":"电声的（乐器）","definition":"using electricity to amplify or shape sound","definitionCN":"用电来放大或塑造声音","example":"He switched from acoustic to electric guitar at seventeen.","exampleCN":"他十七岁时从木吉他换成了电吉他。","why":"Once a pickup and an amplifier stand between player and listener, the instrument is called electric even though the strings are ordinary.","whyCN":"当拾音器与放大器夹在演奏者和听众之间，即使琴弦很普通，乐器也被称作电声的。"},{"no":"05","title":"Of shock and execution","titleCN":"电击的、电刑的","definition":"relating to electric shock or to execution by current","definitionCN":"与电击或用电执行死刑有关","example":"The old prison still has an electric chair in its museum.","exampleCN":"那座旧监狱的博物馆里还摆着一把电椅。","why":"The same force that lights a room can stop a heart, and the adjective follows it into the language of danger.","whyCN":"点亮房间的同一股力量也能让心脏停止，这个形容词就跟着它进入危险的话语。"},{"no":"06","title":"Exciting a crowd","titleCN":"令人激动的、紧张刺激的","definition":"so exciting that the mood feels charged","definitionCN":"激动到气氛仿佛带电","example":"The crowd gave the dancers an electric welcome.","exampleCN":"人群给舞者报以沸腾般的欢迎。","why":"The metaphor is bodily: excitement runs through a crowd like current through wire, and no one can see it.","whyCN":"这个比喻是身体性的：兴奋在人群里流动，像电流过导线，谁也看不见。"},{"no":"07","title":"Of electric light","titleCN":"电灯与照明的","definition":"relating to light produced by electricity","definitionCN":"与用电产生的光有关","example":"Electric light changed the working hours of entire cities.","exampleCN":"电灯改变了整座城市的作息。","why":"Lighting was the first mass use of current, so the adjective became fixed to lamps and signs.","whyCN":"照明是电流最早的大规模用途，因此这个形容词固定搭配到灯与招牌上。"},{"no":"08","title":"A sudden strong effect","titleCN":"比喻：突然而强烈的冲击","definition":"having a sudden, sharp effect like a shock","definitionCN":"具有像电击那样突然而尖锐的效果","example":"News of the merger had an electric effect on the share price.","exampleCN":"合并的消息对股价产生了触电般的冲击。","why":"The abstract sense borrows the shock rather than the light: a single event passes through a system and changes it at once.","whyCN":"抽象义借的是电击而不是灯光：一个事件穿过整个系统，瞬间把它改变。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Electric was coined in New Latin from the Greek word for amber and entered English in the seventeenth century. Dates are approximate.","cn":"electric 是新拉丁语用希腊语「琥珀」一词造出的，十七世纪进入英语。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK ELEKTRON","en":"Greek ēlektron meant amber; rubbed amber was known to attract straw and feathers. The deeper origin of the Greek word is source uncertain.","cn":"希腊 ēlektron 意为琥珀；摩擦过的琥珀能吸草屑与羽毛。这个希腊词更深层的来源属于来源不确定。"},{"era":"LATIN ELECTRUM","en":"Latin borrowed the noun as electrum, which named amber and also a pale gold alloy.","cn":"拉丁语借入该名词作 electrum，既指琥珀，也指一种淡金色合金。"},{"era":"NEW LATIN","en":"William Gilbert formed electricus around 1600 for bodies that attract like rubbed amber, using the Latin stem.","cn":"吉尔伯特约在 1600 年用拉丁词干造出 electricus，指像摩擦琥珀那样产生吸引的物体。"},{"era":"ENGLISH","en":"Electric came into English in the seventeenth century and was soon applied to any substance showing the effect.","cn":"electric 在十七世纪进入英语，很快用于任何显现该效应的物质。"},{"era":"EIGHTEENTH-CENTURY SCIENCE","en":"Battery piles and Leyden jars made the adjective practical, and electric current and electric shock became fixed phrases.","cn":"伏打电堆与莱顿瓶让这个形容词变得实用，电流与电击成了固定搭配。"},{"era":"APPLIED AND FIGURATIVE","en":"Nineteenth-century motors and lamps, then twentieth-century guitars and crowds, kept widening the range of the word.","cn":"十九世纪的电动机与电灯，接着二十世纪的吉他与人群，不断拓宽这个词的范围。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds relatives and one look-alike; group two holds words that split the same adjective territory.","cn":"第一组是同族词与一个形近词；第二组是划分同一形容词领域的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"electrical","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɪkl/","tag":"same stem, broader","definition":"Relates to systems and engineering rather than to one device: electrical wiring, electrical fault.","definitionCN":"指系统与工程，而非单台装置：电气布线、电气故障。"},{"word":"electricity","ipa":"/ˌɪlekˈtrɪsəti/","tag":"same stem, noun","definition":"The phenomenon or supply; electric is the adjective built on it.","definitionCN":"现象或供应本身；electric 是建在其上的形容词。"},{"word":"electrician","ipa":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɪʃn/","tag":"same stem, person","definition":"A tradesperson who works with wiring; it names a person, not a quality.","definitionCN":"与线路打交道的技工；指人而非性质。"},{"word":"electronic","ipa":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɒnɪk/","tag":"look-alike, different base","definition":"Built on electron and used for signal circuits, not for mains power.","definitionCN":"由 electron 构成，用于信号电路，而非市电。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"electrical","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɪkl/","tag":"system word","definition":"The safer choice for wiring, grids and engineering; electric is for the working device.","definitionCN":"布线、电网与工程更宜用它；electric 用于正在工作的装置。"},{"word":"powered","ipa":"/ˈpaʊəd/","tag":"covers any source","definition":"A neutral word: a powered gate may run on electricity, battery or sun.","definitionCN":"中性词：有动力的门可能靠电、电池或太阳能。"},{"word":"live","ipa":"/laɪv/","tag":"dangerous charge","definition":"Carrying voltage now; it describes the risk, not the design.","definitionCN":"当下带电；描述风险，而不是设计。"},{"word":"thrilling","ipa":"/ˈθrɪlɪŋ/","tag":"excitement word","definition":"Plain word for strong excitement; electric adds the sense of something passing through a crowd.","definitionCN":"强烈兴奋的平实说法；electric 多了「传遍人群」的意味。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real amber source, the real compounds and the real split with electrical.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的琥珀来源、真实的复合词，以及它与 electrical 真实的分工。"},"normal":[{"en":"The word came from amber, and amber's trick was attraction by rubbing, so electric first meant amber-like.","cn":"这个词来自琥珀，而琥珀的把戏是摩擦后吸物，因此 electric 最初意为「像琥珀的」。"},{"en":"The family runs electricity, electrical, electrician, electrify and electrification.","cn":"同族词包括 electricity、electrical、electrician、electrify 与 electrification。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the device sense: electric car, electric motor, electric guitar, electric shock.","cn":"固定搭配标出装置义：电动汽车、电动机、电吉他、电击。"},{"en":"Electric goes with the thing, electrical with the system: an electric kettle, the electrical wiring.","cn":"electric 配物件，electrical 配系统：电水壶、电气布线。"},{"en":"The metaphor keeps the shock: an electric performance hits the audience all at once.","cn":"比喻保留了电击感：一场 electric 的演出让观众同时被击中。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a car that leaves no exhaust and no noise, only the sound of tyres.","cn":"想象一辆没有尾气也没有轰鸣的车，只剩轮胎的声音。"},{"en":"Picture a wire that is live and must not be touched.","cn":"想象一根带电的导线，绝不能碰。"},{"en":"Picture a hall where the applause arrives like a single pulse.","cn":"想象一座大厅，掌声像一次脉冲那样同时到达。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Most electric motors convert more than eighty percent of their input into motion.","cn":"大多数电动机把八成以上的输入转成运动。"},{"en":"The band toured with a full electric set and no acoustic numbers.","cn":"乐队巡演全程用电声配置，没有木吉他曲目。"},{"en":"His first electric shock came from an old lamp socket.","cn":"他第一次触电来自一只旧灯座。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"electr-（琥珀）+ -ic（形容词后缀）——像摩擦琥珀那样有吸引力 → 电的；电动的","word":"electric"},"root":"希腊 ēlektron（琥珀）→ 拉丁 electrum → 新拉丁 electricus（吉尔伯特，约 1600）→ 英语 electric。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses start with a motor-driven machine and the power behind it, pass through charge, amplified sound, shock, excitement, lamps, and end with a single sharp effect.","cn":"八个义项从电动机驱动的机器与背后的电力出发，经过电荷、电声、电击、兴奋、电灯，最后落到一次尖锐的冲击。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a car sliding out of a garage with no exhaust and no engine sound.","cn":"核心意象：一辆没有排气管、也没有引擎声的车滑出车库。"},"chain":["AMBER","DRIVEN BY CURRENT","CARRIES CHARGE","SOUND AMPLIFIED","SHOCK","EXCITEMENT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02 · 07","en":"The power source, the force itself, and the first mass use of it in lighting.","cn":"动力来源、那股力本身，以及它最早的大规模用途——照明。"},{"senses":"03","en":"The quantity a body can hold and pass on.","cn":"物体能够持有并传递的那个量。"},{"senses":"04","en":"Current inserted into sound, so the instrument is named for its power.","cn":"电流进入声音，乐器便以它的动力命名。"},{"senses":"05","en":"The same force turned against the body as shock or execution.","cn":"同一股力量反过来作用于身体，成为电击或电刑。"},{"senses":"06 · 08","en":"The shock felt as excitement in a crowd, or as one sharp public event.","cn":"电击被感受为人群中的兴奋，或一次尖锐的公共事件。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Electric is the base adjective of the family, and every other word is built on this stem with a visible suffix.","cn":"electric 是这一词族的基础形容词，其余词都在这个词干上加可见后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"New Latin electricus rests on Latin electrum, borrowed from Greek ēlektron 'amber'; the suffix -ic is the Latin adjectival ending.","cn":"新拉丁 electricus 建立在拉丁 electrum 上，后者借自希腊 ēlektron「琥珀」；-ic 是拉丁形容词词尾。"},"items":[{"word":"electric","structure":"electr- + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"of electricity; worked by it","meaningCN":"电的；电动的（材料名加形容词后缀，转为性质）","example":"An electric saw cut the beam.","exampleCN":"一把电锯切开了横梁。"},{"word":"electricity","structure":"electric + -ity (state, quality)","meaning":"the phenomenon and its supply","meaningCN":"电；电力（加性质后缀，形容词转抽象名词）","example":"Electricity failed during the storm.","exampleCN":"暴风雨中停了电。"},{"word":"electrical","structure":"electric + -al (relational adjective)","meaning":"belonging to electric systems","meaningCN":"电气的（加关系后缀，由单台装置扩到系统）","example":"The electrical room is locked.","exampleCN":"电气间是锁着的。"},{"word":"electrician","structure":"electric + -ian (person of a trade)","meaning":"one who works on electric wiring","meaningCN":"电工（加职业人后缀，性质转从业者）","example":"The electrician arrived at noon.","exampleCN":"电工中午到了。"},{"word":"electrify","structure":"electric + -fy (make)","meaning":"to charge or equip with electricity; to shock","meaningCN":"使带电；使震惊（加使动后缀，名词变动词并引申）","example":"The fence was electrified last year.","exampleCN":"围栏去年通了电。"},{"word":"electrification","structure":"electrify + -ation (process)","meaning":"the process of converting to electric power","meaningCN":"电气化（再加过程后缀，动作转工程进程）","example":"Rural electrification took decades.","exampleCN":"农村电气化花了几十年。"},{"word":"electrode","structure":"electro- + -ode (way, path)","meaning":"a conductor where current enters or leaves","meaningCN":"电极（电加通路，系统转具体部件）","example":"The electrode sparked against the plate.","exampleCN":"电极在板上打出火花。"},{"word":"electronics","structure":"electron + -ics (field of study)","meaning":"the technology of signal circuits","meaningCN":"电子学；电子器件（电子加学科后缀，供电转信号）","example":"Electronics made the device portable.","exampleCN":"电子器件让这个装置变得便携。"},{"word":"piezoelectric","structure":"piezo- (pressure) + electric","meaning":"producing charge when pressed","meaningCN":"压电的（压力加电，动力来源变成机械挤压）","example":"A piezoelectric strip lights the display.","exampleCN":"一条压电带点亮显示屏。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"electrum","structure":"electrum (n., from Greek ēlektron)","meaning":"amber; pale gold alloy","meaningCN":"琥珀；淡金色合金"},{"word":"electricus","structure":"electricus, electrica, electricum (New Latin adjective, c. 1600)","meaning":"electric, like amber","meaningCN":"电的；像琥珀的"},{"word":"ēlektron","structure":"ēlektron (Greek noun)","meaning":"amber","meaningCN":"琥珀"},{"word":"electricitas","structure":"electricitas (New Latin noun)","meaning":"the quality of being electric","meaningCN":"带电的性质"}]}},{"word":"electric current","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈlektrɪk ˈkʌrənt/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈlektrɪk ˈkɜːrənt/","definition_zh":"电流；电流强度；直流电或交流电","definition_en":"the flow of electric charge through a conductor, or the rate at which that charge flows","core_image":"一根铜线里，数不清的看不见的小颗粒排成队，朝同一个方向前进","scene":"实验台上，一根细导线刚接上电池，旁边的磁针立刻偏转，像被线里的什么东西推了一下。The compass needle moved as soon as an electric current reached the coil.","sceneCN":"这里 electric current 指「电荷在导体中的定向流动」（第 1 个义项：电流这一现象）；句意为电流一到达线圈，罗盘指针就偏转。图中可辨识物件：电池、细导线、线圈、磁针。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"电流；电流强度（可数或不可数）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"直流电或交流电（按方向分为两类）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"direct current","zh":"直流电"},{"phrase":"alternating current","zh":"交流电"},{"phrase":"a steady current","zh":"稳定的电流"},{"phrase":"current strength","zh":"电流强度"},{"phrase":"electric current flows","zh":"电流通过"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"electric current"},{"label":"复数","form":"electric currents"},{"label":"形容词（电流的；安培的）","form":"amperic"},{"label":"相关形容词（导电的）","form":"conductive"},{"label":"相关名词（导体）","form":"conductor"},{"label":"相关名词（电流强度，安培数）","form":"amperage"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"current","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"电流；水流；流动的；现行的"},{"word":"currently","pos":"adv.","zh":"目前；当前"},{"word":"currency","pos":"n.","zh":"货币；流通"},{"word":"occur","pos":"v.","zh":"发生；出现"},{"word":"concurrent","pos":"adj.","zh":"同时发生的"},{"word":"excursion","pos":"n.","zh":"远足；偏移"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Charge in directed motion","titleCN":"电流：电荷的定向移动","definition":"the directed movement of electric charge through a conductor","definitionCN":"电荷在导体中沿一定方向移动","example":"An electric current heats the filament until it glows.","exampleCN":"电流把灯丝加热到发光。","why":"The phrase pairs a power source with a running word: charge is not static but travelling, and that travel is the current.","whyCN":"这个短语把电源与一个「奔跑」的词配在一起：电荷不是静止的，而在行进，这种行进就是电流。"},{"no":"02","title":"The measured rate of flow","titleCN":"电流强度：可测量的流量","definition":"the rate of charge flow, measured in amperes","definitionCN":"电荷流动的速率，以安培计量","example":"An electric current of two amperes will trip this small fuse.","exampleCN":"两安培的电流就会烧断这只小保险丝。","why":"Once instruments could count the flow, the phrase came to mean the number as well as the event, just as a river's current can be measured.","whyCN":"当仪器能够计数流量，这个短语就同时指事件与数值，正如河水的流速可以被测量。"},{"no":"03","title":"Direct current","titleCN":"直流电：方向不变","definition":"current that flows in one direction only","definitionCN":"只朝一个方向流动的电流","example":"Batteries send a direct electric current through the torch.","exampleCN":"电池向手电筒提供直流电。","why":"A chemical cell pushes charge one way, so the earliest currents were direct by nature rather than by design.","whyCN":"化学电池把电荷往一个方向推，因此最早的电流天生就是直流的，而非设计出来的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Alternating current","titleCN":"交流电：周期性反向","definition":"current that reverses direction at regular intervals","definitionCN":"按固定周期反复改变方向的电流","example":"The grid delivers alternating electric current to every socket in the building.","exampleCN":"电网向楼里每个插座输送交流电。","why":"Generators spin, and a spinning coil naturally pushes charge first one way and then the other, which made alternating current the practical choice for long-distance supply.","whyCN":"发电机在旋转，旋转的线圈自然先把电荷推向一边、再推向另一边，这使交流电成为远距离供电的实用选择。"},{"no":"05","title":"The current inside a wire","titleCN":"导线中流动的电流","definition":"the current carried by a particular wire or circuit","definitionCN":"特定导线或电路所承载的电流","example":"The electric current in this cable is too weak to start the motor.","exampleCN":"这根电缆里的电流太弱，带不动电动机。","why":"The phrase can point at one local instance of flow, which is what an electrician actually measures and traces.","whyCN":"这个短语也能指某一处具体的流动，也就是电工实际测量与排查的对象。"},{"no":"06","title":"The agreed direction of flow","titleCN":"约定电流方向：正电荷流向","definition":"the conventional direction from positive to negative, fixed before electrons were known","definitionCN":"在电子被发现之前约定的、由正极到负极的方向","example":"Textbooks draw the electric current from the positive terminal to the negative one.","exampleCN":"教科书把电流画成从正极流向负极。","why":"The custom was set before anyone knew that electrons carry a negative charge, so the agreed arrow points opposite to the actual electron drift.","whyCN":"这一约定在人们知道电子带负电之前就已定下，因此约定的箭头与实际电子的漂移方向相反。"},{"no":"07","title":"Current in a living body","titleCN":"生物电：神经与肌肉中的电流","definition":"the small currents that pass through nerves and muscles","definitionCN":"通过神经与肌肉的微弱电流","example":"A tiny electric current carries the signal along the nerve.","exampleCN":"一股极小的电流沿神经传递信号。","why":"The same word was extended to biology once it was clear that nerves move charge rather than a special fluid.","whyCN":"当人们确认神经运送的是电荷而不是某种特殊流体，同一个词就被扩展到生物学。"},{"no":"08","title":"The effects a current produces","titleCN":"电流的效应：热、磁与化学作用","definition":"the heating, magnetic and chemical effects produced by a current","definitionCN":"电流产生的热效应、磁效应与化学效应","example":"The electric current deposits metal on the cathode during plating.","exampleCN":"电镀时电流把金属沉积到阴极上。","why":"A flow of charge is known by what it does: it heats, it bends a compass and it splits compounds, so the phrase also names those effects in context.","whyCN":"电荷的流动靠它所做的事显现：加热、使罗盘偏转、分解化合物，因此这个短语在语境中也指这些效应。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Electric current joins the Greek-derived adjective electric to current, a word from Latin currere 'to run'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"electric current 把源自希腊语的形容词 electric 与来自拉丁 currere「奔跑」的 current 组合起来。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN CURRERE","en":"Latin currere meant 'to run, to flow', and its present participle currens described water or anything else in motion.","cn":"拉丁 currere 意为「跑、流」，其现在分词 currens 描述水或任何处于运动中的东西。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"Old French corant carried the participle into English as current, first for running water and then for any flow.","cn":"古法语 corant 把这个分词带进英语作 current，先用指流动的水，再泛指任何流动。"},{"era":"MIDDLE ENGLISH","en":"By the fourteenth century current was both adjective and noun, naming a stream and anything that runs in time.","cn":"到十四世纪，current 既是形容词也是名词，指水流，也指在时间中奔流的一切。"},{"era":"VOLTAIC PILE","en":"After Volta's pile of 1800, experimenters needed a phrase for moving charge and borrowed the running word, giving electric current.","cn":"1800 年伏打电堆之后，实验者需要说法来指运动的电荷，于是借用了「奔跑」这个词，形成 electric current。"},{"era":"MEASUREMENT","en":"In the 1820s Ampere's work made the flow measurable; the ampere became its unit, formally adopted in 1881.","cn":"十九世纪二十年代安培的工作使流量可测量；安培成为它的单位，1881 年正式采用。"},{"era":"AC, DC AND BIOLOGY","en":"Late nineteenth-century power systems divided current into direct and alternating, and later physiology found currents in nerves and muscles.","cn":"十九世纪末的电力系统把电流分为直流与交流，后来的生理学又在神经与肌肉中发现了电流。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the two halves of the phrase and look-alikes from other roots; group two holds the quantities it is measured or confused with.","cn":"第一组是短语的两个组成部分，以及来自其他词根的形近词；第二组是它常被计量或混淆的量。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"current","ipa":"/ˈkʌrənt/","tag":"head noun","definition":"A flow of water, air or charge; alone it does not say what is flowing.","definitionCN":"水、空气或电荷的流动；单独使用时不说明流的是什么。"},{"word":"electric","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɪk/","tag":"modifier","definition":"Of electricity; the adjective only names the power, not the motion.","definitionCN":"电的；形容词只命名动力，不表运动。"},{"word":"currant","ipa":"/ˈkʌrənt/","tag":"look-alike, different root","definition":"A small dried grape named after Corinth; the spelling matches but the ancestry does not.","definitionCN":"一种以科林斯得名的小葡萄干；拼写相同，来源不同。"},{"word":"occur","ipa":"/əˈkɜː/","tag":"look-alike, same Latin root","definition":"To happen, from ob- plus currere 'run toward'; it shares the root but means an event, not a flow.","definitionCN":"发生，来自 ob- 加 currere「跑向」；词根相同，但指事件而非流动。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"voltage","ipa":"/ˈvəʊltɪdʒ/","tag":"pressure word","definition":"The difference that drives the flow; current is what actually moves.","definitionCN":"推动流动的势差；current 才是真正移动的东西。"},{"word":"charge","ipa":"/tʃɑːdʒ/","tag":"quantity word","definition":"The amount of electricity carried, not its rate of movement.","definitionCN":"所携带的电量，而不是移动速率。"},{"word":"amperage","ipa":"/ˈæmpərɪdʒ/","tag":"unit word","definition":"The strength of a current expressed in amperes.","definitionCN":"以安培表示的电流强度。"},{"word":"power","ipa":"/ˈpaʊə/","tag":"wider quantity","definition":"Energy delivered per second, the product of current and voltage.","definitionCN":"每秒输送的能量，是电流与电压的乘积。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the two real halves, the real unit and the real AC/DC split.","cn":"正常联想使用短语两个真实成分、真实单位，以及真实的交直流分野。"},"normal":[{"en":"Current is a running word: the same root gives occur, excursion and concurrent, all about going.","cn":"current 是一个「奔跑」的词：同一词根还给出 occur、excursion、concurrent，全都与「走」有关。"},{"en":"The phrase is power plus motion: electric says what it is, current says that it moves.","cn":"这个短语是「电」加「运动」：electric 说明是什么，current 说明它在动。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases split the directions: direct current goes one way, alternating current keeps turning round.","cn":"固定搭配分出方向：直流电只走一边，交流电不断掉头。"},{"en":"The unit is the ampere, the instrument is the ammeter, and the quantity is amperage.","cn":"单位是安培，仪器是安培计，所测的量是安培数。"},{"en":"Batteries give direct current; the wall socket gives alternating current.","cn":"电池给直流电，墙上的插座给交流电。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a river: voltage is the height drop, current is how much water passes each second.","cn":"想象一条河：电压是落差，电流是每秒通过的水量。"},{"en":"Picture an arrow drawn on a map that points opposite to the crowd actually walking.","cn":"想象地图上画的箭头，与人群实际行走的方向相反。"},{"en":"Picture a nerve as a wire so thin that the current is almost a whisper.","cn":"想象一根神经像细到极致的导线，里面的电流几乎只是一声耳语。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A current of one ampere carries about six billion billion electrons past a point each second.","cn":"一安培的电流每秒钟约有六十亿亿个电子经过某一点。"},{"en":"The technician measured the current before replacing the fuse.","cn":"技术员在更换保险丝之前先测了电流。"},{"en":"Alternating current made it possible to send power over long distances.","cn":"交流电使远距离输电成为可能。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"electric（电的）+ current（流动之物）——电在导体里流动 → 电流","word":"electric current"},"root":"electric 来自希腊 ēlektron（琥珀）经拉丁 electrum 与新拉丁 electricus；current 来自拉丁 currere（奔跑）的现在分词 currens。两者合为「流动的电」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with charge in motion and its measured rate, split into two directions, narrow to one wire, then widen to the agreed arrow, to living bodies and to the effects a flow produces.","cn":"八个义项从运动的电荷与它的流量开始，分成两个方向，收窄到一根导线，再扩到约定的箭头、活体，以及流动所产生的效应。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: invisible particles queuing inside copper and walking in one direction.","cn":"核心意象：看不见的颗粒在铜里排成队，朝一个方向走。"},"chain":["MOVING CHARGE","RATE MEASURED","TWO DIRECTIONS","THROUGH A WIRE","AGREED ARROW","IN A BODY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 05","en":"The event and one local instance: charge moves, and here is the wire where it moves.","cn":"事件与一处具体实例：电荷在动，而这里是它动的那根线。"},{"senses":"02","en":"The event turned into a number that an instrument can read.","cn":"事件变成仪器能读出的数字。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"Two directions: one fixed by a chemical cell, one produced by a spinning generator.","cn":"两个方向：一个由化学电池固定，一个由旋转的发电机产生。"},{"senses":"06","en":"The arrow agreed on before anyone knew which particles actually move.","cn":"在还不知道究竟是哪种粒子在动之前，人们就约定好的箭头。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"The flow found in nerves, and the heat, magnetism and chemistry it leaves behind.","cn":"在神经中发现的流动，以及它留下的热、磁与化学变化。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase is two analyzable words: electric is an adjective on the amber stem, and current is a Latin participle meaning 'running'.","cn":"这个短语由两个可分析的词组成：electric 是琥珀词干上的形容词，current 是意为「奔跑」的拉丁分词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin currere 'to run' supplies currens and current; Greek ēlektron 'amber' supplies the electric half through Latin electrum and New Latin electricus.","cn":"拉丁 currere「奔跑」提供 currens 与 current；希腊 ēlektron「琥珀」经拉丁 electrum 与新拉丁 electricus 提供 electric 那一半。"},"items":[{"word":"electric","structure":"electr- + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"of electricity","meaningCN":"电的（琥珀词干加形容词后缀）","example":"An electric field drives the flow.","exampleCN":"电场驱动这股流动。"},{"word":"current","structure":"curr- + -ent (present participle)","meaning":"running, flowing; a flow","meaningCN":"流动的；流动（加现在分词后缀，动作转为名词）","example":"The current ran through the coil.","exampleCN":"电流通过线圈。"},{"word":"currently","structure":"current + -ly (adverb suffix)","meaning":"at the present time","meaningCN":"目前；当前（加副词后缀，由「流动」转为「当下」）","example":"The line is currently closed.","exampleCN":"这条线路目前关闭。"},{"word":"currency","structure":"curr- + -ency (state of flowing)","meaning":"money in circulation","meaningCN":"货币；流通（加状态后缀，由流动转为流通物）","example":"The currency lost value quickly.","exampleCN":"这种货币迅速贬值。"},{"word":"occur","structure":"ob- (toward) + currere (run)","meaning":"to happen, to present itself","meaningCN":"发生；出现（「跑向」某人，转为事件发生）","example":"The fault occurs at high load.","exampleCN":"故障在高负荷时发生。"},{"word":"concurrent","structure":"con- (together) + current","meaning":"happening at the same time","meaningCN":"同时发生的（「一起跑」转为时间上并行）","example":"Two concurrent tests were running.","exampleCN":"两项测试同时进行。"},{"word":"excursion","structure":"ex- (out) + currere (run)","meaning":"a short journey out and back","meaningCN":"远足；短途出行（「跑出去」转为往返行程）","example":"The class made a day excursion.","exampleCN":"班级进行了一次一日远足。"},{"word":"amperage","structure":"ampere + -age (quantity)","meaning":"current strength in amperes","meaningCN":"安培数；电流强度（单位名加数量后缀，转成可测的量）","example":"Check the amperage before wiring.","exampleCN":"接线前先确认安培数。"},{"word":"ammeter","structure":"ampere + -meter (measuring device)","meaning":"an instrument for measuring current","meaningCN":"安培计（单位名加测量器械后缀，量转为量具）","example":"The ammeter read almost zero.","exampleCN":"安培计读数几乎为零。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"currere","structure":"currere, curro, cucurri, cursum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to run, to flow","meaningCN":"跑；流动"},{"word":"currens","structure":"currens, currentis (present participle)","meaning":"running, flowing","meaningCN":"奔跑的；流动的"},{"word":"electricus","structure":"electricus, electrica, electricum (New Latin adjective)","meaning":"electric, like amber","meaningCN":"电的；像琥珀的"},{"word":"ēlektron","structure":"ēlektron (Greek noun)","meaning":"amber","meaningCN":"琥珀"}]}},{"word":"voltage","ipa_uk":"/ˈvəʊltɪdʒ/","ipa_us":"/ˈvoʊltɪdʒ/","definition_zh":"电压；电势差；伏特数；（比喻）强度、张力","definition_en":"the difference in electric potential between two points, measured in volts, or a figurative level of intensity","core_image":"水塔架在高处，水管两端的高度差把水压向低处，差越大，冲力越强","scene":"维修工把表笔搭在电池两端，表盘指针跳到刻度十二的位置，他才点头接上线路。The meter showed a steady voltage across the battery terminals.","sceneCN":"这里 voltage 指「两点之间的电势差」（第 1 个义项：电势差）；句意为电表显示电池两端有稳定的电压。图中可辨识物件：万用表、表笔、电池、导线。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"电压；电势差（可数或不可数）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"伏特数；电压等级"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（比喻）强度；张力"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"high voltage","zh":"高电压"},{"phrase":"low voltage","zh":"低电压"},{"phrase":"voltage drop","zh":"电压降"},{"phrase":"supply voltage","zh":"电源电压"},{"phrase":"voltage regulator","zh":"稳压器"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"voltage"},{"label":"复数","form":"voltages"},{"label":"单位名词","form":"volt"},{"label":"测量仪器","form":"voltmeter"},{"label":"形容词（伏特的）","form":"voltaic"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"volt","pos":"n.","zh":"伏特（电压单位）"},{"word":"voltmeter","pos":"n.","zh":"伏特计；电压表"},{"word":"voltaic","pos":"adj.","zh":"伏打式的；由化学作用产生电的"},{"word":"kilovolt","pos":"n.","zh":"千伏"},{"word":"millivolt","pos":"n.","zh":"毫伏"},{"word":"voltage divider","pos":"n.","zh":"分压器"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Difference in potential","titleCN":"电压：两点间的电势差","definition":"the difference in electric potential between two points, which drives charge to move","definitionCN":"两点之间电势的差，正是它推动电荷移动","example":"A voltage appears between the plates as soon as the cell is connected.","exampleCN":"电池一接通，两片极板之间就出现电压。","why":"The word names a difference, not a substance: nothing flows until two points sit at unequal levels.","whyCN":"这个词命名的是一种差，而不是一种物质：只有当两点处于不同水平时，才会有东西流动。"},{"no":"02","title":"The value in volts","titleCN":"电压值：以伏特计的数量","definition":"the size of that difference expressed as a number of volts","definitionCN":"把这一差值用伏特数表示出来","example":"The label says the voltage is twelve volts.","exampleCN":"标签上写着电压是十二伏。","why":"Once a unit existed, the difference could be stated as a number, and the noun took on that reading too.","whyCN":"当单位出现之后，差值就能用数字说出，这个名词也就多了这层读数义。"},{"no":"03","title":"Supply voltage","titleCN":"电源电压、市电电压","definition":"the voltage provided by a supply such as mains or a battery","definitionCN":"由市电或电池等电源提供的电压","example":"The heater is designed for the local supply voltage.","exampleCN":"这台取暖器是按本地市电电压设计的。","why":"Household devices are built around a standard level, so the word often names the supply rather than a measurement.","whyCN":"家用电器围绕一个标准等级设计，因此这个词常指供电本身，而不是一次测量。"},{"no":"04","title":"High and low levels","titleCN":"高压与低压的等级划分","definition":"one of the standard bands, high or low, into which supplies are sorted","definitionCN":"供电按高、低划分的标准等级之一","example":"Only trained staff may enter the high voltage room.","exampleCN":"只有受训人员才能进入高压室。","why":"Safety rules divide the continuous range into bands, and each band gets a plain label built on the word.","whyCN":"安全规则把连续的数值范围划成等级，每一档都得到一个以这个词构成的通俗标签。"},{"no":"05","title":"Loss along a wire","titleCN":"电压降：线路中损失的电压","definition":"the fall in voltage along a wire or component carrying current","definitionCN":"电流通过导线或元件时电压的下降","example":"A long thin cable causes a serious voltage drop.","exampleCN":"又长又细的电缆会造成严重的电压降。","why":"Resistance turns part of the drive into heat, so the difference shrinks as current travels.","whyCN":"电阻把一部分推动力变成热，因此电流前进时那段落差会缩小。"},{"no":"06","title":"A battery's level","titleCN":"电池电压","definition":"the voltage a cell or battery can provide","definitionCN":"电池能够提供的电压","example":"The battery voltage falls slowly as the phone runs.","exampleCN":"手机运行时电池电压缓慢下降。","why":"A chemical cell is the simplest source of a fixed difference, so its level is described with the same noun.","whyCN":"化学电池是最简单的固定势差来源，因此它的水平也用同一个名词描述。"},{"no":"07","title":"A meter reading","titleCN":"电压读数与测量","definition":"the reading a meter gives when it measures potential difference","definitionCN":"仪表测量电势差时给出的读数","example":"He wrote the voltage down before changing the fuse.","exampleCN":"他在换保险丝之前把电压读数记了下来。","why":"Measurement is the practical face of the concept: the needle converts an invisible difference into a number on a dial.","whyCN":"测量是这个概念实用的一面：指针把看不见的差变成表盘上的数字。"},{"no":"08","title":"Intensity of a moment","titleCN":"比喻：情绪的强度、现场的张力","definition":"a figurative level of tension, energy or intensity","definitionCN":"比喻性的紧张、能量或强度水平","example":"The finale raised the voltage of the whole hall.","exampleCN":"终曲把整个大厅的情绪电压抬高了。","why":"The metaphor borrows the pressure of a difference: a performance or a room can be high voltage when the tension is strong.","whyCN":"这个比喻借用了势差的压力：张力很强时，一场演出或一间屋子就可以是「高电压」的。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Voltage is a nineteenth-century formation on the name of Alessandro Volta, whose pile gave science its first steady current. Dates are approximate.","cn":"voltage 是十九世纪在伏打之名上构成的词，他的电堆给了科学第一股稳定电流。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"ALESSANDRO VOLTA","en":"Alessandro Volta, an Italian physicist, built the voltaic pile in 1800 and showed that a chemical stack could produce a steady flow of charge.","cn":"意大利物理学家伏打在 1800 年制成伏打电堆，证明化学堆能产生稳定的电荷流动。"},{"era":"THE VOLT","en":"The unit of potential difference was named the volt in his honour and formally adopted at the International Electrical Congress of 1881.","cn":"电势差的单位以他的名字命名为伏特，并在 1881 年国际电学大会上正式采用。"},{"era":"VOLTAGE","en":"English formed voltage from volt with the suffix -age in the late nineteenth century, following the pattern of amperage and wattage.","cn":"英语在十九世纪晚期用 volt 加后缀 -age 构成 voltage，仿照 amperage 与 wattage 的模式。"},{"era":"MAINS SUPPLY","en":"As public power systems spread, high voltage and low voltage became standard safety labels for supply levels.","cn":"随着公共电力系统普及，高压与低压成为供电等级的标准安全标签。"},{"era":"MEASUREMENT","en":"Twentieth-century instruments made the reading of a voltage an everyday act, and the noun absorbed both the quantity and the reading.","cn":"二十世纪的仪器让读取电压成为日常动作，这个名词同时吸收了量与读数两层意思。"},{"era":"FIGURATIVE","en":"Late twentieth-century writing applied the word to tension and excitement, as in a high voltage performance.","cn":"二十世纪晚期的写作把这个词用于紧张与兴奋，如「高电压的演出」。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds formations on volt and one look-alike suffix; group two holds the electrical quantities next to voltage.","cn":"第一组是 volt 上的构词与一个形近后缀词；第二组是与电压相邻的电学量。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"volt","ipa":"/vəʊlt/","tag":"unit","definition":"The unit itself; voltage is the quantity that the unit measures.","definitionCN":"单位本身；voltage 是它所要测量的量。"},{"word":"voltmeter","ipa":"/ˈvəʊltmiːtə/","tag":"instrument","definition":"The device that reads voltage; the ending -meter marks a measuring tool.","definitionCN":"读取电压的器具；-meter 后缀标记量具。"},{"word":"amperage","ipa":"/ˈæmpərɪdʒ/","tag":"same suffix, different base","definition":"Current strength in amperes; it shares the -age ending but not the base.","definitionCN":"以安培表示的电流强度；同用 -age 后缀，词基不同。"},{"word":"wattage","ipa":"/ˈwɒtɪdʒ/","tag":"same suffix, different base","definition":"Power in watts; again the suffix matches while the quantity differs.","definitionCN":"以瓦表示的功率；同样是后缀相同而量不同。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"potential difference","ipa":"/pəˈtenʃl ˈdɪfrəns/","tag":"formal synonym","definition":"The precise scientific name for what voltage measures, at the cost of length.","definitionCN":"电压所测之物的精确科学名称，代价是更长。"},{"word":"current","ipa":"/ˈkʌrənt/","tag":"flow it drives","definition":"The charge actually moving; voltage is the push behind it.","definitionCN":"真正在移动的电荷；电压是它背后的推力。"},{"word":"electromotive force","ipa":"/ɪˌlektrəˈməʊtɪv fɔːs/","tag":"source term","definition":"The emf supplied by a source, often treated as the cause of a voltage.","definitionCN":"电源提供的电动势，常被视为电压的成因。"},{"word":"charge","ipa":"/tʃɑːdʒ/","tag":"quantity moved","definition":"The electricity carried by a body; voltage is a difference between two such bodies.","definitionCN":"物体携带的电；电压是两个这种物体之间的差。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real name Volta, the real unit and the real water analogue.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的伏打之名、真实单位，以及真实的水压类比。"},"normal":[{"en":"The name is a person: Volta built the pile, and the unit keeps his name in the form volt.","cn":"这个名字来自一个人：伏打造出电堆，单位以他的名字化作伏特。"},{"en":"The suffix matches its neighbours: volt gives voltage, ampere gives amperage, watt gives wattage.","cn":"后缀与邻居一致：volt 给 voltage，ampere 给 amperage，watt 给 wattage。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the level: high voltage, low voltage, supply voltage, voltage drop.","cn":"固定搭配标出等级：高压、低压、电源电压、电压降。"},{"en":"The water picture works: height is voltage, flow is current, pipe width is resistance.","cn":"水的图景成立：高度是电压，流量是电流，管径是电阻。"},{"en":"A battery is the simplest source, so its level is simply called its voltage.","cn":"电池是最简单的来源，因此它的水平就直接叫它的电压。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a water tower: no height difference, no flow.","cn":"想象一座水塔：没有高度差，就没有水流。"},{"en":"Picture a narrow pipe that loses height along its length: that loss is the voltage drop.","cn":"想象一根细管沿程损失高度：这份损失就是电压降。"},{"en":"Picture a hall where the tension rises note by note until the last chord.","cn":"想象一座大厅，张力一个音一个音地升高，直到最后一个和弦。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The voltage across the resistor is equal to current times resistance.","cn":"电阻两端的电压等于电流乘以电阻。"},{"en":"Never work on a circuit while a dangerous voltage is present.","cn":"有危险电压时绝不能操作电路。"},{"en":"The conductor raised the voltage of the final movement without speeding up.","cn":"指挥没有加快速度，却把末乐章的张力抬了起来。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"volt（伏特，源自伏打之名）+ -age（数量后缀）——用伏特计量的那种势差 → 电压","word":"voltage"},"root":"voltage 为十九世纪构词：意大利物理学家伏打（Volta）之名 → 电压单位 volt → 加 -age 构成 voltage。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses start with a difference in potential, turn it into a number and a supply level, follow it along a wire, read it on a meter, and end with a figurative level of tension.","cn":"八个义项从电势差出发，把它变成数字与供电等级，沿导线追踪它，在仪表上读取它，最后落到比喻性的张力水平。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a water tower whose height difference pushes water through a pipe.","cn":"核心意象：一座水塔，高度差把水压进管道。"},"chain":["PRESSURE OF CHARGE","NUMBER OF VOLTS","MAINS LEVEL","HIGH OR LOW","LOSS ALONG A WIRE","NEEDLE READING"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"The difference itself and the number that states it.","cn":"差值本身，以及说出这个差值的数字。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"The supply chosen for a building, and the safety bands it is sorted into.","cn":"为一栋建筑选定的供电，以及它被划入的安全等级。"},{"senses":"05","en":"The difference shrinking as current travels through resistance.","cn":"电流经过电阻时逐渐缩小的差值。"},{"senses":"06 · 07","en":"The simplest source and the dial that turns it into a number.","cn":"最简单的来源，以及把它变成数字的表盘。"},{"senses":"08","en":"The pressure of a moment, felt as tension rather than measured in volts.","cn":"某一刻的压力，被感受为张力，而不是用伏特计量。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Voltage is a modern derivative of the unit name volt, so the family is read from the scientist's name outward.","cn":"voltage 是单位名 volt 的现代派生词，整个词族从这位科学家的名字向外读。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Volta is an Italian family name, not a Latin word; the unit volt and its compounds are modern scientific coinages, so there are no Latin relatives to list.","cn":"Volta 是意大利姓氏而非拉丁词；单位 volt 及其复合词都是现代科学造词，因此没有可列的拉丁同族形式。"},"items":[{"word":"volt","structure":"Volta (surname) → volt (unit)","meaning":"the unit of potential difference","meaningCN":"伏特（电势差单位，由人名转为单位）","example":"The cell supplies one and a half volts.","exampleCN":"这节电池提供一点五伏。"},{"word":"voltage","structure":"volt + -age (quantity suffix)","meaning":"potential difference measured in volts","meaningCN":"电压（单位名加数量后缀，单位转为可测的量）","example":"The voltage rose sharply.","exampleCN":"电压急剧上升。"},{"word":"voltmeter","structure":"volt + -meter (measuring device)","meaning":"an instrument that reads voltage","meaningCN":"电压表（单位名加量具后缀，量转为仪器）","example":"The voltmeter needle settled.","exampleCN":"电压表指针稳定下来。"},{"word":"voltaic","structure":"Volta + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"producing electricity by chemical action","meaningCN":"伏打式的；由化学作用生电的（人名加形容词后缀，转成方式）","example":"A voltaic cell powered the first telegraphs.","exampleCN":"伏打电池驱动了最早的电报。"},{"word":"kilovolt","structure":"kilo- (thousand) + volt","meaning":"a thousand volts","meaningCN":"千伏（加千倍前缀，单位被放大）","example":"The line runs at several kilovolts.","exampleCN":"这条线路运行在数千伏。"},{"word":"millivolt","structure":"milli- (thousandth) + volt","meaning":"one thousandth of a volt","meaningCN":"毫伏（加千分之一前缀，单位被缩小）","example":"The signal is only a few millivolts.","exampleCN":"信号只有几毫伏。"},{"word":"high-voltage","structure":"high + voltage (compound)","meaning":"carrying or needing a high voltage","meaningCN":"高压的（由「高」与电压复合，量转为等级标签）","example":"High-voltage cables cross the valley.","exampleCN":"高压电缆穿过山谷。"},{"word":"voltage divider","structure":"voltage + divider (compound)","meaning":"a circuit that splits a voltage into smaller parts","meaningCN":"分压器（电压加分配者复合，量转为电路功能）","example":"The sensor uses a voltage divider.","exampleCN":"传感器使用一个分压器。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"conductor","ipa_uk":"/kənˈdʌktə/","ipa_us":"/kənˈdʌktər/","definition_zh":"导体；导线；乐队指挥；列车员；售票员","definition_en":"a material that carries heat or electricity, or a person who leads an orchestra, a train or a bus","core_image":"一支队伍沿着一条通道把东西一件件传下去，直到最末端的人手里","scene":"音乐厅里，指挥抬起双手，整个乐团在同一秒吸气，随后弦乐齐声进入。The conductor raised both hands and the orchestra began together.","sceneCN":"这里 conductor 指「乐队指挥」（第 5 个义项：指挥乐团的人）；句意为指挥抬起双手，乐团齐声开始。图中可辨识物件：指挥台、指挥棒、乐谱、乐团。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"导体；导线；导电或导热的材料"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"乐队指挥"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"列车员；（公共汽车）售票员"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a good conductor","zh":"良导体"},{"phrase":"electrical conductor","zh":"电导体"},{"phrase":"thermal conductor","zh":"热导体"},{"phrase":"orchestra conductor","zh":"乐团指挥"},{"phrase":"train conductor","zh":"列车员"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"conductor"},{"label":"复数","form":"conductors"},{"label":"动词","form":"conduct"},{"label":"名词（传导）","form":"conduction"},{"label":"形容词","form":"conductive"},{"label":"名词（传导率）","form":"conductivity"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"conduct","pos":"v./n.","zh":"传导；指挥；行为"},{"word":"conduction","pos":"n.","zh":"传导"},{"word":"conductive","pos":"adj.","zh":"导电的；导热的"},{"word":"conductivity","pos":"n.","zh":"传导率；电导率"},{"word":"semiconductor","pos":"n.","zh":"半导体"},{"word":"conductance","pos":"n.","zh":"电导"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A material that passes energy","titleCN":"导体：能传导电或热的材料","definition":"a material or object through which heat or electricity passes easily","definitionCN":"热或电容易通过的材料或物体","example":"Copper is a good conductor, which is why cables are made of it.","exampleCN":"铜是良导体，因此电缆多用铜做。","why":"The Latin verb meant 'to lead together', and a conductor leads energy from one place to another without being changed by it.","whyCN":"拉丁动词意为「一起引导」，导体把能量从一处引到另一处，自身却不被改变。"},{"no":"02","title":"An electrical conductor","titleCN":"电导体：允许电荷流动的材料","definition":"a material in which electric charge can move freely","definitionCN":"电荷可以在其中自由移动的材料","example":"Silver is the best electrical conductor among common metals.","exampleCN":"在常见金属中，银是最好的电导体。","why":"In electricity the word narrows to charge: the material provides the path, and the current is what travels along it.","whyCN":"在电学中，这个词收窄到电荷：材料提供道路，电流才是沿路前进的东西。"},{"no":"03","title":"A thermal conductor","titleCN":"热导体：传热材料","definition":"a material that carries heat well","definitionCN":"导热良好的材料","example":"A metal pan is a thermal conductor, so the handle must be insulated.","exampleCN":"金属锅是热导体，因此锅柄必须隔热。","why":"Heat, like charge, needs a material that lets its particles pass energy along, so the same word covers both cases.","whyCN":"热与电荷一样，需要一种能让粒子把能量一路传下去的材料，因此同一个词覆盖了两种情形。"},{"no":"04","title":"A wire or current path","titleCN":"电路中的导线或导电部件","definition":"a wire or metal part that carries current in a circuit","definitionCN":"电路中承载电流的导线或金属部件","example":"The conductor in the cable is stranded copper.","exampleCN":"电缆里的导体是多股铜线。","why":"A wire is the conductor made into a product, so the word also names the physical part an electrician handles.","whyCN":"导线是把导体做成了产品，因此这个词也指电工手里的那个实体部件。"},{"no":"05","title":"The leader of an orchestra","titleCN":"乐队指挥","definition":"a person who directs an orchestra or choir in performance","definitionCN":"在演出中指导管弦乐团或合唱团的人","example":"The conductor raised both hands and the orchestra began together.","exampleCN":"指挥抬起双手，乐团齐声开始。","why":"The person does to the players what the material does to energy: both lead many separate parts into one moving stream.","whyCN":"这个人对乐手做的事，正如材料对能量做的事：都把许多分散的部分引入同一条流动。"},{"no":"06","title":"The guard on a train","titleCN":"列车员","definition":"an official who manages passengers and tickets on a train","definitionCN":"在列车上管理乘客与车票的乘务人员","example":"The conductor walked the aisle checking tickets.","exampleCN":"列车员沿过道查票。","why":"Railways borrowed the leading word for the person who conducts passengers and collects fares along the route.","whyCN":"铁路借用了这个「引导」的词，指沿线路照看乘客并收票的人。"},{"no":"07","title":"The fare collector on a bus","titleCN":"公共汽车售票员","definition":"a person who collects fares and issues tickets on a bus","definitionCN":"在公共汽车上收车费、发票的人","example":"The conductor rang the bell for the next stop.","exampleCN":"售票员按铃提示下一站。","why":"The same role moved from trains to buses: someone must lead passengers along the route and settle fares.","whyCN":"同一个角色从列车移到公交：总得有人沿线路照看乘客并结清车费。"},{"no":"08","title":"A carrier of ideas","titleCN":"比喻：传递思想或能量的中介","definition":"a person or thing that carries ideas, culture or energy to others","definitionCN":"把思想、文化或能量传给别人的中介","example":"She acted as a conductor for the new music in her town.","exampleCN":"她成了新音乐在她所在城市里的传播者。","why":"The metaphor keeps the core: something passes through a medium and arrives elsewhere, and the medium is named for the passage.","whyCN":"这个比喻保留了核心：某种东西穿过一个媒介抵达别处，而媒介因这条通路得名。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Conductor comes from Latin conducere 'to lead together', built on com- and ducere 'to lead'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"conductor 来自拉丁 conducere「一起引导」，由 com- 与 ducere「引导」构成。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN DUCERE","en":"Latin ducere meant 'to lead, to draw', the same root that gives duke and duct.","cn":"拉丁 ducere 意为「引导、拉」，同一词根还给出 duke（公爵）与 duct（管道）。"},{"era":"LATIN CONDUCERE","en":"Com- 'together' plus ducere produced conducere, 'to bring together, to lead along, to hire'.","cn":"com-「一起」加 ducere 构成 conducere，意为「聚在一起、沿着引导、雇请」。"},{"era":"LATIN CONDUCTOR","en":"Conductor in Latin named one who leads or hires, especially a contractor or a guide.","cn":"拉丁 conductor 指引导者或雇请者，尤指承包人与向导。"},{"era":"ENGLISH CONDUCT","en":"English borrowed conduct in the fourteenth century as a verb of leading and guiding, and conductor followed as the person.","cn":"英语在十四世纪借入 conduct，作引导、指导的动词，conductor 随后指做这件事的人。"},{"era":"MUSICAL SENSE","en":"By the late eighteenth century conductor named the person who beats time and directs an ensemble.","cn":"到十八世纪晚期，conductor 指打拍子并指导乐团的人。"},{"era":"TRANSPORT AND PHYSICS","en":"Nineteenth-century railways gave the word to the train official, while physics used it for the material that carries charge or heat.","cn":"十九世纪的铁路把这个词给了列车乘务员，物理学则用它指运送电荷或热的材料。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds derivatives of the same Latin verb; group two holds the people and materials that carry something onward.","cn":"第一组是同一拉丁动词的派生词；第二组是把东西继续运送下去的人与材料。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"conduct","ipa":"/kənˈdʌkt/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"To lead, carry or manage; conductor is the person or thing that does it.","definitionCN":"引导、传导或管理；conductor 是执行者或导体。"},{"word":"conduction","ipa":"/kənˈdʌkʃn/","tag":"same root, process","definition":"The process of carrying heat or charge through a material.","definitionCN":"热或电荷通过材料的过程。"},{"word":"conductive","ipa":"/kənˈdʌktɪv/","tag":"same root, adjective","definition":"Describing a material that passes energy; conductor is the noun.","definitionCN":"形容材料能传递能量；conductor 是对应名词。"},{"word":"conductivity","ipa":"/ˌkɒndʌkˈtɪvəti/","tag":"same root, measure","definition":"How well a material conducts, a number rather than an object.","definitionCN":"材料传导能力的高低，是一个数值而非物体。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"guide","ipa":"/ɡaɪd/","tag":"person who leads","definition":"Someone who shows the way; a conductor also keeps a group together in time.","definitionCN":"带路的人；指挥还要让一群人在时间上合为一体。"},{"word":"director","ipa":"/dəˈrektə/","tag":"artistic leader","definition":"The person in charge of a production or institution; the musical conductor works with the players.","definitionCN":"负责演出或机构的人；音乐指挥与乐手直接合作。"},{"word":"insulator","ipa":"/ɪnˈsʌleɪtə/","tag":"opposite material","definition":"A material that blocks heat or charge; it is the exact opposite of a conductor.","definitionCN":"阻挡热或电荷的材料，正是导体的反面。"},{"word":"carrier","ipa":"/ˈkæriə/","tag":"generic carrier","definition":"Anything that transports something else, from a letter carrier to a charge carrier.","definitionCN":"任何运送他物的东西，从邮递员到载流子。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real Latin verb, the real musical and railway senses, and the real physics contrast.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的拉丁动词、真实的音乐与铁路义，以及真实的物理对立。"},"normal":[{"en":"The root means lead: conduct, conductor, conduction and conductivity all describe leading something along.","cn":"词根意为「引导」：conduct、conductor、conduction、conductivity 都描述把某物引过去。"},{"en":"The family runs conduct, conduction, conductive, conductivity, semiconductor and conductance.","cn":"同族词包括 conduct、conduction、conductive、conductivity、semiconductor 与 conductance。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the material sense: good conductor, electrical conductor, thermal conductor.","cn":"固定搭配标出材料义：良导体、电导体、热导体。"},{"en":"A conductor leads players, passengers or charge; the direction is always from one place to another.","cn":"指挥带乐手，列车员带乘客，导体带电荷；方向总是从一处到另一处。"},{"en":"The physics contrast is clean: a conductor passes, an insulator blocks.","cn":"物理上的对立很清楚：导体放行，绝缘体阻挡。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a relay race: each hand passes the baton to the next without keeping it.","cn":"想象一场接力：每一手都把棒传给下一手，并不留下。"},{"en":"Picture a hall where one raised hand makes two hundred bows move as one.","cn":"想象一座大厅，一只抬起的手让两百把琴弓合成一个动作。"},{"en":"Picture a narrow gate that lets water through and a wall that refuses it.","cn":"想象一道放水通过的小门，以及一堵拒绝水的墙。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Pure water is a poor conductor, which is why it is used in demonstrations.","cn":"纯水是劣导体，因此常被用于演示。"},{"en":"The conductor stopped the orchestra and asked for a softer entry.","cn":"指挥停下乐团，要求更轻的进入。"},{"en":"The conductor checked our tickets just after the train left the station.","cn":"列车刚出站，列车员就来查票。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"con-（一起）+ duct（引导）+ -or（做某事的人或物）——把东西一起引过去的人或物 → 指挥；导体","word":"conductor"},"root":"拉丁 conducere（com- 一起 + ducere 引导）→ 拉丁 conductor（引导者）→ 英语 conductor；物理义与音乐义都在引导这一核心上分叉。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with a material that passes energy, narrow to electric and thermal paths and a wire, then move to the orchestra leader, the train and bus officials, and end with a carrier of ideas.","cn":"八个义项从传递能量的材料开始，收窄到电与热的通路及导线，再转到乐团指挥、列车与公交的乘务人员，最后落到思想的传递者。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a line of people passing something hand to hand until it reaches the end.","cn":"核心意象：一队人把东西一手一手传下去，直到最末端。"},"chain":["LEAD TOGETHER","MATERIAL THAT PASSES","COPPER WIRE","ORCHESTRA LEADER","TRAIN GUARD","CARRIER OF IDEAS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04","en":"The material and the made part: what passes energy, and the wire that does it in a circuit.","cn":"材料与制成品：什么能传递能量，以及电路中做这件事的导线。"},{"senses":"02","en":"The electrical case, where the thing passed is charge.","cn":"电学情形，被传递的东西是电荷。"},{"senses":"03","en":"The thermal case, where the thing passed is heat.","cn":"热学情形，被传递的东西是热。"},{"senses":"05 · 06 · 07","en":"People who lead others along: players on a stage, passengers on a train or a bus.","cn":"引导他人的人：舞台上的乐手、列车与公交上的乘客。"},{"senses":"08","en":"The core detached from metal and made abstract: a medium for ideas.","cn":"核心脱离金属而被抽象化：思想的媒介。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Conductor is the person-or-thing noun of the verb conduct, built on Latin conducere.","cn":"conductor 是动词 conduct 的「人或物」名词，建立在拉丁 conducere 上。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin conducere joins com- 'together' and ducere 'to lead'; conductor and conductus belong to the same verb, and English added -ive, -ivity and -ance to the stem.","cn":"拉丁 conducere 由 com-「一起」与 ducere「引导」构成；conductor 与 conductus 同出这一动词，英语又在词干上加 -ive、-ivity 与 -ance。"},"items":[{"word":"conduct","structure":"con- + duct (lead)","meaning":"to lead, carry or manage","meaningCN":"传导；引导；管理（前缀加引导词根，动作本身）","example":"Metals conduct heat well.","exampleCN":"金属导热良好。"},{"word":"conductor","structure":"conduct + -or (one who or that does)","meaning":"a thing or person that carries or leads","meaningCN":"导体；指挥（加执行者后缀，动作转执行者）","example":"The conductor stopped the players.","exampleCN":"指挥让乐手停下。"},{"word":"conduction","structure":"conduct + -ion (process)","meaning":"the passing of heat or charge through matter","meaningCN":"传导过程（加过程后缀，动作转物理过程）","example":"Conduction warms the whole bar.","exampleCN":"传导把整根棒加热。"},{"word":"conductive","structure":"conduct + -ive (tending to)","meaning":"able to pass heat or charge","meaningCN":"导电的；导热的（加倾向后缀，动作转性质）","example":"The paste is conductive.","exampleCN":"这种膏体是导电的。"},{"word":"conductivity","structure":"conductive + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the measured ability to conduct","meaningCN":"传导率；电导率（再加性质后缀，性质转可测量的量）","example":"Copper has high conductivity.","exampleCN":"铜的电导率高。"},{"word":"conductance","structure":"conduct + -ance (state)","meaning":"the ease with which a path passes current","meaningCN":"电导（加状态后缀，动作转通路能力）","example":"Conductance falls as the wire lengthens.","exampleCN":"导线变长时电导下降。"},{"word":"semiconductor","structure":"semi- (half) + conductor","meaning":"a material that conducts only under conditions","meaningCN":"半导体（加「一半」前缀，导体性质被限定）","example":"A semiconductor switches the current.","exampleCN":"半导体开关电流。"},{"word":"misconduct","structure":"mis- (wrongly) + conduct","meaning":"wrong behaviour, especially in an official role","meaningCN":"失职；不当行为（加「错误」前缀，引导转为行为评价）","example":"The guard was dismissed for misconduct.","exampleCN":"这名警卫因失职被解雇。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"ducere","structure":"ducere, duco, duxi, ductum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to lead, to draw","meaningCN":"引导；拉"},{"word":"conducere","structure":"conducere, conduco, conduxi, conductum (verb)","meaning":"to lead together, to hire","meaningCN":"一起引导；雇请"},{"word":"conductor","structure":"conductor, conductoris (m., third declension)","meaning":"one who leads or hires","meaningCN":"引导者；雇请者"},{"word":"conductus","structure":"conductus (past participle)","meaning":"led, brought together","meaningCN":"被引导的；被聚集的"}]}},{"word":"conductive","ipa_uk":"/kənˈdʌktɪv/","ipa_us":"/kənˈdʌktɪv/","definition_zh":"导电的；导热的；有助于……的","definition_en":"able to carry heat or electricity, or able to help something happen","core_image":"一条铜带把热量从火焰这头送到那头，中途几乎没有丢掉什么","scene":"实验室里，学生把一根铜棒的一端放进火焰，另一端的蜡很快开始融化。The copper strip proved so conductive that the wax melted within seconds.","sceneCN":"这里 conductive 指「导热的」（第 2 个义项：能传递热）；句意为铜条导热太好，蜡几秒就融化了。图中可辨识物件：铜棒、火焰、蜡块、温度计。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"导电的；导热的；可传导的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"有助于……的；有利于……发生的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"conductive material","zh":"导电材料"},{"phrase":"electrically conductive","zh":"导电的"},{"phrase":"thermally conductive","zh":"导热的"},{"phrase":"conductive to learning","zh":"有助于学习的"},{"phrase":"conductive hearing loss","zh":"传导性听力损失"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more conductive"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most conductive"},{"label":"名词（传导率）","form":"conductivity"},{"label":"名词（传导）","form":"conduction"},{"label":"名词（导体）","form":"conductor"},{"label":"副词","form":"conductively"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"conduct","pos":"v./n.","zh":"传导；指挥；行为"},{"word":"conduction","pos":"n.","zh":"传导"},{"word":"conductivity","pos":"n.","zh":"传导率；电导率"},{"word":"conductor","pos":"n.","zh":"导体；指挥"},{"word":"semiconductor","pos":"n.","zh":"半导体"},{"word":"nonconductive","pos":"adj.","zh":"不导电的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Carrying electric charge","titleCN":"导电的：能让电荷通过","definition":"able to carry electric charge from one place to another","definitionCN":"能把电荷从一处送到另一处","example":"The salt solution becomes conductive once the ions separate.","exampleCN":"离子一旦分开，盐溶液就变得导电。","why":"The Latin verb meant leading along, and the suffix adds a tendency: a conductive material tends to let charge travel through it.","whyCN":"拉丁动词意为「引导」，后缀又加上「倾向」：导电材料倾向于让电荷穿过。"},{"no":"02","title":"Carrying heat","titleCN":"导热的：能让热通过","definition":"able to carry heat from a warmer place to a cooler one","definitionCN":"能把热从较热处传到较冷处","example":"The copper strip proved so conductive that the wax melted within seconds.","exampleCN":"铜条导热太好，蜡几秒就融化了。","why":"Heat and charge both move through the same solids in the same way, so one adjective serves the two cases.","whyCN":"热与电荷在同样的固体里以同样的方式移动，因此一个形容词同时服务两种情形。"},{"no":"03","title":"Able to pass something through","titleCN":"可传导的：能让某种能量通过","definition":"able to let a form of energy or a signal pass through a medium","definitionCN":"能让某种能量或信号穿过介质","example":"The gel is conductive to ultrasound but not to light.","exampleCN":"这种凝胶能传导超声，却不能让光通过。","why":"The core of the word is passage rather than electricity, so it applies to sound, light and other signals when a medium carries them.","whyCN":"这个词的核心是「通过」，而不是电，因此当介质运送声音、光等信号时也能用它。"},{"no":"04","title":"Strongly conductive","titleCN":"导电或导热性强的；良导的","definition":"having a high ability to carry charge or heat","definitionCN":"传导电荷或热的能力很强","example":"Silver is the most conductive metal, which is why it is used in contacts.","exampleCN":"银是导电性最强的金属，因此常用于触点。","why":"The adjective is gradable: materials are compared by how much they pass, so it also means strongly conductive.","whyCN":"这个形容词有程度差别：材料按通过量比较，因此它也指「传导性强的」。"},{"no":"05","title":"Of conductance","titleCN":"电导的；与传导率有关的","definition":"relating to conductivity or to the measured ease of passing current","definitionCN":"与传导率或以数值衡量的通电难易有关","example":"The team measured the conductive properties of the alloy at low temperature.","exampleCN":"团队测量了这种合金在低温下的电导特性。","why":"Once the ability is expressed as a number, the adjective attaches to measurements and technical descriptions.","whyCN":"当这种能力被表示成数值，形容词就附着在测量与技术描述上。"},{"no":"06","title":"Of sound reaching the ear","titleCN":"传导性听力损失的（医学）","definition":"relating to sound being blocked in its path to the inner ear rather than to the nerve","definitionCN":"指声音在到达内耳的路途中受阻，而不是神经本身出问题","example":"Conductive hearing loss improves when the blockage is removed.","exampleCN":"传导性听力损失在阻塞被清除后会改善。","why":"Medicine borrowed the word for a pathway problem: the sound is fine, but its conduction through the ear is interrupted.","whyCN":"医学借用了这个词来表示通路问题：声音本身没问题，是它在耳内的传导被中断了。"},{"no":"07","title":"Helping something happen","titleCN":"有助于……的；有利于……的","definition":"tending to help or promote a result, often followed by to","definitionCN":"倾向于促成某种结果，常接 to","example":"A quiet room is conductive to concentration.","exampleCN":"安静的屋子有助于集中注意力。","why":"The metaphor keeps the idea of a path: conditions that are conductive to something make it easy for that thing to travel toward its result.","whyCN":"这个隐喻保留了通路的意思：有利于某事的条件，让那件事更容易走向结果。"},{"no":"08","title":"Likely to set off a reaction","titleCN":"抽象义：容易引发某种结果或氛围的","definition":"likely to bring about a particular mood, reaction or outcome","definitionCN":"容易带来某种气氛、反应或结果","example":"That rumour was conductive to panic in the crowded hall.","exampleCN":"那条谣言很容易在拥挤的大厅里引发恐慌。","why":"The abstract sense pushes the path idea into cause: what is conductive to panic lets panic spread as if along a wire.","whyCN":"抽象义把通路推向因果：有利于恐慌的东西，让恐慌像沿导线一样扩散。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Conductive is conduct plus the Latin suffix -ive, from the verb conducere 'to lead together'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"conductive 是 conduct 加拉丁后缀 -ive 构成，源自动词 conducere「一起引导」。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN CONDUCERE","en":"Conducere joined com- 'together' with ducere 'to lead', giving the sense of bringing something along a path.","cn":"conducere 由 com-「一起」与 ducere「引导」构成，意为把某物沿一条路带过去。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN CONDUCTIVUS","en":"Later Latin formed conductivus, 'tending to lead or carry', which English took as conductive in the seventeenth century.","cn":"晚期拉丁语构成 conductivus，意为「有引导、运送倾向的」，英语在十七世纪借入作 conductive。"},{"era":"ENGLISH CONDUCTIVE","en":"Early English uses described substances that carry heat or fluid, long before the word was tied to electricity.","cn":"早期英语用法描述能传热或传流体的物质，远在它被绑定到电之前。"},{"era":"PHYSICS","en":"Eighteenth- and nineteenth-century experimenters applied it to materials that pass charge, and conductivity became its measured noun.","cn":"十八、十九世纪的实验者用它指能通过电荷的材料，conductivity 成为其可测量的名词形式。"},{"era":"CONDUCTIVE TO","en":"The phrase conductive to, meaning helpful to a result, is recorded from the seventeenth century and grew alongside the physical sense.","cn":"conductive to 表示有助于某种结果，自十七世纪起有记录，与物理义同时发展。"},{"era":"MEDICAL SENSE","en":"Twentieth-century audiology used conductive for sound blocked on its way through the outer or middle ear.","cn":"二十世纪的听力学用 conductive 指声音在外耳或中耳通道上受阻。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds derivatives of the same Latin verb; group two holds words about passing or helping things through.","cn":"第一组是同一拉丁动词的派生词；第二组是关于让东西通过或促成的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"conduct","ipa":"/kənˈdʌkt/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"To carry or lead; conductive describes the ability to do so.","definitionCN":"运送或引导；conductive 描述具备这种能力。"},{"word":"conduction","ipa":"/kənˈdʌkʃn/","tag":"same root, process","definition":"The process of carrying heat or charge through a material.","definitionCN":"热或电荷通过材料的过程。"},{"word":"conductor","ipa":"/kənˈdʌktə/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"The material or person that carries; the adjective describes it.","definitionCN":"承载或引导的材料或人；形容词描述这一性质。"},{"word":"conductivity","ipa":"/ˌkɒndʌkˈtɪvəti/","tag":"same root, measure","definition":"How well a material conducts, expressed as a number.","definitionCN":"材料传导能力的数值表示。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"transmitting","ipa":"/trænzˈmɪtɪŋ/","tag":"active passage","definition":"Actively sending energy or signals onward, often with a device attached.","definitionCN":"主动把能量或信号送出去，常涉及具体装置。"},{"word":"permeable","ipa":"/ˈpɜːmiəbl/","tag":"lets things through","definition":"Allows fluids or gases to pass through pores; not used for charge.","definitionCN":"允许流体或气体穿过孔隙；不用于电荷。"},{"word":"insulating","ipa":"/ɪnˈsʌleɪtɪŋ/","tag":"the opposite","definition":"Preventing heat or charge from passing; the exact reverse of conductive.","definitionCN":"阻止热或电荷通过，正是 conductive 的反面。"},{"word":"favourable","ipa":"/ˈfeɪvərəbl/","tag":"helps a result","definition":"The plain word for conditions that help something succeed, close to conductive to.","definitionCN":"表示条件有助于成功的平实说法，接近 conductive to。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real Latin verb, the real suffixes, and the real split between electricity and help.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的拉丁动词、真实的后缀，以及电学义与「有助于」义的真实分工。"},"normal":[{"en":"The root is lead: conduct, conductor, conduction and conductivity all describe something travelling along a path.","cn":"词根是「引导」：conduct、conductor、conduction、conductivity 都描述沿通路行进的过程。"},{"en":"The suffix -ive adds a tendency: a conductive material tends to let energy through.","cn":"后缀 -ive 加「倾向」：导电材料倾向于让能量通过。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the physics: conductive material, electrically conductive, thermally conductive.","cn":"固定搭配标出物理义：导电材料、电导的、导热的。"},{"en":"The same adjective turns social: a quiet room is conductive to concentration.","cn":"同一个形容词也转向社会语境：安静的屋子有助于集中注意力。"},{"en":"Medicine keeps the path picture: conductive hearing loss is a blockage on the way in, not a damaged nerve.","cn":"医学保留了通路图景：传导性听力损失是入口堵塞，而不是神经受损。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture heat walking down a copper rod hand over hand.","cn":"想象热沿着铜棒一手接一手地往下走。"},{"en":"Picture a hall with the doors open, so sound walks in without effort.","cn":"想象一座门都敞开的大厅，声音毫不费力地走进来。"},{"en":"Picture conditions arranged like rails, so an outcome can roll toward you.","cn":"想象条件摆成轨道，让结果顺着轨道滚向你。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The new polymer is conductive but still flexible enough to print on.","cn":"这种新聚合物能导电，又软到可以印刷。"},{"en":"Poorly conductive walls let the heat escape within an hour.","cn":"导热差的墙一小时内就把热量放跑了。"},{"en":"A regular routine is conductive to better sleep.","cn":"规律的作息有助于改善睡眠。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"con-（一起）+ duct（引导）+ -ive（有……倾向的）——倾向于让能量通过 → 导电的、导热的；有助于的","word":"conductive"},"root":"拉丁 conducere（一起引导）→ 晚期拉丁 conductivus（有运送倾向的）→ 英语 conductive；电学义与「有助于」义都从「沿路引过去」发展而来。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with charge and heat passing through a material, widen to any energy, become a measured property, turn medical, and end with conditions that help a result along.","cn":"八个义项从电荷与热穿过材料开始，扩展到任何能量，变成可测量的性质，转入医学，最后落到有助于结果的条件。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a copper strip passing heat from a flame to a lump of wax.","cn":"核心意象：一条铜带把热从火焰送到一块蜡。"},"chain":["LEAD TOGETHER","PASSES ENERGY","COPPER","MEASURE OF PASSAGE","SOUND PATH","HELPS ALONG"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04","en":"The electric case and its strong form: charge passes, and some metals pass it very well.","cn":"电学情形及其强形式：电荷通过，有些金属通过得极好。"},{"senses":"02","en":"The thermal case, where what travels is heat.","cn":"热学情形，通过的是热。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"Any energy through any medium, and the number that states how easily it passes.","cn":"任何能量穿过任何介质，以及说明通过难易的数值。"},{"senses":"06","en":"Sound blocked on its path through the ear, so the pathway itself is the problem.","cn":"声音在耳内通道上受阻，问题出在通路本身。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"Conditions that help a result travel toward you, or let a mood spread.","cn":"有助于结果走向你的条件，或让某种情绪扩散的条件。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Conductive is the adjective of conduct, and the whole family attaches ordinary suffixes to the Latin stem duct-.","cn":"conductive 是 conduct 的形容词，整个词族都在拉丁词干 duct- 上加普通后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Conducere and its participle conductus supply the stem; conductivus is a later Latin adjective, and English built conductor, conduction, conductivity and conductance on the same base.","cn":"conducere 及其分词 conductus 提供词干；conductivus 是晚期拉丁形容词，英语又在同一词基上构造 conductor、conduction、conductivity 与 conductance。"},"items":[{"word":"conduct","structure":"con- + duct (lead)","meaning":"to carry, lead or manage","meaningCN":"传导；引导；管理（前缀加引导词根，动作本身）","example":"Copper conducts heat quickly.","exampleCN":"铜传热很快。"},{"word":"conductive","structure":"conduct + -ive (tending to)","meaning":"tending to carry heat or charge","meaningCN":"有传导倾向的（加倾向后缀，动作转性质）","example":"The sheet is conductive on one side.","exampleCN":"这片薄板一面导电。"},{"word":"conduction","structure":"conduct + -ion (process)","meaning":"the passing of heat or charge through matter","meaningCN":"传导过程（加过程后缀，动作转过程）","example":"Conduction explains the warm handle.","exampleCN":"传导解释了手柄为什么发热。"},{"word":"conductivity","structure":"conductive + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the measured ability to conduct","meaningCN":"传导率（再加性质后缀，性质转数值）","example":"Its conductivity is close to copper.","exampleCN":"它的传导率接近铜。"},{"word":"conductor","structure":"conduct + -or (one that does)","meaning":"a material or person that carries","meaningCN":"导体；指挥（加执行者后缀，动作转执行者）","example":"Carbon is a fair conductor.","exampleCN":"碳是尚可的导体。"},{"word":"conductance","structure":"conduct + -ance (state)","meaning":"the ease with which a path passes current","meaningCN":"电导（加状态后缀，动作转通路能力）","example":"Conductance doubles when the wire thickens.","exampleCN":"导线变粗时电导翻倍。"},{"word":"semiconductor","structure":"semi- (half) + conductor","meaning":"a material that conducts only under set conditions","meaningCN":"半导体（加「一半」前缀，导体性质被限定）","example":"A semiconductor can switch the current.","exampleCN":"半导体能开关电流。"},{"word":"nonconductive","structure":"non- (not) + conductive","meaning":"not able to carry charge","meaningCN":"不导电的（加否定前缀，性质被取消）","example":"The handle is nonconductive.","exampleCN":"手柄是不导电的。"},{"word":"photoconductive","structure":"photo- (light) + conductive","meaning":"becoming conductive when light falls on it","meaningCN":"光导的（加「光」前缀，传导条件变成光照）","example":"The sensor uses a photoconductive layer.","exampleCN":"传感器使用一层光导材料。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"ducere","structure":"ducere, duco, duxi, ductum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to lead, to draw","meaningCN":"引导；拉"},{"word":"conductus","structure":"conductus (past participle of conducere)","meaning":"led, brought along","meaningCN":"被引导的；被带过去的"},{"word":"conductivus","structure":"conductivus, conductiva, conductivum (Later Latin adjective)","meaning":"tending to lead or carry","meaningCN":"有引导、运送倾向的"},{"word":"conductio","structure":"conductio, conductionis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a leading together; a hiring","meaningCN":"引导；租雇"}]}},{"word":"insulator","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈsʌleɪtə/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈsʌleɪtər/","definition_zh":"绝缘体；绝缘材料；绝缘子；隔绝外界影响的东西","definition_en":"a material or object that stops electricity, heat or sound from passing, or something that cuts people off from outside influence","core_image":"一块干燥的橡胶把带电的铜线裹住，手可以放心地握住外面那层","scene":"电工作业时先戴上厚橡胶手套，再去碰那根裸线，手套外层的材料把电流牢牢挡在里面。A thick rubber insulator kept the current away from her hands.","sceneCN":"这里 insulator 指「绝缘体、绝缘材料」（第 1 个义项：阻止电流通过的材料）；句意为厚橡胶绝缘层把电流挡在她手外。图中可辨识物件：橡胶手套、裸线、配电箱、绝缘垫。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"绝缘体；绝缘材料；绝缘子"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"隔绝外界影响的人或物（比喻）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"electrical insulator","zh":"电绝缘体"},{"phrase":"thermal insulator","zh":"绝热材料"},{"phrase":"a good insulator","zh":"良好的绝缘体"},{"phrase":"ceramic insulator","zh":"陶瓷绝缘子"},{"phrase":"sound insulator","zh":"隔音材料"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"insulator"},{"label":"复数","form":"insulators"},{"label":"动词","form":"insulate"},{"label":"名词（绝缘；绝缘材料）","form":"insulation"},{"label":"形容词","form":"insulating"},{"label":"形容词（绝缘的）","form":"insulated"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"insulate","pos":"v.","zh":"使绝缘；使隔离"},{"word":"insulation","pos":"n.","zh":"绝缘；绝缘材料"},{"word":"insulating","pos":"adj.","zh":"绝缘的；隔热的"},{"word":"insular","pos":"adj.","zh":"岛屿的；偏狭的"},{"word":"isolate","pos":"v.","zh":"隔离；使孤立"},{"word":"peninsula","pos":"n.","zh":"半岛"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A material that blocks current","titleCN":"绝缘体：不导电的材料","definition":"a material that does not let electric charge pass through it easily","definitionCN":"不易让电荷通过的材料","example":"Rubber is a good insulator, so gloves are made from it.","exampleCN":"橡胶是良绝缘体，因此手套用橡胶做。","why":"The Latin word meant 'made into an island', and an island keeps water out: an insulator keeps charge out.","whyCN":"拉丁词意为「被造成岛屿」，岛把水挡在外面：绝缘体把电荷挡在外面。"},{"no":"02","title":"A specific electrical insulator","titleCN":"电绝缘材料：具体的绝缘物质","definition":"a particular material such as glass, rubber or ceramic used to block current","definitionCN":"玻璃、橡胶、陶瓷等具体用来阻断电流的材料","example":"Glass is used as an insulator in high-voltage fittings.","exampleCN":"玻璃在高压配件中用作绝缘材料。","why":"The general property becomes a trade material, so the word names the substances an engineer actually chooses.","whyCN":"一般性质变成行业材料，因此这个词指工程师实际挑选的那些物质。"},{"no":"03","title":"A thermal insulator","titleCN":"绝热材料：阻挡热传递","definition":"a material that slows the passage of heat","definitionCN":"减缓热传递的材料","example":"Foam is a thermal insulator, so it keeps the pipe warm.","exampleCN":"泡沫是绝热材料，因此能让管道保温。","why":"Heat needs a path through matter, and a material full of trapped air removes that path.","whyCN":"热需要穿过物质的路径，而充满滞留空气的材料把这条路径去掉了。"},{"no":"04","title":"A sound insulator","titleCN":"隔音材料：阻挡声音","definition":"a material that reduces the passage of sound","definitionCN":"减弱声音传播的材料","example":"The studio walls use a sound insulator between the layers.","exampleCN":"录音室墙体在层间使用隔音材料。","why":"Sound is vibration carried through matter, so a soft, air-filled layer breaks the chain of contact that would pass it on.","whyCN":"声音是靠物质传递的振动，因此柔软、含空气的一层会打断那条本可传声的接触链。"},{"no":"05","title":"The ceramic part on a power line","titleCN":"绝缘子：输电设备上的瓷件","definition":"a shaped ceramic or glass part that holds a live conductor away from its support","definitionCN":"把带电导线与支架隔开的成形陶瓷或玻璃部件","example":"The porcelain insulator flashed over in the storm.","exampleCN":"暴雨中那只瓷绝缘子发生了闪络。","why":"Engineering turns the material into a named component: the insulator is the object that does the blocking on a pole.","whyCN":"工程把材料变成有名字的部件：绝缘子就是杆上执行阻断的那个物件。"},{"no":"06","title":"The sheath on a cable","titleCN":"电线护套：包在导线外的绝缘层","definition":"the covering around a wire that keeps current inside and hands outside","definitionCN":"包在导线外、把电流关在里面、把人挡在外面的包层","example":"The insulator on the old cable had cracked.","exampleCN":"旧电缆外面的绝缘层已经开裂。","why":"The material becomes a manufactured covering, so the same noun names a thin sheath rather than a block.","whyCN":"材料变成了制成品包层，因此同一个名词可以指薄薄的一层护套，而不是厚块。"},{"no":"07","title":"Something that cuts you off","titleCN":"比喻：隔绝外界影响的东西","definition":"something that keeps a person or group apart from outside influence","definitionCN":"使个人或群体与外界影响隔开的东西","example":"Wealth acted as an insulator against the noise of the city.","exampleCN":"财富成了一道把城市的喧闹挡在外面的屏障。","why":"The metaphor is physical again: as rubber blocks charge, money or distance blocks disturbance.","whyCN":"这个比喻又回到物理层面：橡胶挡住电荷，金钱或距离挡住干扰。"},{"no":"08","title":"A protective barrier","titleCN":"抽象义：把人与干扰隔开的屏障","definition":"a barrier that protects someone from criticism, pressure or unwanted contact","definitionCN":"保护某人免受批评、压力或不想要的接触的屏障","example":"His routine was an insulator between work and worry.","exampleCN":"他的日常作息成了工作与忧虑之间的一道屏障。","why":"A habit can work like a layer of rubber: it keeps outside pressure from reaching the person inside.","whyCN":"习惯可以像一层橡胶那样起作用：它让外界的压力到不了里面的人。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Insulator comes from Latin insula 'island' through the verb insulate, 'to make into an island'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"insulator 经动词 insulate「使成岛屿」上溯拉丁 insula「岛」。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN INSULA","en":"Insula meant 'island' and also a block of flats in Rome; the core picture is something surrounded by a barrier.","cn":"insula 意为「岛」，也指罗马城里的一栋公寓楼；核心图景是被屏障围住的某物。"},{"era":"LATIN INSULATUS","en":"Insulatus meant 'made like an island', that is, cut off from what surrounds it.","cn":"insulatus 意为「被造成岛屿那样」，也就是与周围隔开。"},{"era":"ENGLISH INSULATE","en":"English insulate appeared in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries for setting something apart, and only later for blocking heat or charge.","cn":"英语 insulate 在十六、十七世纪出现，指把某物隔开，后来才用于阻挡热或电。"},{"era":"PHYSICS","en":"Eighteenth- and nineteenth-century experimenters called materials that block charge insulators, and the word became a technical noun.","cn":"十八、十九世纪的实验者把阻断电荷的材料称为绝缘体，这个词成为技术名词。"},{"era":"CERAMIC PART","en":"Telegraph and power lines needed shaped ceramic and glass pieces, so insulator also named a manufactured component.","cn":"电报与电力线路需要成形的陶瓷与玻璃件，因此 insulator 也指一种制成品部件。"},{"era":"FIGURATIVE","en":"Twentieth-century writing extended the noun to anything that shields a person from outside pressure.","cn":"二十世纪的写作把这个名词扩展到任何为人挡住外界压力的事物。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds derivatives of the same island root; group two holds materials and barriers with a similar job.","cn":"第一组是同出「岛」这一词根的派生词；第二组是作用相近的材料与屏障。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"insulate","ipa":"/ɪnˈsʌleɪt/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"To cut something off from heat, charge or contact; the noun is the material that does it.","definitionCN":"使某物与热、电或接触隔开；名词是执行这件事的材料。"},{"word":"insulation","ipa":"/ˌɪnsjuˈleɪʃn/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"The act or the whole layer of insulating material, rather than one piece.","definitionCN":"绝缘行为或整层绝缘材料，而非单个物件。"},{"word":"insular","ipa":"/ˈɪnsjələ/","tag":"same root, adjective","definition":"Island-like, hence narrow in outlook; it keeps the literal island image.","definitionCN":"像岛一样的，因而引申为眼界狭窄；保留了字面的岛的形象。"},{"word":"isolate","ipa":"/aɪˈsəʊleɪt/","tag":"same root through Italian","definition":"To set apart from others; it shares the island picture but not the technical sense.","definitionCN":"使与别人分开；共享「岛」的图景，但没有技术义。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"dielectric","ipa":"/daɪˈɪlektrɪk/","tag":"technical synonym","definition":"A material that polarizes rather than conducts; common in capacitors and cable design.","definitionCN":"会极化而不导电的材料；常用于电容器与电缆设计。"},{"word":"nonconductor","ipa":"/ˌnɒnkənˈdʌktə/","tag":"plain synonym","definition":"A simple word for a material that does not carry charge.","definitionCN":"不导电材料的平实说法。"},{"word":"shield","ipa":"/ʃiːld/","tag":"barrier","definition":"Something that blocks a hazard; it may reflect or absorb rather than simply refuse passage.","definitionCN":"挡住危险的东西；它可能反射或吸收，而不只是拒绝通过。"},{"word":"barrier","ipa":"/ˈbæriə/","tag":"general block","definition":"Anything that stops movement or influence, often literal and often social.","definitionCN":"阻挡移动或影响的任何东西，常为具体之物，也常用于社会语境。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real island root, the real engineering part and the real contrast with a conductor.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的「岛」词根、真实的工程部件，以及它与导体的真实对照。"},"normal":[{"en":"The root is island: an insulator makes a little island that charge cannot cross.","cn":"词根是「岛」：绝缘体造出一座小岛，电荷过不去。"},{"en":"The family runs insulate, insulation, insulating, insulator and the older insular.","cn":"同族词包括 insulate、insulation、insulating、insulator 以及更早的 insular。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the job: electrical insulator, thermal insulator, sound insulator, ceramic insulator.","cn":"固定搭配标出用途：电绝缘体、绝热材料、隔音材料、陶瓷绝缘子。"},{"en":"The pair is clean: a conductor passes, an insulator refuses.","cn":"这一对很清楚：导体放行，绝缘体拒绝。"},{"en":"On a power pole the insulator is a visible object, not just a property.","cn":"在电线杆上，绝缘子是一件看得见的物件，而不只是一种性质。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a dry rubber coat around a live wire, and a hand on the coat.","cn":"想象带电导线外裹着一层干橡胶，一只手按在橡胶上。"},{"en":"Picture a moat around a castle: the same water that would carry a boat is now a barrier.","cn":"想象城堡周围的护城河：本来能载船的水，此刻成了屏障。"},{"en":"Picture a person surrounded by so much quiet that the city cannot reach them.","cn":"想象一个人被足够的安静围住，城市的声音到不了他。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Dry air is a decent insulator until the voltage is high enough to break it down.","cn":"干燥空气是尚可的绝缘体，直到电压高到把它击穿。"},{"en":"Each insulator on the line was inspected after the storm.","cn":"风暴之后，线路上的每只绝缘子都被检查过。"},{"en":"Long hours alone had become an insulator against bad news.","cn":"长时间的独处成了一道挡住坏消息的屏障。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"insul-（岛）+ -ator（做某事的东西）——把电流围成一座进不来的岛 → 绝缘体","word":"insulator"},"root":"拉丁 insula（岛）→ insulatus（被造成岛屿的）→ 英语 insulate（隔开）→ insulator（执行隔绝的材料或部件）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with a material that blocks charge and narrow to trade substances, then block heat and sound, become a ceramic part and a cable sheath, and end with a barrier against the world.","cn":"八个义项从阻断电荷的材料开始，收窄到行业物质，再阻断热与声，成为瓷件与电缆护套，最后落到挡住外界的屏障。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a dry rubber coat around a live wire, with a hand resting safely on the outside.","cn":"核心意象：带电导线外裹着干橡胶，一只手安全地放在外面。"},"chain":["MADE AN ISLAND","BLOCKS CHARGE","BLOCKS HEAT","BLOCKS SOUND","CERAMIC PART","CABLE COVER"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"The general material and the specific substances an engineer selects.","cn":"一般材料，以及工程师具体选择的物质。"},{"senses":"03","en":"Heat stopped by trapping air and removing its path.","cn":"用滞留空气去掉通路，从而挡住热。"},{"senses":"04","en":"Sound stopped before it reaches the other side of a wall.","cn":"声音在到达墙的另一面之前被挡住。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"Two made objects: the ceramic piece on a pole, and the sheath on a wire.","cn":"两件制成品：杆上的瓷件，以及导线外的护套。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"The barrier turned social: money, routine or distance kept between a person and the world.","cn":"屏障转向社会：金钱、作息或距离被放在一个人与世界之间。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Insulator is the agent noun of insulate, built on the Latin word for island.","cn":"insulator 是 insulate 的施事名词，建立在拉丁语「岛」一词上。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin insula gives insulatus 'made like an island'; English insulate and insulator grew from that, while isolate came through Italian from the same source.","cn":"拉丁 insula 给出 insulatus「被造成岛屿那样」；英语 insulate 与 insulator 由此发展，isolate 则经意大利语同出一源。"},"items":[{"word":"insulate","structure":"insul- + -ate (verb suffix)","meaning":"to cut off from heat, charge or contact","meaningCN":"使绝缘；使隔离（岛词根加动词后缀，地点转为动作）","example":"They insulated the loft last winter.","exampleCN":"他们去年冬天给阁楼做了保温。"},{"word":"insulator","structure":"insulate + -or (one that does)","meaning":"a material or part that blocks passage","meaningCN":"绝缘体（加施事后缀，动作转执行材料）","example":"The insulator failed in the rain.","exampleCN":"绝缘体在雨中失效了。"},{"word":"insulation","structure":"insulate + -ion (process or result)","meaning":"the act or the material that insulates","meaningCN":"绝缘；绝缘材料（加过程后缀，动作转行为与材料）","example":"Insulation cut the heating bill.","exampleCN":"保温层降低了取暖费。"},{"word":"insulating","structure":"insulate + -ing (adjective)","meaning":"serving to block heat or charge","meaningCN":"起绝缘作用的（加形容词后缀，动作为属性）","example":"An insulating mat covers the floor.","exampleCN":"地面上铺着一块绝缘垫。"},{"word":"insular","structure":"insul- + -ar (adjective suffix)","meaning":"island-like; narrow in outlook","meaningCN":"岛屿的；偏狭的（岛词根加形容词后缀，地理义转为性格义）","example":"Insular habits slowed the reform.","exampleCN":"偏狭的习惯拖慢了改革。"},{"word":"insularity","structure":"insular + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the state of being cut off or narrow","meaningCN":"隔绝状态；偏狭（再加性质后缀，性格义转抽象名词）","example":"Insularity kept the village suspicious.","exampleCN":"与外界隔绝使村子多疑。"},{"word":"isolate","structure":"isol- + -ate (verb, via Italian)","meaning":"to set apart from others","meaningCN":"隔离；使孤立（同源「岛」义经意大利语，地理义转为分离动作）","example":"They isolated the faulty cell.","exampleCN":"他们把故障电池单独隔开。"},{"word":"isolation","structure":"isolate + -ion (process)","meaning":"the state of being set apart","meaningCN":"隔离状态（加过程后缀，动作转状态）","example":"The ward was kept in isolation.","exampleCN":"病房被隔离起来。"},{"word":"peninsula","structure":"paene- (almost) + insula (island)","meaning":"land almost surrounded by water","meaningCN":"半岛（「几乎」加岛，岛的图景被减弱）","example":"The town sits on a peninsula.","exampleCN":"这座镇子坐落在一个半岛上。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"insula","structure":"insula, insulae (f., first declension)","meaning":"island; a block of flats","meaningCN":"岛；一栋公寓楼"},{"word":"insulatus","structure":"insulatus, insulata, insulatum (adjective)","meaning":"made like an island; cut off","meaningCN":"被造成岛屿那样的；隔开的"},{"word":"insulare","structure":"insulare (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to make into an island","meaningCN":"使成岛屿"},{"word":"insularis","structure":"insularis, insulare (adjective)","meaning":"of an island","meaningCN":"岛屿的"}]}},{"word":"insulation","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪnsjuˈleɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪnsəˈleɪʃn/","definition_zh":"绝缘；隔热；隔音；绝缘材料；与外界隔绝的状态","definition_en":"the act or material that stops heat, electricity or sound from passing, or a state of being cut off from others","core_image":"屋顶下铺满厚厚的浅色纤维，屋外寒风呼啸，屋内的人只穿一件薄衫","scene":"阁楼里铺满厚厚的浅色纤维，窗外的风把树枝吹得乱响，屋里的人却只穿一件薄衫。Good insulation kept the upper floor warm all night.","sceneCN":"这里 insulation 指「建筑保温层」（第 3 个义项：隔热层、保温材料）；句意为良好的保温层让楼上整夜都暖和。图中可辨识物件：屋顶椽子、纤维保温棉、温度计、薄衫。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"绝缘；隔热；隔音（不可数）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"绝缘材料；保温材料（不可数）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"隔绝状态；免受影响（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"thermal insulation","zh":"隔热；保温"},{"phrase":"electrical insulation","zh":"电绝缘"},{"phrase":"sound insulation","zh":"隔音"},{"phrase":"loft insulation","zh":"阁楼保温层"},{"phrase":"insulation material","zh":"绝缘材料"}],"forms":[{"label":"名词（不可数）","form":"insulation"},{"label":"动词","form":"insulate"},{"label":"名词（绝缘体）","form":"insulator"},{"label":"形容词","form":"insulating"},{"label":"形容词（已隔热的）","form":"insulated"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"insulate","pos":"v.","zh":"使绝缘；使隔热；使隔离"},{"word":"insulator","pos":"n.","zh":"绝缘体；绝缘子"},{"word":"insulating","pos":"adj.","zh":"绝缘的；隔热的"},{"word":"isolate","pos":"v.","zh":"隔离；使孤立"},{"word":"isolation","pos":"n.","zh":"隔离；孤立"},{"word":"peninsula","pos":"n.","zh":"半岛"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The act of blocking flow","titleCN":"绝缘：阻断电、热或声的传递","definition":"the act or state of preventing heat, electricity or sound from passing","definitionCN":"阻止热、电或声音通过的行为或状态","example":"Good insulation keeps the house cool in summer.","exampleCN":"良好的隔热让房子在夏天保持凉爽。","why":"The word is the action noun of insulate: an island is made around something, and nothing crosses the water.","whyCN":"这个词是 insulate 的动作名词：在事物周围造出一座岛，什么都渡不过来。"},{"no":"02","title":"The material that does it","titleCN":"绝缘材料；保温材料（总称）","definition":"the material used to block the passage of heat, charge or sound","definitionCN":"用来阻挡热、电或声通过的材料","example":"The walls are filled with insulation made from recycled paper.","exampleCN":"墙里填充的是用再生纸制成的保温材料。","why":"English often uses one noun for the act and for the stuff that performs it, so insulation means both the blocking and the blocker.","whyCN":"英语常用同一个名词兼指动作与执行该动作的材料，因此 insulation 既指阻断，也指阻断物。"},{"no":"03","title":"The layer in a building","titleCN":"建筑保温层、隔热层","definition":"a layer of material fitted into walls, roofs or floors to slow heat loss","definitionCN":"装入墙体、屋顶或地板以减缓热损失的一层材料","example":"Good insulation kept the upper floor warm all night.","exampleCN":"良好的保温层让楼上整夜都暖和。","why":"In construction the abstract act becomes a visible layer with a measured thickness.","whyCN":"在建筑中，抽象的行为变成一层有厚度、可测量的实物。"},{"no":"04","title":"Blocking sound","titleCN":"隔音","definition":"material or treatment that reduces the transfer of sound","definitionCN":"减少声音传递的材料或处理","example":"Sound insulation between the flats was poor, so every step was heard.","exampleCN":"两户之间的隔音很差，每一步都听得见。","why":"Sound travels as vibration through solid contact, so soft or broken layers stop the chain before it reaches the next room.","whyCN":"声音靠固体接触以振动传播，因此柔软或断续的层会在到达下一间屋子之前打断这条链。"},{"no":"05","title":"The covering on a wire","titleCN":"电线的绝缘包层","definition":"the non-conducting covering around a cable","definitionCN":"电缆外围不导电的包层","example":"The insulation had perished where the cable met the wall.","exampleCN":"电缆与墙相接处的绝缘层已经老化。","why":"A cable needs the same barrier in a thin, flexible form, so the mass noun also names a sleeve.","whyCN":"电缆需要同样屏障的薄而柔软形式，因此这个不可数名词也指一层护套。"},{"no":"06","title":"The measured ability to hold heat","titleCN":"保温性能：保持热的能力","definition":"the effectiveness of a material or structure in limiting heat loss","definitionCN":"材料或结构限制热损失的效果","example":"Double glazing raises the insulation of the whole window.","exampleCN":"双层玻璃提高了整扇窗的保温性能。","why":"Once performance could be rated, the noun also named a measurable quality rather than a substance.","whyCN":"当性能可以被评级，这个名词也指一种可测量的品质，而不只是物质。"},{"no":"07","title":"Being cut off","titleCN":"与外界隔绝的状态","definition":"the state of being separated from other people or from outside events","definitionCN":"与他人或外界事件分开的状态","example":"Years of insulation had left him unprepared for the city.","exampleCN":"多年的与世隔绝让他在城市里措手不及。","why":"The island picture returns in a social form: water around a person instead of rubber around a wire.","whyCN":"「岛」的图景以社会形式回归：围住一个人的是水，而不是导线外的橡胶。"},{"no":"08","title":"Protection from criticism","titleCN":"抽象义：免受批评或影响","definition":"the state of being protected from criticism, pressure or unwanted attention","definitionCN":"受到保护、免于批评、压力或不必要关注的状态","example":"Wealth gave the family an insulation from public blame.","exampleCN":"财富让这家人免受公众指责。","why":"The metaphor treats blame as a current that would otherwise reach them, and money as the layer that stops it.","whyCN":"这个比喻把指责当作一股本会到达他们的电流，而金钱就是挡住它的那一层。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Insulation is the noun of insulate, from Latin insula 'island'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"insulation 是 insulate 的名词形式，来自拉丁 insula「岛」。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN INSULA","en":"Insula meant 'island' and also a block of flats; both images involve something enclosed by a boundary.","cn":"insula 意为「岛」，也指一栋公寓楼；两种形象都是被边界围住的某物。"},{"era":"LATIN INSULATUS","en":"Insulatus, 'made like an island', described something cut off from its surroundings.","cn":"insulatus 意为「被造成岛屿那样」，描述与周围隔开的某物。"},{"era":"ENGLISH INSULATE","en":"The verb insulate entered English in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries with the general sense of setting apart.","cn":"动词 insulate 在十六、十七世纪进入英语，泛指派开、隔开。"},{"era":"INSULATION","en":"The noun insulation followed, at first naming the act of separation; the physical senses of heat and charge blocking came later.","cn":"名词 insulation 随后出现，最初指分隔行为；阻断热与电的物理义后来才发展起来。"},{"era":"BUILDING USE","en":"Nineteenth- and twentieth-century building practice made insulation a trade word for the layers fitted into walls and roofs.","cn":"十九、二十世纪的建筑实践使 insulation 成为装入墙体与屋顶的各层的行业词。"},{"era":"FIGURATIVE","en":"Twentieth-century writing used the noun for social and emotional isolation as well as for physical barriers.","cn":"二十世纪的写作把这个名词用于社会与情感上的隔绝，也用于物理屏障。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds relatives from the island root; group two holds words for protection and separation.","cn":"第一组是同出「岛」词根的亲属词；第二组是表示保护与分离的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"insulate","ipa":"/ɪnˈsʌleɪt/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"The action; insulation is the resulting state, layer or material.","definitionCN":"动作本身；insulation 是由此形成的状态、层或材料。"},{"word":"insulator","ipa":"/ɪnˈsʌleɪtə/","tag":"same root, object","definition":"One piece or component that blocks passage; insulation is the whole layer or mass.","definitionCN":"阻挡通过的单个物件或部件；insulation 是整层或整体材料。"},{"word":"isolate","ipa":"/aɪˈsəʊleɪt/","tag":"same root via Italian","definition":"To set apart from others, usually people or cells, not heat.","definitionCN":"使与其他人或细胞分开，通常不用于热。"},{"word":"insular","ipa":"/ˈɪnsjələ/","tag":"same root, adjective","definition":"Island-like or narrow; it describes outlook, not a building layer.","definitionCN":"像岛的、偏狭的；描述眼界，而非建筑层。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"padding","ipa":"/ˈpædɪŋ/","tag":"soft barrier","definition":"Soft material used to absorb shock or fill space; it cushions rather than insulates.","definitionCN":"用于缓冲或填隙的软材料；重在缓冲而非阻断。"},{"word":"lagging","ipa":"/ˈlæɡɪŋ/","tag":"pipe wrapping","definition":"The trade word for insulation wrapped around pipes and tanks.","definitionCN":"包在管道与储罐外的保温材料的行业说法。"},{"word":"shielding","ipa":"/ˈʃiːldɪŋ/","tag":"blocking radiation","definition":"Protection that deflects or absorbs radiation, often metal rather than fibre.","definitionCN":"偏转或吸收辐射的防护，常用金属而非纤维。"},{"word":"isolation","ipa":"/ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃn/","tag":"social separation","definition":"Being kept apart from others; it names the social state, not the material.","definitionCN":"被人为隔开；指社会状态，而非材料。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the island root, the building trade and the real measurement of heat loss.","cn":"正常联想使用「岛」词根、建筑行业说法，以及真实的热损失测量。"},"normal":[{"en":"The root is island: insulation builds a little island around a room or a wire.","cn":"词根是「岛」：绝缘在房间或导线周围造出一座小岛。"},{"en":"The family runs insulate, insulator, insulating, insulated and the older insular.","cn":"同族词包括 insulate、insulator、insulating、insulated 以及更早的 insular。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the uses: thermal insulation, electrical insulation, sound insulation, loft insulation.","cn":"固定搭配标出用途：隔热、电绝缘、隔音、阁楼保温。"},{"en":"One noun covers both the act and the material, so context decides whether it is a process or a product.","cn":"一个名词兼指动作与材料，因此靠语境判断是过程还是产品。"},{"en":"The measure is real: insulation is rated by how much heat it stops, not by how thick it looks.","cn":"这个量是真实的：保温性能按它挡住多少热来评级，而不是看它看起来多厚。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a quilt of trapped air around a house, and winter walking past without entering.","cn":"想象房子外面盖着一层滞留空气的被子，冬天走过却进不来。"},{"en":"Picture a wire in a rubber sleeve, and a hand on the sleeve.","cn":"想象导线裹在橡胶套里，一只手按在套上。"},{"en":"Picture a person on an island who hears the mainland only as a rumour.","cn":"想象岛上的人，只把大陆的消息当作传闻来听。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Loft insulation paid for itself within two winters.","cn":"阁楼保温层两个冬天就收回了成本。"},{"en":"Damaged insulation on a cable is a fire risk and must be replaced.","cn":"电缆上损坏的绝缘层有火灾风险，必须更换。"},{"en":"The village's insulation from the coast road kept its old customs alive.","cn":"村子与海岸公路的隔绝让它保住了古老习俗。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"insul-（岛）+ -ation（行为、状态）——把某物围成一座与外界隔绝的岛 → 绝缘、隔热","word":"insulation"},"root":"拉丁 insula（岛）→ insulatus（被造成岛屿的）→ 英语 insulate → insulation；由「隔开」发展为阻断热、电、声，再引申为与外界隔绝。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with the act of blocking flow, become the material and the building layer, then sound and cable cover, a measured performance, and end with social and emotional separation.","cn":"八个义项从阻断流动的行为开始，变成材料与建筑层，再到隔音与电缆包层、可测量的性能，最后落到社会与情感上的隔绝。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a thick pale fibre filling the roof space while the winter wind rattles the branches outside.","cn":"核心意象：浅色厚纤维填满屋顶空间，屋外寒风摇动树枝。"},"chain":["ISLAND STATE","BLOCKING FLOW","BUILDING LAYER","QUIET ROOM","CABLE SHEATH","SHIELDED FROM WORDS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"The act of cutting off and the material that performs it.","cn":"隔绝行为，以及执行这一行为的材料。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"The layer in a house and the rated performance it delivers.","cn":"房屋中的那一层，以及它所提供的可评级性能。"},{"senses":"04","en":"Sound stopped so that two rooms stay separate.","cn":"声音被挡住，两间屋子得以分开。"},{"senses":"05","en":"A sheath around a cable, keeping current in and hands out.","cn":"电缆外的护套，把电流关在里面、把手挡在外面。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"A person made into an island, protected from the world or from blame.","cn":"一个人被造成岛屿，免受外界或指责的侵扰。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Insulation is the action noun of insulate, and the whole family rests on the Latin word for island.","cn":"insulation 是 insulate 的动作名词，整个词族都建立在拉丁语「岛」一词上。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin insula gives insulatus and the verb insulare; English insulate, insulation, insulator and insular all come from that base, while isolate arrived through Italian.","cn":"拉丁 insula 给出 insulatus 与动词 insulare；英语 insulate、insulation、insulator 与 insular 都出自这一词基，isolate 则经意大利语而来。"},"items":[{"word":"insulate","structure":"insul- + -ate (verb suffix)","meaning":"to cut something off from heat, charge or contact","meaningCN":"使绝缘；使隔离（岛词根加动词后缀，地点转为动作）","example":"They insulated the water pipes.","exampleCN":"他们给水管做了保温。"},{"word":"insulation","structure":"insulate + -ion (action, result)","meaning":"the act or material of blocking flow","meaningCN":"绝缘；绝缘材料（加过程后缀，动作转行为与结果）","example":"Insulation lowered the bills.","exampleCN":"保温层降低了账单。"},{"word":"insulator","structure":"insulate + -or (one that does)","meaning":"a material or part that blocks passage","meaningCN":"绝缘体（加施事后缀，动作转执行物件）","example":"The insulator cracked.","exampleCN":"绝缘子裂了。"},{"word":"insulating","structure":"insulate + -ing (adjective)","meaning":"serving to block heat or charge","meaningCN":"起绝缘作用的（加形容词后缀，动作为属性）","example":"Insulating tape sealed the joint.","exampleCN":"绝缘胶带封住了接头。"},{"word":"insular","structure":"insul- + -ar (adjective suffix)","meaning":"island-like; limited in outlook","meaningCN":"岛屿的；偏狭的（岛词根加形容词后缀，地理转性格）","example":"Their insular view slowed reform.","exampleCN":"他们偏狭的视野拖慢了改革。"},{"word":"insularity","structure":"insular + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the state of being cut off","meaningCN":"隔绝；偏狭（再加性质后缀，性格转抽象名词）","example":"Insularity protected and limited them.","exampleCN":"隔绝既保护也限制了它们。"},{"word":"isolate","structure":"isol- + -ate (verb, via Italian)","meaning":"to set apart from others","meaningCN":"隔离；使孤立（同源「岛」义经意大利语，地理转分离）","example":"Doctors isolated the patient.","exampleCN":"医生把病人隔离了。"},{"word":"isolation","structure":"isolate + -ion (state)","meaning":"the state of being set apart","meaningCN":"隔离状态（加过程后缀，动作转状态）","example":"Isolation weakened the team.","exampleCN":"隔离削弱了团队。"},{"word":"peninsula","structure":"paene- (almost) + insula (island)","meaning":"land almost surrounded by water","meaningCN":"半岛（「几乎」加岛，岛的图景被减弱）","example":"A road runs down the peninsula.","exampleCN":"一条路沿半岛延伸。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"insula","structure":"insula, insulae (f., first declension)","meaning":"island; a block of flats","meaningCN":"岛；一栋公寓楼"},{"word":"insulatus","structure":"insulatus, insulata, insulatum (adjective)","meaning":"made like an island","meaningCN":"被造成岛屿那样的"},{"word":"insulare","structure":"insulare (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to make into an island","meaningCN":"使成岛屿"},{"word":"insularis","structure":"insularis, insulare (adjective)","meaning":"of an island","meaningCN":"岛屿的"}]}},{"word":"circuit","ipa_uk":"/ˈsɜːkɪt/","ipa_us":"/ˈsɜːrkɪt/","definition_zh":"电路；环路；一圈；巡回路线；巡回赛；神经回路","definition_en":"a closed path that current can travel around, or any route, tour or loop that returns to its starting point","core_image":"一条闭合跑道，车一圈圈回到起点，路始终不断","scene":"桌上摊着一张草图，一条线从电池出发，绕过灯泡又回到电池，恰好闭合成一个圈。The drawing showed a complete circuit with no gap in it.","sceneCN":"这里 circuit 指「闭合的电路」（第 1 个义项：电流可绕行的闭合通路）；句意为图上画出一个没有缺口的完整电路。图中可辨识物件：电池、灯泡、导线、图纸。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"电路；闭合回路"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"一圈；环行；巡回路线；巡回赛"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"神经回路；循环系统（比喻）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"electric circuit","zh":"电路"},{"phrase":"closed circuit","zh":"闭合电路"},{"phrase":"short circuit","zh":"短路"},{"phrase":"circuit court","zh":"巡回法庭"},{"phrase":"lecture circuit","zh":"巡回演讲路线"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"circuit"},{"label":"复数","form":"circuits"},{"label":"形容词（迂回的）","form":"circuitous"},{"label":"名词（电路系统；电路元件）","form":"circuitry"},{"label":"动词（绕行）","form":"circuit"},{"label":"名词（巡行；循环）","form":"circulation"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"circuitous","pos":"adj.","zh":"迂回的；绕远路的"},{"word":"circuitry","pos":"n.","zh":"电路系统；电路元件"},{"word":"circulate","pos":"v.","zh":"循环；流通"},{"word":"circulation","pos":"n.","zh":"循环；发行量"},{"word":"circle","pos":"n.","zh":"圆；圈子"},{"word":"circus","pos":"n.","zh":"马戏团；圆形广场"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A closed path for current","titleCN":"电路：电流可绕行的闭合通路","definition":"a complete path around which electric current can flow","definitionCN":"电流可以绕行的完整通路","example":"The lamp lights only when the circuit is closed.","exampleCN":"只有电路闭合时灯才会亮。","why":"The Latin word means 'a going around'; a current needs exactly that, a path with no break that returns to its source.","whyCN":"拉丁词义就是「绕一圈」；电流需要的正是一条毫无缺口、回到源头的路径。"},{"no":"02","title":"A wired arrangement","titleCN":"电路装置：元件的线路组合","definition":"a particular arrangement of components and wires, such as a series or parallel circuit","definitionCN":"元件与导线的特定组合，如串联或并联电路","example":"The two lamps are in a parallel circuit, so one can fail alone.","exampleCN":"两盏灯接在并联电路里，因此一盏可以单独坏掉。","why":"Beyond the abstract loop, the word names the built arrangement, which determines how current divides.","whyCN":"除了抽象的环路，这个词也指实际接成的组合，正是它决定电流如何分流。"},{"no":"03","title":"One lap or round","titleCN":"一圈；环行路线","definition":"one complete lap or a route that returns to its start","definitionCN":"完整的一圈，或回到起点的路线","example":"The runner completed three circuits of the park.","exampleCN":"跑者绕公园跑了三圈。","why":"The oldest sense is simply going around, which is why the same word fits a lap, a tour and a wire loop.","whyCN":"最古老的一义就是绕行，因此同一个词既指一圈、一次巡游，也指导线形成的环。"},{"no":"04","title":"A court on tour","titleCN":"巡回法庭与巡回审判区","definition":"a court that travels to hear cases in different places, or the district it covers","definitionCN":"到不同地点审案的法庭，或它所管辖的巡回区","example":"The case went before the circuit court last spring.","exampleCN":"这起案件去年春天由巡回法庭审理。","why":"Judges once travelled a fixed round of towns, and the route gave the court its name.","whyCN":"法官曾经按固定的城镇路线巡行，路线的名字就成了法庭的名字。"},{"no":"05","title":"A tour of venues","titleCN":"巡回演出或演讲路线","definition":"a series of performances or talks given in different places","definitionCN":"在不同地点进行的一系列演出或演讲","example":"The band spent a year on the club circuit.","exampleCN":"乐队在俱乐部巡演线上跑了一年。","why":"Performers follow a round of venues as judges once followed a round of towns, so the travelling route keeps the name.","whyCN":"表演者沿着固定的演出场地巡游，正如法官曾沿着城镇巡游，这条旅行的路线沿用了旧名。"},{"no":"06","title":"A racing ring","titleCN":"赛车环道","definition":"a track laid out as a loop for racing","definitionCN":"为赛车铺设的环形跑道","example":"The new circuit has two long straights and a tight hairpin.","exampleCN":"新赛道有两条长直道和一个急弯。","why":"A race track is literally a closed loop, so the word needs no metaphor here at all.","whyCN":"赛道本身就是一个闭合的环，因此这里根本不需要比喻。"},{"no":"07","title":"A professional tour","titleCN":"职业巡回赛","definition":"the series of tournaments or events that professionals play in","definitionCN":"职业选手参加的一系列赛事","example":"She moved from junior events to the main circuit at nineteen.","exampleCN":"她十九岁从青少年赛事进入主巡回赛。","why":"Sport borrows the travelling round: players move from event to event along a fixed season.","whyCN":"体育借用了旅行的环形路线：选手按赛季从一个赛事转到下一个赛事。"},{"no":"08","title":"A loop in the body or in logic","titleCN":"神经回路；抽象循环","definition":"a closed chain of nerves, signals or steps that feed back into themselves","definitionCN":"神经、信号或步骤自我回馈的闭环","example":"The reflex depends on a simple circuit in the spinal cord.","exampleCN":"这一反射依赖脊髓里一个简单的神经回路。","why":"The abstract sense keeps the shape of the loop and drops the wire: signals leave, return and start again.","whyCN":"抽象义保留了环的形状而去掉导线：信号出发、返回，再重新开始。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Circuit comes from Latin circuitus 'a going around', from circumire 'to go around'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"circuit 来自拉丁 circuitus「绕行」，其动词为 circumire「绕圈走」。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN IRE","en":"Latin ire meant 'to go', the verb behind many English words about movement and departure.","cn":"拉丁 ire 意为「走」，是许多表示移动与离开的英语词背后的动词。"},{"era":"LATIN CIRCUMIRE","en":"Circum 'around' plus ire produced circumire, 'to go around', used of troops, travellers and the sun.","cn":"circum「环绕」加 ire 构成 circumire，意为「绕行」，用于军队、旅人与太阳。"},{"era":"LATIN CIRCUITUS","en":"The noun circuitus named a going around or a revolution, and also a defined round or district.","cn":"名词 circuitus 指绕行或一周，也指划定的一圈或辖区。"},{"era":"ENGLISH","en":"English borrowed circuit in the fourteenth century for a circular journey and for a district visited in turn.","cn":"英语在十四世纪借入 circuit，指环形旅程，也指依次巡视的辖区。"},{"era":"LEGAL AND ELECTRIC","en":"Judges on circuit gave the legal sense, and nineteenth-century physics gave the word its closed conducting path.","cn":"巡回审判的法官给出法律义，十九世纪物理学又给这个词一个闭合导电路径。"},{"era":"SPORT AND ABSTRACT","en":"Nineteenth- and twentieth-century sport and physiology extended circuit to tournaments and to nerve loops.","cn":"十九、二十世纪的体育与生理学把 circuit 扩展到巡回赛与神经回路。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds relatives of the same going-around root; group two holds words for loops and routes.","cn":"第一组是同出「绕行」词根的亲属词；第二组是表示环路与路线的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"circle","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkl/","tag":"related round word","definition":"A perfectly round shape; circuit is the act or path of going round rather than the shape.","definitionCN":"完美的圆形；circuit 指绕行的动作或路径，而非形状。"},{"word":"circuitous","ipa":"/səˈkjuːɪtəs/","tag":"same root, adjective","definition":"Going the long way round; it describes a route, not a closed loop.","definitionCN":"绕远路的；描述路线，而非闭合回路。"},{"word":"circus","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkəs/","tag":"look-alike, ring word","definition":"A round arena and later a performance company; it shares the ring image but not the path sense.","definitionCN":"圆形竞技场，后指马戏团；共享环形形象，但没有路径义。"},{"word":"circulate","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkjəleɪt/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"To move around and return, used of blood, air or news.","definitionCN":"循环并返回，用于血液、空气或消息。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"loop","ipa":"/luːp/","tag":"shape word","definition":"A path that curves back on itself; circuit adds the electrical or institutional use.","definitionCN":"自我折返的路径；circuit 多了电学或制度上的用法。"},{"word":"network","ipa":"/ˈnetwɜːk/","tag":"many paths","definition":"A set of connected routes or nodes, usually with branches rather than one ring.","definitionCN":"相互连接的路线或节点，通常有分支，而不是单一环。"},{"word":"route","ipa":"/ruːt/","tag":"plain path","definition":"Any way from one place to another; it need not return.","definitionCN":"从一处到另一处的任何路；不必返回。"},{"word":"tour","ipa":"/tʊə/","tag":"travelling round","definition":"A journey visiting several places, close to the performance sense of circuit.","definitionCN":"走访多地的旅程，接近 circuit 的演出义。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real Latin verb, the real legal sense and the real electrical sense.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的拉丁动词、真实的法律义与真实的电学义。"},"normal":[{"en":"The root is go around: circum plus ire, the same ire that appears in exit and transit.","cn":"词根是「绕行」：circum 加 ire，与 exit、transit 里的 ire 同源。"},{"en":"The family runs circuit, circuitous, circuitry, circulate, circulation and circle.","cn":"同族词包括 circuit、circuitous、circuitry、circulate、circulation 与 circle。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the electrical sense: electric circuit, closed circuit, short circuit.","cn":"固定搭配标出电学义：电路、闭合电路、短路。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the travelling sense: circuit court, lecture circuit, club circuit.","cn":"固定搭配标出巡回义：巡回法庭、巡回演讲路线、俱乐部巡演线。"},{"en":"The shape is always the same: leave, go round, come back.","cn":"形状始终如一：离开、绕一圈、再回来。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a model railway whose track has no gap, so the train can run forever.","cn":"想象一条没有缺口的模型铁轨，火车可以一直跑。"},{"en":"Picture a judge's carriage moving from town to town on a fixed round.","cn":"想象法官的马车按固定路线从一个镇走到另一个镇。"},{"en":"Picture a signal in the spine that triggers a reply and comes back for the next one.","cn":"想象脊髓里的信号触发回应，又回来等待下一次。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A break anywhere in the circuit stops the current everywhere.","cn":"电路中任何一处断开，电流就处处停止。"},{"en":"The speakers spent the summer on the festival circuit.","cn":"这些演讲者整个夏天都在音乐节巡回线上。"},{"en":"The engineer traced the feedback circuit on the diagram.","cn":"工程师在图纸上追踪那条反馈回路。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"circ-（环绕）+ it（走）——绕着走一圈再回到原处 → 电路；环路；巡回","word":"circuit"},"root":"拉丁 circum（环绕）+ ire（走）→ circumire（绕行）→ circuitus（绕行、一周）→ 英语 circuit；电学义与巡回义都保留「绕一圈回来」的核心。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with a closed conducting path and its built arrangement, then a lap and a travelling round, become courts, tours and race tracks, and end with a nerve loop.","cn":"八个义项从闭合导电路径与它的接法开始，接着是一圈与巡回路线，变成法庭、巡演与赛道，最后落到神经回路。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a closed track that returns to its start with no gap anywhere.","cn":"核心意象：一条闭合的跑道，处处无缺口，最终回到起点。"},"chain":["GOING AROUND","CLOSED LOOP","ROUTE AROUND","COURT ON TOUR","RACING RING","NEURAL LOOP"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"The closed path and the particular way its parts are wired.","cn":"闭合路径，以及各部件具体的接线方式。"},{"senses":"03","en":"The plainest sense: one lap, one round of a park or a track.","cn":"最朴素的一义：跑一圈，绕公园或跑道一周。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"A fixed round of towns, followed by judges and later by performers.","cn":"固定的城镇路线，先由法官走，后由表演者走。"},{"senses":"06 · 07","en":"The loop laid out for racing, and the season of events played along it.","cn":"为赛车铺出的环道，以及沿它展开的赛季。"},{"senses":"08","en":"The loop detached from wire and road: signals that leave and return.","cn":"环路脱离导线与道路：信号出去又回来。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Circuit is a Latin noun of motion, and its relatives attach suffixes to the same circum- and ire- parts.","cn":"circuit 是表示运动的拉丁名词，其亲属词都在 circum- 与 ire- 这两个成分上加后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin circumire 'to go around' and its noun circuitus supply the core; circulus and circus are related round-words but from a different formation.","cn":"拉丁 circumire「绕行」及其名词 circuitus 提供核心；circulus 与 circus 是相关的「圆」词，但构词不同。"},"items":[{"word":"circuit","structure":"circum- + it (go)","meaning":"a going around; a closed path","meaningCN":"电路；环路（环绕加走，动作转路径）","example":"The circuit is open.","exampleCN":"电路断开了。"},{"word":"circuitous","structure":"circuit + -ous (full of)","meaning":"roundabout, indirect","meaningCN":"迂回的；绕远路的（加形容词后缀，路径转性质）","example":"A circuitous route avoided the flood.","exampleCN":"一条迂回路线避开了洪水。"},{"word":"circuitry","structure":"circuit + -ry (collective)","meaning":"the whole system of circuits and parts","meaningCN":"电路系统；电路元件（加集合后缀，单条路径转整套系统）","example":"The circuitry fits on one chip.","exampleCN":"整套电路装在一枚芯片上。"},{"word":"circulate","structure":"circul- + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to move round and return","meaningCN":"循环；流通（加动词后缀，路径转动作为循环）","example":"Air circulates through the shaft.","exampleCN":"空气在竖井里循环。"},{"word":"circulation","structure":"circulate + -ion (process)","meaning":"movement round a system","meaningCN":"循环；发行（加过程后缀，动作转持续过程）","example":"Poor circulation chills the feet.","exampleCN":"循环不良使双脚发冷。"},{"word":"circle","structure":"circul- + -le (diminutive)","meaning":"a round shape or group","meaningCN":"圆；圈子（加指小后缀，路径转为形状）","example":"They sat in a circle.","exampleCN":"他们围坐成一圈。"},{"word":"circus","structure":"circ- + -us (round place)","meaning":"a round arena; a travelling show","meaningCN":"圆形广场；马戏团（环形场所转为演出团体）","example":"The circus came to town.","exampleCN":"马戏团进城了。"},{"word":"circumscribe","structure":"circum- (around) + scribe (write)","meaning":"to draw a line around; to limit","meaningCN":"圈定；限制（环绕加书写，围线转为限制）","example":"Rules circumscribe the agency.","exampleCN":"规则限制了该机构的权限。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"ire","structure":"ire, eo, ii, itum (verb, irregular)","meaning":"to go","meaningCN":"走；去"},{"word":"circumire","structure":"circumire (circum- + ire)","meaning":"to go around","meaningCN":"绕行"},{"word":"circuitus","structure":"circuitus, circuitus (m., fourth declension)","meaning":"a going around; a revolution","meaningCN":"绕行；一周"},{"word":"circum","structure":"circum (preposition and prefix)","meaning":"around","meaningCN":"环绕；在周围"}]}},{"word":"circuit board","ipa_uk":"/ˈsɜːkɪt bɔːd/","ipa_us":"/ˈsɜːrkɪt bɔːrd/","definition_zh":"电路板；印刷电路板；主板","definition_en":"a flat board that holds and connects electronic components through printed or wired paths","core_image":"一块绿色薄板上布满细密的铜线，像一座小城市的街道网","scene":"维修台上摆着一块绿色薄板，细密的铜线连着小方块，技师用探针沿线路一点点查下去。He traced the fault along the circuit board with a probe.","sceneCN":"这里 circuit board 指「安装并连接电子元件的板」（第 1 个义项：电路板本体）；句意为技师用探针沿电路板的线路排查故障。图中可辨识物件：绿色电路板、芯片、焊点、探针。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"电路板；印刷电路板"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"主板；系统板"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"printed circuit board","zh":"印刷电路板"},{"phrase":"a faulty circuit board","zh":"故障电路板"},{"phrase":"circuit board design","zh":"电路板设计"},{"phrase":"motherboard","zh":"主板"},{"phrase":"surface mount","zh":"表面贴装"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"circuit board"},{"label":"复数","form":"circuit boards"},{"label":"缩写（印刷电路板）","form":"PCB"},{"label":"相关名词（电路）","form":"circuit"},{"label":"相关名词（主板）","form":"motherboard"},{"label":"相关名词（电路系统）","form":"circuitry"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"circuit","pos":"n.","zh":"电路；环路"},{"word":"circuitry","pos":"n.","zh":"电路系统；电路元件"},{"word":"circuitous","pos":"adj.","zh":"迂回的"},{"word":"board","pos":"n.","zh":"板；委员会；董事会"},{"word":"motherboard","pos":"n.","zh":"主板"},{"word":"breadboard","pos":"n.","zh":"实验用插线板"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A flat board of components","titleCN":"电路板：承载并连接元件的板","definition":"a flat insulating board on which electronic components are mounted and connected","definitionCN":"安装电子元件并把它们连接起来的平整绝缘板","example":"The circuit board holds every chip and connector in the radio.","exampleCN":"这块电路板承载着收音机里所有芯片与接插件。","why":"The compound is literal: a circuit needs a path, and a board gives that path a flat physical home.","whyCN":"这个复合词很字面：电路需要一条路径，而板给这条路径一个平整的实体归宿。"},{"no":"02","title":"The printed version","titleCN":"印刷电路板：铜箔印成的板","definition":"a board whose connecting paths are printed in copper rather than wired by hand","definitionCN":"连接线路以铜箔印制而非手工接线的板","example":"The factory replaced hand wiring with a printed circuit board.","exampleCN":"工厂用印刷电路板取代了手工接线。","why":"Printing turned the wiring into part of the board itself, which is why the printed version became the standard object.","whyCN":"印刷把接线变成板本身的一部分，因此印刷版本成了标准的物件。"},{"no":"03","title":"The main board of a computer","titleCN":"主板：计算机里的中心电路板","definition":"the central board that connects the processor, memory and other units","definitionCN":"连接处理器、内存与其他单元的中心电路板","example":"He replaced the circuit board but kept the old drives.","exampleCN":"他换了主板，却留下了旧硬盘。","why":"In a computer one board sits at the centre of all the others, and the plain word board takes the role name.","whyCN":"计算机里有一块板位于其他板之间，普普通通的 board 就承担了这个角色名。"},{"no":"04","title":"The traces and joints on it","titleCN":"板上的走线与焊点","definition":"the thin copper paths and solder joints that carry signals across the board","definitionCN":"在板上传输信号的细铜线与焊点","example":"A hairline crack in the traces stopped the circuit board from working.","exampleCN":"走线上一道发丝般的裂缝让这块板失灵。","why":"Up close, the board is a landscape of roads and junctions, and the word also names those features.","whyCN":"近距离看，板是一片由道路和交叉点构成的风景，这个词也指这些特征。"},{"no":"05","title":"Board production","titleCN":"电路板的生产与组装","definition":"the industrial process of making and assembling boards","definitionCN":"制造与装配电路板的工业过程","example":"The circuit board line runs three shifts a day.","exampleCN":"这条电路板生产线每天三班倒。","why":"Once boards are mass-produced, the compound also names the industry and the line that makes them.","whyCN":"一旦电路板被批量生产，这个复合词也指制造它的行业与产线。"},{"no":"06","title":"Board repair","titleCN":"电路板故障与维修","definition":"the work of finding and fixing faults on a board","definitionCN":"在板上查找并修复故障的工作","example":"The shop charged a fee to inspect the circuit board.","exampleCN":"这家店收了一笔检测电路板的费用。","why":"Repair is the reverse of assembly: the board is opened, probed and made whole again.","whyCN":"维修是装配的反面：把板打开、探测，再让它恢复完整。"},{"no":"07","title":"Board layout","titleCN":"电路板设计布局","definition":"the planned arrangement of components and traces on a board","definitionCN":"板上元件与走线的规划布置","example":"A good circuit board layout keeps the power paths short.","exampleCN":"好的电路板布局会让电源路径尽量短。","why":"Before a board exists it is a drawing, and the compound also names that design stage.","whyCN":"在板存在之前，它是一张图，因此这个复合词也指那个设计阶段。"},{"no":"08","title":"A skeleton for many parts","titleCN":"比喻：把许多部分组织成系统的骨架","definition":"a metaphor for any framework that organizes many separate parts into one system","definitionCN":"任何把许多分立部分组织成一个系统的框架的比喻","example":"The committee acted as a circuit board for the whole reform.","exampleCN":"委员会成了整场改革的电路板。","why":"The metaphor keeps the function: parts do not work alone; a flat framework connects them and lets something flow between them.","whyCN":"这个比喻保留了功能：部件不会单独工作，一块平整的框架把它们连起来，让某种东西在期间流动。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Circuit board joins Latin-derived circuit with the Old English word board. Dates are approximate.","cn":"circuit board 把源自拉丁语的 circuit 与古英语的 board 组合在一起。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN CIRCUITUS","en":"Circuitus meant 'a going around', and nineteenth-century physics gave it the sense of a closed conducting path.","cn":"circuitus 意为「绕行」，十九世纪物理学又赋予它闭合导电路径之义。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH BORD","en":"Board came from Old English bord, a plank or table, and widened to flat panels and to committees.","cn":"board 来自古英语 bord，指木板或桌面，后来扩大到平板与委员会。"},{"era":"PRINTED CIRCUIT","en":"The printed circuit was developed in the 1930s and 1940s, with Paul Eisler's copper-on-insulator method often credited in 1943.","cn":"印刷电路在二十世纪三四十年代发展起来，艾斯勒在绝缘板上覆铜的方法常被记作 1943 年。"},{"era":"COMPOUND TERM","en":"Mid-twentieth-century electronics made circuit board the everyday name for the assembled flat unit.","cn":"二十世纪中期的电子工业让 circuit board 成为这种平整组件的日常名称。"},{"era":"MOTHERBOARD","en":"The personal computer of the 1980s fixed motherboard as the name of the central board.","cn":"二十世纪八十年代的个人电脑确定了 motherboard 作为中心电路板的名称。"},{"era":"FIGURATIVE","en":"Recent writing uses the compound for any framework that connects many parts, from committees to urban systems.","cn":"近年的写作把这个复合词用于任何连接许多部分的框架，从委员会到城市系统。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the two words inside the compound and its near relatives; group two holds other boards and assemblies.","cn":"第一组是复合词内部的两个词及其近亲；第二组是其他板类与组件。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"circuit","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkɪt/","tag":"head word","definition":"The path itself; the board is the physical thing that carries it.","definitionCN":"路径本身；板是承载它的实体。"},{"word":"circuitry","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkɪtri/","tag":"same family","definition":"The whole collection of circuits and parts in a device.","definitionCN":"一台设备里全部电路与元件的总称。"},{"word":"board","ipa":"/bɔːd/","tag":"second element","definition":"A flat panel, or a committee; alone it says nothing about electronics.","definitionCN":"平板，或委员会；单独使用不涉及电子。"},{"word":"breadboard","ipa":"/ˈbredbɔːd/","tag":"look-alike, different use","definition":"A reusable board for prototyping, not a finished printed unit.","definitionCN":"用于原型的可重复插接板，不是成品印刷板。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"motherboard","ipa":"/ˈmʌðəbɔːd/","tag":"central board","definition":"The main board of a computer, a kind of circuit board with a specific role.","definitionCN":"计算机的主板，是承担特定角色的一种电路板。"},{"word":"printed circuit","ipa":"/ˈprɪntɪd ˈsɜːkɪt/","tag":"the path layer","definition":"The copper pattern itself; the board is the panel it sits on.","definitionCN":"铜箔图案本身；板是它所在的平板。"},{"word":"chip","ipa":"/tʃɪp/","tag":"component","definition":"A single integrated circuit; the board connects many of them.","definitionCN":"单个集成电路；板把许多芯片连接起来。"},{"word":"panel","ipa":"/ˈpænl/","tag":"flat part","definition":"Any flat section of a surface, often without electronics.","definitionCN":"任何平整的面板，常与电子无关。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the two literal halves, the printed process and the real computer part.","cn":"正常联想使用两个字面成分、印刷工艺，以及真实的计算机部件。"},"normal":[{"en":"The compound is literal: a circuit on a board, paths on a flat panel.","cn":"这个复合词很字面：板上的电路，平板上的路径。"},{"en":"The family runs circuit, circuitry, circuitous, board, motherboard and breadboard.","cn":"同族词包括 circuit、circuitry、circuitous、board、motherboard 与 breadboard。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the technical sense: printed circuit board, circuit board design, faulty circuit board.","cn":"固定搭配标出技术义：印刷电路板、电路板设计、故障电路板。"},{"en":"Printing is the key step: copper paths are printed instead of hand-wired.","cn":"印刷是关键一步：铜线被印上去，而不是手工接线。"},{"en":"The board connects parts; the parts do not work alone.","cn":"板把各部分连起来；零件单独并不工作。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a small city seen from above: copper streets and chip buildings.","cn":"想象俯瞰一座小城：铜线是街道，芯片是楼房。"},{"en":"Picture a probe walking one street at a time until it finds the break.","cn":"想象探针沿一条条街道走，直到找到断口。"},{"en":"Picture a committee table where every department finally reaches every other.","cn":"想象一张委员会桌，各部门终于都能互相联系。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A single spilled drop can ruin an unsealed circuit board.","cn":"一滴洒出的液体就能毁掉未封装的电路板。"},{"en":"The design team moved the connector to shorten the circuit board layout.","cn":"设计团队移动接插件，以缩短电路板布局。"},{"en":"The old radio still works, though its circuit board is larger than a hand.","cn":"这台旧收音机还能用，尽管它的电路板比一只手还大。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"circuit（电路）+ board（板）——承载电路的板 → 电路板","word":"circuit board"},"root":"circuit 来自拉丁 circuitus（绕行）→ 闭合路径；board 来自古英语 bord（木板）；两者合为「承载电路的平板」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with the flat panel and its printed form, narrow to a computer's main board and its traces, widen to production, repair and design, and end with a framework metaphor.","cn":"八个义项从平整板材与印刷形式开始，收窄到计算机主板与板上走线，再扩到生产、维修与设计，最后落到框架的比喻。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a green panel whose thin copper streets connect rows of small blocks.","cn":"核心意象：一块绿色薄板，细铜线街道连接着一排排小方块。"},"chain":["FLAT BOARD","PRINTED COPPER","SOCKETS AND CHIPS","TRACES","FACTORY LINE","REPAIR BENCH"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"The panel and the printing that turned wiring into part of it.","cn":"板材，以及把接线变成板本身一部分的印刷工艺。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"The central board of a computer, and the traces and joints seen up close.","cn":"计算机的中心板，以及近看时的走线与焊点。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"The line that builds boards and the bench where they are brought back to life.","cn":"制造电路板的生产线，以及让它恢复工作的维修台。"},{"senses":"07","en":"The drawing stage, before any copper exists.","cn":"还没有铜箔之前的图纸阶段。"},{"senses":"08","en":"A framework that connects many parts so that something can flow between them.","cn":"一个连接许多部分、让某种东西在其间流动的框架。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The compound is readable word by word: circuit from Latin, board from Old English.","cn":"这个复合词可以逐字读：circuit 来自拉丁语，board 来自古英语。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin circuitus and circumire supply the first element; board goes back to Old English bord, so a Latin-English compound is the whole story.","cn":"拉丁 circuitus 与 circumire 提供第一个成分；board 上溯古英语 bord，因此这是一个拉丁—英语复合词。"},"items":[{"word":"circuit","structure":"circum- + it (go)","meaning":"a closed path","meaningCN":"电路；环路（环绕加走，动作转路径）","example":"The circuit failed.","exampleCN":"电路失效了。"},{"word":"circuit board","structure":"circuit + board (compound)","meaning":"a flat panel carrying a circuit","meaningCN":"电路板（电路加板，路径得到实体承载）","example":"The circuit board was replaced.","exampleCN":"电路板被更换。"},{"word":"circuitry","structure":"circuit + -ry (collective)","meaning":"all the circuits of a device","meaningCN":"电路系统（加集合后缀，单条路径转整套电路）","example":"The circuitry is dense.","exampleCN":"电路系统很密集。"},{"word":"circuitous","structure":"circuit + -ous (full of)","meaning":"indirect, roundabout","meaningCN":"迂回的（加形容词后缀，路径转性质）","example":"A circuitous path led uphill.","exampleCN":"一条迂回的小路通向山上。"},{"word":"board","structure":"bord (Old English plank)","meaning":"a flat panel or a committee","meaningCN":"板；委员会（古英语木板，转为平板与机构）","example":"The board met at noon.","exampleCN":"委员会中午开会。"},{"word":"motherboard","structure":"mother + board (compound)","meaning":"the central board of a computer","meaningCN":"主板（母加板，板的作用被定为中心）","example":"The motherboard supports two drives.","exampleCN":"主板支持两块硬盘。"},{"word":"breadboard","structure":"bread + board (compound)","meaning":"a reusable board for testing circuits","meaningCN":"实验插线板（面包加板，板转为原型工具）","example":"He built the first version on a breadboard.","exampleCN":"他在插线板上搭出第一版。"},{"word":"keyboard","structure":"key + board (compound)","meaning":"a panel of keys","meaningCN":"键盘（键加板，板转为输入面板）","example":"The keyboard is backlit.","exampleCN":"键盘有背光。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"circuitus","structure":"circuitus, circuitus (m., fourth declension)","meaning":"a going around","meaningCN":"绕行；一周"},{"word":"circumire","structure":"circumire (circum- + ire)","meaning":"to go around","meaningCN":"绕行"},{"word":"circum","structure":"circum (preposition and prefix)","meaning":"around","meaningCN":"环绕"}]}},{"word":"electron","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈlektrɒn/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈlektrɑːn/","definition_zh":"电子；自由电子；价电子","definition_en":"a stable particle with a negative electric charge that is part of every atom and carries current in metals","core_image":"一颗极小极轻的珠子绕着一个沉重的中心飞快旋转，几乎不占什么位置","scene":"云室里，一道细细的轨迹在黑暗中弯成弧线，像有什么极小的东西刚刚穿过。A single electron left the faint track across the chamber.","sceneCN":"这里 electron 指「带负电的基本粒子」（第 1 个义项：电子这一粒子）；句意为一个电子在云室里留下淡淡的轨迹。图中可辨识物件：云室、弧形轨迹、磁场线圈、光源。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"电子（带负电的基本粒子）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（复合词中）电子器件、电子学相关"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"electron beam","zh":"电子束"},{"phrase":"free electron","zh":"自由电子"},{"phrase":"valence electron","zh":"价电子"},{"phrase":"electron microscope","zh":"电子显微镜"},{"phrase":"electron pair","zh":"电子对"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"electron"},{"label":"复数","form":"electrons"},{"label":"形容词","form":"electronic"},{"label":"名词（电子学）","form":"electronics"},{"label":"形容词（电子的；带负电的）","form":"electronegative"},{"label":"形容词（光电的）","form":"photoelectronic"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"electronic","pos":"adj.","zh":"电子的；电子学的"},{"word":"electronics","pos":"n.","zh":"电子学；电子器件"},{"word":"electronegative","pos":"adj.","zh":"带负电的；电负性的"},{"word":"photoelectron","pos":"n.","zh":"光电子"},{"word":"electronvolt","pos":"n.","zh":"电子伏"},{"word":"electrolysis","pos":"n.","zh":"电解"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The negative particle","titleCN":"电子：带负电的基本粒子","definition":"a stable elementary particle carrying a negative charge","definitionCN":"带负电的稳定基本粒子","example":"An electron is roughly two thousand times lighter than a proton.","exampleCN":"一个电子大约比质子轻两千倍。","why":"The name was coined for a unit of charge before the particle was seen, then transferred to the particle itself.","whyCN":"这个名字先是为电荷单位造的，后来才转到粒子本身。"},{"no":"02","title":"An electron in an atom","titleCN":"原子核外的电子","definition":"one of the electrons bound to a nucleus in an atom","definitionCN":"原子中束缚在原子核周围的电子之一","example":"Each shell of the atom holds a fixed number of electrons.","exampleCN":"原子的每一层容纳固定数目的电子。","why":"Bound electrons occupy set shells, so the word also names the orbiting members of an atom.","whyCN":"束缚电子占据固定的壳层，因此这个词也指原子中绕行的成员。"},{"no":"03","title":"A free electron","titleCN":"自由电子：金属中可移动的电子","definition":"an electron that is not bound to an atom and can move through a material","definitionCN":"未被原子束缚、能在材料中移动的电子","example":"A metal conducts because its free electrons can drift under a field.","exampleCN":"金属能导电，是因为自由电子可以在电场下漂移。","why":"The same particle becomes a current carrier once it is free of its atom, and the adjective free marks the change.","whyCN":"同一颗粒子一旦脱离原子，就成为载流子，free 这个形容词标记了这一变化。"},{"no":"04","title":"A beam of them","titleCN":"电子束","definition":"a stream of electrons travelling in the same direction in a vacuum","definitionCN":"在真空中同向飞行的一束电子","example":"The electron beam scans the screen line by line.","exampleCN":"电子束一行一行地扫描屏幕。","why":"Accelerated electrons can be shaped into a beam, and that beam becomes a tool for imaging and display.","whyCN":"被加速的电子可以聚成束，而这束电子又成为成像与显示的工具。"},{"no":"05","title":"A shared pair in a bond","titleCN":"成对电子；共价键中的电子","definition":"one of the pair of electrons shared between atoms in a covalent bond","definitionCN":"共价键中两个原子共享的那对电子之一","example":"The two atoms share an electron pair in the bond.","exampleCN":"两个原子在键中共用一对电子。","why":"Chemistry cares about where electrons sit, so the word also names the shared pair that holds atoms together.","whyCN":"化学关心电子待在哪里，因此这个词也指把原子连在一起的那对共用电子。"},{"no":"06","title":"The outermost ones","titleCN":"价电子：参与成键的最外层电子","definition":"an electron in the outermost shell that can take part in bonding","definitionCN":"最外层、能够参与成键的电子","example":"Carbon has four valence electrons, so it forms four bonds.","exampleCN":"碳有四个价电子，因此能形成四个键。","why":"The outermost electrons decide how an atom combines, and the term valence marks that role.","whyCN":"最外层的电子决定原子如何结合，valence 这个术语标记的正是这一角色。"},{"no":"07","title":"The carrier inside a device","titleCN":"器件中的载流电子","definition":"an electron moving through a semiconductor or a vacuum tube as part of a current","definitionCN":"在半导体或真空中作为电流一部分移动的电子","example":"The transistor controls how many electrons pass through the channel.","exampleCN":"晶体管控制有多少电子通过沟道。","why":"Electronics is built on controlling electron flow, so the particle is also named as the working carrier of a device.","whyCN":"电子学建立在控制电子流之上，因此这颗粒子也作为器件中的工作载流子被命名。"},{"no":"08","title":"A particle with wave behaviour","titleCN":"电子的波动性与量子态","definition":"an electron described as a wave with spin, not only as a small ball","definitionCN":"不只当作小球，而是描述为带自旋的波","example":"The experiment showed the electron behaving as a wave.","exampleCN":"实验显示电子表现得像波。","why":"Quantum theory changed the picture: the same particle has a wavelength and a spin, so the word also carries that description.","whyCN":"量子理论改变了图景：同一颗粒子既有波长又有自旋，因此这个词也承载这种描述。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Electron was coined in 1891 from the Greek word for amber, first as a unit of charge and later as the particle. Dates are approximate.","cn":"electron 于 1891 年用希腊语「琥珀」一词造出，先指电荷单位，后指粒子本身。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK ELEKTRON","en":"Greek ēlektron meant amber, and early electric research began with the attraction of rubbed amber. The deeper origin of the Greek word is source uncertain.","cn":"希腊 ēlektron 意为琥珀，早期电学研究正是从摩擦琥珀的吸引现象开始。这个希腊词更深层的来源属于来源不确定。"},{"era":"STONEY 1891","en":"George Johnstone Stoney proposed electron as the name of a fixed unit of electric charge, before any particle had been isolated.","cn":"乔治·约翰斯通·斯托尼在 1891 年提出用 electron 命名一个固定的电荷单位，此时还没有任何粒子被分离出来。"},{"era":"THOMSON 1897","en":"J. J. Thomson's work on cathode rays identified a negatively charged particle far lighter than an atom, and the unit name moved to the particle.","cn":"汤姆逊 1897 年对阴极射线的研究识别出一种比原子轻得多的带负电粒子，单位名随之转指这个粒子。"},{"era":"ATOMIC MODEL","en":"Twentieth-century atomic theory placed electrons in shells around the nucleus, giving the bound and free senses.","cn":"二十世纪的原子理论把电子放在核外各层，由此产生束缚电子与自由电子的用法。"},{"era":"QUANTUM DESCRIPTION","en":"From the 1920s the electron was described by a wave function with spin, not only as a small charged ball.","cn":"自二十世纪二十年代起，电子用带自旋的波函数描述，而不只是一颗带电小球。"},{"era":"TECHNOLOGY","en":"Electron beam, electron microscope and semiconductor electronics turned the particle into a named working element of devices.","cn":"电子束、电子显微镜与半导体电子学把这颗粒子变成装置中有名字的工作要素。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words on the same amber stem; group two holds the particles and quantities next to the electron.","cn":"第一组是同出琥珀词干的词；第二组是与电子相邻的粒子与量。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"electric","ipa":"/ɪˈlektrɪk/","tag":"same stem, adjective","definition":"Of electricity; it describes power, not a particle.","definitionCN":"电的；描述电力，而非粒子。"},{"word":"electricity","ipa":"/ˌɪlekˈtrɪsəti/","tag":"same stem, noun","definition":"The phenomenon or supply; electrons are its carriers.","definitionCN":"现象或供应；电子是它的载体。"},{"word":"electronic","ipa":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɒnɪk/","tag":"same stem, adjective","definition":"Of devices that control electron flow and process signals.","definitionCN":"指控制电子流动、处理信号的装置。"},{"word":"electronics","ipa":"/ɪˌlekˈtrɒnɪks/","tag":"same stem, field","definition":"The technology and study of such devices, not the particle.","definitionCN":"这类装置的技术与学科，而非粒子本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"proton","ipa":"/ˈprəʊtɒn/","tag":"positive particle","definition":"A positively charged particle in the nucleus, much heavier than an electron.","definitionCN":"原子核中带正电的粒子，比电子重得多。"},{"word":"neutron","ipa":"/ˈnjuːtrɒn/","tag":"neutral particle","definition":"An uncharged particle in the nucleus; it carries no electric charge at all.","definitionCN":"核内不带电的粒子，完全没有电荷。"},{"word":"ion","ipa":"/ˈaɪən/","tag":"charged atom","definition":"An atom or molecule that has gained or lost electrons, so it carries a net charge.","definitionCN":"获得或失去电子而带净电荷的原子或分子。"},{"word":"charge","ipa":"/tʃɑːdʒ/","tag":"quantity","definition":"The property the electron carries, measured in coulombs.","definitionCN":"电子所携带的性质，以库仑计量。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations use the real amber source, the real 1891 coinage and the real device terms.","cn":"正常联想使用真实的琥珀来源、真实的 1891 年造词，以及真实的器件术语。"},"normal":[{"en":"The name came from amber, the first substance that showed electric attraction.","cn":"这个名字来自琥珀，最早显现电吸引的物质。"},{"en":"The word was a unit before it was a particle: Stoney named the charge, Thomson found the thing.","cn":"这个词先是一个单位，后是一个粒子：斯托尼命名电荷，汤姆逊找到实体。"},{"en":"The family runs electronic, electronics, electronegative, photoelectron and electronvolt.","cn":"同族词包括 electronic、electronics、electronegative、photoelectron 与 electronvolt。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the roles: free electron, valence electron, electron beam, electron pair.","cn":"固定搭配标出角色：自由电子、价电子、电子束、电子对。"},{"en":"The charge is negative, and the conventional current arrow points the other way.","cn":"电荷为负，而约定的电流箭头指向相反方向。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a tiny bead orbiting a heavy centre at a distance that dwarfs it.","cn":"想象一颗小珠绕着一个沉重的中心转，距离远大于它本身。"},{"en":"Picture a beam so fine that it writes lines too small for any pen.","cn":"想象一束细到能写出任何笔都写不出的细线的光。"},{"en":"Picture a particle that is also a wave, spread across the whole experiment.","cn":"想象一颗同时也是波的粒子，铺展在整个实验里。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Each electron carries one negative unit of charge.","cn":"每个电子携带一个负电荷单位。"},{"en":"The electron beam is focused by magnetic coils, not glass lenses.","cn":"电子束由磁线圈聚焦，而不是玻璃透镜。"},{"en":"Adding one electron to an atom turns it into a negative ion.","cn":"给原子加一个电子就使它成为负离子。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"electr-（琥珀、电）+ -on（粒子后缀）——电所依赖的那颗带负电的小粒子 → 电子","word":"electron"},"root":"希腊 ēlektron（琥珀）→ 新拉丁 electricus → 1891 年斯托尼以 electron 命名电荷单位 → 1897 年汤姆逊发现粒子后转指电子。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses begin with the particle itself, then its place in an atom, its free and beam forms, its bonding roles, its work in devices, and its quantum description.","cn":"八个义项从粒子本身开始，接着是它在原子中的位置、自由态与束态、成键角色、器件中的工作，以及量子描述。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a tiny bead orbiting a heavy centre, almost weightless and never still.","cn":"核心意象：一颗小珠绕着沉重的中心转，几乎没重量，也从不停下。"},"chain":["AMBER","NEGATIVE CHARGE","ORBITING","FREE IN METAL","BEAM IN VACUUM","WAVE AND SPIN"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"The particle named for the charge it carries.","cn":"以它所携带的电荷命名的粒子。"},{"senses":"02 · 03","en":"Bound in shells, or freed to drift through metal.","cn":"束缚在壳层里，或自由地在金属中漂移。"},{"senses":"04","en":"A stream shaped in vacuum and used as a tool.","cn":"在真空中被塑成束、当作工具使用的电子流。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"The shared pair in a bond, and the outermost ones that decide it.","cn":"键中共用的一对电子，以及决定成键的最外层电子。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"The working carrier inside a device, and the wave with spin behind it.","cn":"器件中工作的载流子，以及其背后的带自旋的波。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Electron is built on the electric stem with the particle ending -on, and the family grows in two directions, devices and charge.","cn":"electron 是在电的词干上加粒子后缀 -on 构成，词族朝器件与电荷两个方向发展。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Greek ēlektron 'amber' gave Latin electrum and New Latin electricus; electron is an English scientific coinage of 1891 with the -on particle ending.","cn":"希腊 ēlektron「琥珀」给出拉丁 electrum 与新拉丁 electricus；electron 是 1891 年的英语科学造词，带 -on 粒子后缀。"},"items":[{"word":"electron","structure":"electr- + -on (particle suffix)","meaning":"the negative particle","meaningCN":"电子（电词干加粒子后缀，现象转为实体）","example":"An electron carries negative charge.","exampleCN":"电子带负电。"},{"word":"electronic","structure":"electron + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"working by controlled electron flow","meaningCN":"电子的（加形容词后缀，粒子转为装置性质）","example":"An electronic lock replaced the key.","exampleCN":"电子锁取代了钥匙。"},{"word":"electronics","structure":"electron + -ics (field of study)","meaning":"the technology of electronic devices","meaningCN":"电子学；电子器件（加学科后缀，粒子转技术领域）","example":"Electronics shrank the radio.","exampleCN":"电子器件让收音机变小。"},{"word":"electronegative","structure":"electro- + negative","meaning":"tending to attract electrons","meaningCN":"电负性的；带负电的（电加负，电荷倾向变成化学性质）","example":"Oxygen is strongly electronegative.","exampleCN":"氧的电负性很强。"},{"word":"electropositive","structure":"electro- + positive","meaning":"tending to give up electrons","meaningCN":"电正性的（电加正，电荷倾向转相反性质）","example":"Sodium is electropositive.","exampleCN":"钠是电正性的。"},{"word":"photoelectron","structure":"photo- (light) + electron","meaning":"an electron released by light","meaningCN":"光电子（光加电子，释放原因变成光照）","example":"The surface emitted photoelectrons.","exampleCN":"表面发射出光电子。"},{"word":"electronvolt","structure":"electron + volt (compound)","meaning":"the energy gained by an electron across one volt","meaningCN":"电子伏（电子加伏特，粒子与单位合成能量单位）","example":"The gap is about two electronvolts.","exampleCN":"能隙约为两电子伏。"},{"word":"electrolysis","structure":"electro- + -lysis (loosening)","meaning":"chemical change driven by current","meaningCN":"电解（电加分解，电流引发化学变化）","example":"Electrolysis splits the water.","exampleCN":"电解把水分解。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"ēlektron","structure":"ēlektron (Greek noun)","meaning":"amber","meaningCN":"琥珀"},{"word":"electrum","structure":"electrum (n., from Greek)","meaning":"amber; pale gold alloy","meaningCN":"琥珀；淡金色合金"},{"word":"electricus","structure":"electricus, electrica, electricum (New Latin adjective)","meaning":"electric, like amber","meaningCN":"电的；像琥珀的"}]}}]);
